t11\",\"WD Black SN850X 8 TB NVMe SSD\"]** — Massive storage for model weights, corpora, and scratch—still blazing fast.\n\n- **product_entity[\"turn0product10\",\"LG 32″ 4K Monitor\"]** — Clear, spacious display for running code side-by-side with logs, dashboards, and docs.\n\n---\n\n###  Summary Table (Estimated EU Prices):\n\n| Component                           | Est. Price (€) |\n|------------------------------------|----------------|\n| Intel Core i9-14900K               | ~486           |\n| Gigabyte Z790 EAGLE AX             | ~220           |\n| Corsair Nautilus 360 RS Cooler     | ~127           |\n| ASUS ROG Strix 1200 W Platinum PSU | ~313           |\n| Crucial T500 2 TB NVMe SSD         | ~153           |\n| WD Black SN850X 8 TB NVMe SSD      | ~695           |\n| LG 32″ 4K Monitor                  | ~510           |\n| **Subtotal (all)**                 | **~ €2,504**   |\n\nCombined with your GPU, RAM, and case from before (approx. €3,550), plus these components (~€2,500), your **full build lands around €6,050**—with top-tier performance and EU availability.\n\n---\n\n###  Notes on GPU Pricing & Caution\n\nBased on recent retail listings:\n\n- The **RTX 5090** is hovering between **€2,400 – €2,800** in Europe for standard models (e.g., Zotac, Gigabyte) and reaches **€3,000+** for premium or water-cooled editions. Some outlets are even easing prices closer to MSRP occasionally.  \n  citeturn0search17turn0search16turn0news24\n\n- **Caution**: There have been alarming reports of GPU scams (e.g., fake or tampered 5090s arriving from Amazon or resellers), so buying from reputable EU/UK vendors with solid return policies is crucial.  \n  citeturn0news19turn0news23\n\n---\n\n###  What To Do Next:\n\n1. Decide on the **GPU model and vendor** you prefer (balance price vs availability).\n2. Confirm if you prefer installing via the **DSM reverse proxy** or Caddy once your Synology is set up.\n3. I can help you draft or check the order list for Iri