"pytorch-cu121\" }\ntorchaudio  = { version = \"2.8.0\",  source = \"pytorch-cu121\" }\n```\n(Adjust versions to match your torch 2.8.0 compatibility.)\n\n---\n\n## Why this fixes it\n- TOML tables require `key = value`. `torch==…` is invalid syntax in `[tool.poetry.dependencies]`. fileciteturn387file0\n- Keeping `pytorch-cu121` as an **explicit source** ensures Poetry resolves CUDA wheels from the PyTorch index rather than CPU wheels from PyPI. fileciteturn387file0\n\nIf anything else errors after this, paste the new message and I’ll zero in on the next line."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
