\n```\n\nIf you **really** want Poetry aware of Triton (optional), add this to `[tool.poetry.dependencies]`:\n\n```toml\ntriton = \">=3.0,<4.0\"\n```\n\n…but it’s not required; letting Torch’s wheels pull the exact compatible `triton` is the smoothest path.\n\nIf you hit any further resolver errors after removing `pytorch-triton`, paste the next message and I’ll zero in on it."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "poetry lock --no-update\nResolving dependencies... (0.8s)\n\nBecause oss20b-test depends on pytorch-triton (3.2.0+git4b3bb1f8) which doesn't match any versions, version solving failed.\n(srcEnv) todd@lava:~/dev/oss20b_test$ # 0) Safety snapshot\ncp pyproject.toml pyproject.toml.bak\ncp poetry.lock poetry.lock.bak\n\n# 1) REMOVE the offending dependency from pyproject.toml\n# (delete the whole line that mentions pytorch-triton)\nsed -i '/^[[:space:]]*pytorch-triton[[:space:]]*=.*/d' pyproject.toml\n\n# 2) Re-parse the lockfile WITHOUT updating versions\npoetry lock --no-update\n\n# 3) Install exactly what's in the lock (no resolver changes)\npoetry install --sync --no-root\nResolving dependencies... (0.4s)\n\nBecause oss20b-test depends on torch (2.8.0) which doesn't match any versions, version solving failed.\nInstalling dependencies from lock file\n\npyproject.toml changed significantly since poetry.lock was last generated. Run `poetry lock [--no-update]` to fix the lock file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it—your resolver is still choking on two things:\n\n1) `pytorch-triton 3.2.0+git…` (nonexistent on any index Poetry knows)  \n2) `torch 2.8.0` from the **CUDA** index (Poetry is searching PyPI by default and “doesn’t match any versions”)\n\nSafest path (no surprise downgrades): **let Poetry manage everything except the PyTorch trio**, and install those with `pip` from the CUDA wheel index after the Poetry install.\n\nBelow is a **cut‑paste sequence** that fixes the project without changing your working versions elsewhere.\n\n---\n\n## A. Clean the TOML of problematic pins\n\n```bash\n# backups\ncp pyproject.toml pyproject.toml.bak\ncp poetry.lock poetry.lock.bak\n\n# 1) drop the bad / non-indexed packages from pyproject\n#    (remove pytorch-triton and the PyTorch trio so Poetry won't try to resolve them)\nsed -i '/^[[:space:]]*pytorch-triton[[:space:]]*=.*/d' pyproject.toml\nsed -i '/^[[:space:]]*torch[[:space:]]*=.*/d'            pyproject.toml\nsed -i '/^[[:space:]]*torchvision[[:space:]]*=.*/d'      pyproject.toml\nsed -i '/^[[:space:]]*torchaudio[[:space:]]*=.*/d'       pyproject.toml\n```\n\n> This keeps the rest of your deps intact and prevents Poetry from touching Torch.\n\n---\n\n## B. Re‑lock strictly to the current graph (no updates)\n\n```bash\n# Re-parse lockfile using what's already pinned in poetry.lock\npoetry lock --no-update\n\n# Install exactly what's in the lock (no resolver changes)\npoetry install --sync --no-root\n```\n\nIf Poetry says the lock “changed significantly,” that’s okay—we removed four lines; let it re‑emit a lock **without** those entries.\n\n---\n\n## C. Now install the CUDA PyTorch wheels (outside Poetry’s resolver)\n\n```bash\n# Install the PyTorch trio from the cu121 index so you get CUDA + the right triton\npoetry run python -m pip install --upgrade \\\n  --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121 \\\n  torch==2.8.0 torchvision==0.19.0 torchaudio==2.8.0\n```\n\n- We **do not** pass `--no-deps` here, so pip can pull the matching `triton` wheel that Torch expects.\n- This avoids the whole “pytorch‑triton 3.2.0+git…” Poetry issue entirely.\n\n---\n\n## D. Verify\n\n```bash\npoetry run python - <<'PY'\nimport torch, importlib\nprint(\"torch:\", torch.__version__)\nprint(\"cuda available:\", torch.cuda.is_available())\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    print(\"gpu:\", torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\ntry:\n    triton = importlib.import_module(\"triton\")\n    print(\"triton:\", triton.__version__)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"triton not found:\", e)\nPY\n```\n\nYou should see `cuda available: True` and a `triton` version (e.g., 3.x).\n\n---\n\n## E. (Optional) Make this repeatable\n\nCreate a **constraints file** so your PyTorch wheel set is reproducible without Poetry managing it:\n\n**`constraints-pytorch-cu121.txt`**\n```\n--index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121\ntorch==2.8.0\ntorchvision==0.1