{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Or MAYBE just stop using poetry. It seems to cause only trouble."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Totally fair. If Poetry is getting in the way, drop it. Here’s a clean, repeatable path to run your stack with **plain venv + pip** (no resolver drama), while still getting the **CUDA 12.1** PyTorch wheels you want.\n\n---\n\n# A) Snapshot what works (once)\n\n> Do this inside your *current* env one last time, so we can reproduce it.\n\n```bash\n# If you’re in `poetry shell`, just run the python/pip it gives you:\npython -m pip freeze > requirements.freeze.txt\n```\n\nKeep that file as a safety net.\n\n---\n\n# B) Minimal “no‑Poetry” project layout\n\n```text\nyour_project/\n  .venv/                      # new venv (local to project)\n  app.py                      # your FastAPI front door (unchanged)\n  vllm_server.sh              # if you’re using vLLM (optional)\n  api_server.sh               # uvicorn launcher\n  smoke_test.sh               # quick curl\n  requirements.in             # non‑PyTorch deps\n  constraints-pytorch-cu121.txt   # CUDA‑enabled torch trio\n  README-repro.md\n```\n\n---\n\n# C) Files to drop in\n\n## 1) `requirements.in`\n> Everything **except** torch/vision/audio. Add/remove to match your project.\n\n```txt\n# Core app\nfastapi==0.115.0\nuvicorn[standard]==0.30.0\nhttpx==0.27.0\npydantic==2.8.2\npython-dotenv==1.0.1\n\n# LLM stack (pick what you use)\nvllm==0.5.3\ntransformers==4.43.0\naccelerate==0.31.0\nbitsandbytes==0.43.1\npeft==0.11.1\ntrl==0.9.6\n\n# If you’re using Zephyr via Ollama only, you can drop vLLM/transformers, etc.\n```\n\n## 2) `constraints-pytorch-cu121.txt`\n> Installs CUDA wheels + matching Triton from NVIDIA’s index (no Poetry needed).\n\n```txt\n--index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121\ntorch==2.8.0\ntorchvision==0.19.0\ntorchaudio==2.8.0\n```\n\n## 3) `api_server.sh`\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n# Activate venv\nif [ ! -d .venv ]; then python3 -m venv .venv; fi\nsource .venv/bin/activate\n\n# Run the API\npython -m uvicorn app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080\n```\n\n## 4) (optional) `vllm_server.sh`\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\nsource .venv/bin/activate\n# Adjust model / context for your GPU. For Zephyr 7B from HF:\npython -m vllm.entrypoints.api_server \\\n  --model HuggingFaceH4/zephyr-7b-beta \\\n  --dtype auto \\\n  --max-model-len 16384 \\\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.85 \\\n  --tensor-parallel-size 1 \\\n  --port 8000\n```\n\n## 5) `smoke_test.sh`\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\ncurl -s \"http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/chat/completions\" \\\n -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n -d '{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Give me 3 steps to verify you are running.\"}]}' | sed 's/\\\\n/\\n/g'\necho\n```\n\n## 6) `README-repro.md`\n```md\n# Reproduce environment (no Poetry)\n\n```bash\n# 1) New venv\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npython -m pip install --upgrade pip\n\n# 2) Install app deps (no torch yet)\npip install -r requirements.in\n\n# 3) Install CUDA 12.1 PyTorch wheels (brings matching Triton)\npip install -r constraints-pytorch-cu121.txt\n\n# 4) Verify GPU\npython - << 'PY'\nimport torch, importlib\nprint(\"torch:\", torch.__version__)\nprint(\"cuda:\", torch.cuda.is_available())\nif torch.cuda.is_available(): print(\"gpu:\", torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\ntry:\n    print(\"triton:\", importlib.import_module(\"triton\").__version__)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"triton missing:\", e)\nPY\n\n# 5a) If using vLLM backend:\n./vllm_server.sh     # serves model on :8000\n\n# 5b) Start your FastAPI front door (points to vLLM or Ollama)\n./api_server.sh\n\n# 6) Test\n./smoke_test.sh\n```\n```\n\n---\n\n# D) One‑liner rebuild (fresh machine)\n\n```bash\n# clone / copy your project folder\ncd your_project\n\npython3 -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate\npython -m pip install --upgrade pip\npip install -r requirements.in\npip install -r constraints-pytorch-cu121.txt\n\n# then run servers\n./vllm_server.sh   # if you use vLLM, else skip\n./api_server.sh\n./smoke_test.sh\n```\n\n---\n\n# E) If you’re on **Ollama + Zephyr** only (no vLLM)\n\n1) Install Ollama once:\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh\nollama pull zephyr:7b-beta\n```\n\n2) Your `requirements.in` can be much smaller (FastAPI, httpx).  \n3) In `app.py`, call `ollama` (as you already do), and skip the vLLM server.\n\n---\n\n# F) What to do with the old Poetry files\n\n- Keep `requirements.freeze.txt` for audit.  \n- **Delete** `poetry.lock` and `pyproject.toml` from the repo (or archive them).  \n- From now on, your “single source of truth” is:\n  - `requirements.in` (app deps)\n  - `constraints-pytorch-cu121.txt` (CUDA torch trio)\n  - the **.venv** created locally (not committed)\n\n---\n\n# G) Why this solves your issues\n\n- No resolver → no surprise downgrades.  \n- You explicitly install **CUDA** wheels from NVIDIA’s index.  \n- `triton` comes automatically with Torch (no weird `pytorch-triton` pins).  \n- Everything is **copy‑paste reproducible**.\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can also give you a **Makefile** with targets like `make venv`, `make deps`, `make run`, and `make clean` to simplify the routine even further."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
