{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "nvcc --version\nCommand 'nvcc' not found, but can be installed with:\nsudo apt install nvidia-cuda-toolkit"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "That means the **CUDA *runtime* is installed**, but the **CUDA *compiler* (`nvcc`) is *not*** — which is exactly what the error message during the PyTorch build was complaining about.\n\nWSL is tricky: sometimes `cuda-toolkit-*` packages only install the runtime libraries (`libcudart.so`) but don't include the compiler.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Install the full compiler by installing **`nvidia-cuda-toolkit`**\n\nRun this in WSL:\n\n```bash\nsudo apt install nvidia-cuda-toolkit\n```\n\nAfter that finishes, verify that `nvcc` works:\n\n```bash\nnvcc --version\n```\n\nOnce that prints a version banner, **re-run your PyTorch build script**, and it should finally compile successfully with `sm_120` support.\n\nWant me to give you a single block you can run that installs it *and* re-runs the script in one go?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "nvcc fatal   : Unsupported gpu architecture 'compute_120'\nnvcc fatal   : Unsupported gpu architecture 'compute_120'\nnvcc fatal   : Unsupported gpu architecture 'compute_120'\nCompiling       src/device/onerank.cu\nmake[2]: *** [Makefile:97: /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/common.cu.o] Error 1\nmake[2]: *** Waiting for unfinished jobs....\nCompiling       /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/gensrc/all_gather.cu\nCompiling       /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/gensrc/all_reduce_minmax_bf16.cu\nnvcc fatal   : Unsupported gpu architecture 'compute_120'\nmake[2]: *** [Makefile:97: /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/onerank.cu.o] Error 1\nnvcc fatal   : Unsupported gpu architecture 'compute_120'\nmake[2]: *** [/home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/gensrc/rules.mk:4: /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/genobj/all_gather.cu.o] Error 1\nCompiling       /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/gensrc/all_reduce_minmax_f16.cu\nnvcc fatal   : Unsupported gpu architecture 'compute_120'\nmake[2]: *** [/home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/gensrc/rules.mk:7: /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/genobj/all_reduce_minmax_bf16.cu.o] Error 1\nnvcc fatal   : Unsupported gpu architecture 'compute_120'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "That error is telling us something important:\n\n> **Your `nvcc` compiler does *not* support the new Ada `sm_120` architecture**, so when PyTorch tries to compile with `TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=\"12.0\"` it fails with:\n>\n> `nvcc fatal: Unsupported gpu architecture 'compute_120'`\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Why this is happening\n\n- Even though your **driver** is CUDA 12.8, the **compiler (`nvcc`) you just installed via `nvidia-cuda-toolkit`) is *older*** (likely CUDA 12.1 or 12.2).\n- That compiler doesn’t recognize `compute_120`, so it throws a fatal error.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Two ways forward:\n\n#### **Option A — Relax the build to target sm_90 (Hopper)**  \nPyTorch won’t generate Ada‐specific kernels, but they *will still run* on your GPU at lower performance.\n\nEdit your build script so this line:\n\n```bash\nexport TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=\"8.9;9.0;12.0\"\n```\n\n…becomes:\n\n```bash\nexport TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=\"8.9;9.0\"\n```\n\nThen re-run the build — it should compile successfully.\n\n➡️ This gives you *working GPU compute* inside WSL right now.\n\n---\n\n#### **Option B — Install the *matching CUDA 12.8 compiler* inside WSL**  \nThis would allow true Ada (`sm_120`) builds — but at the moment NVIDIA **has not yet released a CUDA 12.8 `nvcc` package for Ubuntu 24.04**, so we **can’t use sm_120 yet** under WSL.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Recommendation (practical path):\n\nLet’s **rebuild targeting sm_8.9 + sm_9.0 only**, so your PyTorch works on GPU *now*.  \nWould you like me to send a fixed version of the build script you can run straight away?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
