{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "CMake Error at cmake/public/cuda.cmake:262 (set_property):\n  The link interface of target \"torch::cufile\" contains:\n\n    CUDA::cuFile\n\n  but the target was not found.  Possible reasons include:\n\n    * There is a typo in the target name.\n    * A find_package call is missing for an IMPORTED target.\n    * An ALIAS target is missing.\n\nCall Stack (most recent call first):\n  cmake/Dependencies.cmake:44 (include)\n  CMakeLists.txt:868 (include)\n\n\n-- Generating done (1.1s)\nCMake Generate step failed.  Build files cannot be regenerated correctly."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "That error indicates the PyTorch build system is trying to link against **`CUDA::cuFile`**, which is part of the **NVIDIA GPUDirect Storage (GDS)** libraries — *but those libraries are not available inside WSL*.\n\nThis is a known issue when building PyTorch with WSL + CUDA toolkit >=12, because PyTorch’s CMake defaults to enabling cuFile even though WSL doesn’t support it.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Fix: explicitly **disable cuFile** during the build\n\nEdit the build script to set:\n\n```bash\nexport USE_CUDA=1\nexport USE_CUDNN=1\nexport USE_CUFILE=0\nexport TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=\"8.9;9.0\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 Here’s an updated build script block you can use:\n\n```bash\nexport USE_CUDA=1\nexport USE_CUDNN=1\nexport USE_CUFILE=0      # <---- disable cuFile for WSL\nexport TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=\"8.9;9.0\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔁 So:\n1. Wipe `pytorch/` again:\n   ```bash\n   rm -rf pytorch\n   ```\n\n2. Update your script with the new `USE_CUFILE=0` line\n\n3. Re-run the script\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to generate the **fully patched script** with that already in place so you can just re-run it?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
