* [/home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/gensrc/rules.mk:220: /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/genobj/reduce_scatter_minmax_f32.cu.o] Error 1\nmake[2]: *** [/home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/gensrc/rules.mk:223: /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/genobj/reduce_scatter_minmax_f64.cu.o] Error 1\nmake[2]: *** [/home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/gensrc/rules.mk:226: /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/genobj/reduce_scatter_minmax_f8e4m3.cu.o] Error 1\nmake[2]: *** [/home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/gensrc/rules.mk:214: /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/genobj/reduce_scatter_minmax_bf16.cu.o] Error 1\nmake[2]: *** [/home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/gensrc/rules.mk:229: /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/genobj/reduce_scatter_minmax_f8e5m2.cu.o] Error 1\nmake[2]: Leaving directory '/home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/third_party/nccl/src/device'\nmake[1]: *** [Makefile:70: /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/obj/device/manifest] Error 2\nmake[1]: *** Waiting for unfinished jobs....\nmake[1]: Leaving directory '/home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/third_party/nccl/src'\nmake: *** [Makefile:25: src.build] Error 2\n[1447/8210] Building CXX object third_party/fbgemm/CMakeFiles/fbgemm_generic.dir/src/EmbeddingSpMDM.cc.o\nninja: build stopped: subcommand failed."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "That failure is because your **host compiler (gcc)** is *too new* for the version of `nvcc` inside your CUDA toolkit.\n\nSpecifically:\n\n> `gcc versions later than 12 are not supported!`\n\nYou’re currently on **GCC 13.3.0** (Ubuntu 24.04 ships with that), but `nvcc` only supports **up to gcc-12.x** — so the CUDA portion of the PyTorch build crashes.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Two possible fixes\n\n#### **Option A — Install GCC-12 alongside GCC-13 and tell nvcc to use it**\n> (Recommended — common workaround)\n\n```bash\nsudo apt install gcc-12 g++-12\n\n# Then set these before running your build script:\nexport CC=/usr/bin/gcc-12\nexport CXX=/usr/bin/g++-12\n```\n\n…and re-run the patched build script.\n\n#### **Option B — Override nvcc's check (less safe)**\n\nAdd this to your environment before the build:\n\n```bash\nexport NVCC_FLAGS=\"--allow-unsupported-compiler\"\n```\n\n…but this *may still fail later in the compile* — so Option A is more reliable.\n\n---\n\n### 👉 Suggest we do:\n\n1. Install gcc-12/g++-12  \n2. Export CC/CXX to point at them  \n3. Re-run your `build_torch_wsl_fixed.sh`\n\nWant me to generate the updated build script that *includes* the gcc-12 install and those exports automatically at the top?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "# Then set these before running your build script:\nexport CC=/usr/bin/gcc-12\nexport CXX=/usr/bin/g++-12\nReading package lists... Done\nBuilding dependency tree... Done\nReading state information... Done\ngcc-12 is already the newest version (12.3.0-17ubuntu1).\ngcc-12 set to manually installed.\ng++-12 is already the newest version (12.3.0-17ubuntu1).\ng++-12 set to manually installed.\n0 upgraded, 0 newly installed, 0 to remove and 1 not upgraded."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect — gcc-12 and g++-12 are already installed.\n\nNow before rerunning your PyTorch build script, make sure to **export the compiler variables in the same terminal session**, so `cmake` and `nvcc` use gcc-12 instead of gcc-13:\n\n```bash\nexport CC=/usr/bin/gcc-12\nexport CXX=/usr/bin/g++-12\n```\n\nYou can verify they’re set correctly with:\n\n```bash\n$ echo $CC  => /usr/bin/gcc-12\n$ echo $CXX => /usr/bin/g++-12\n```\n\n---\n\nThen **run your patched build script again**:\n\n```bash\n./build_torch_wsl_fixed.sh | tee torch_build.log\n```\n\nThat should get you past the previous `unsupported GNU version` error.\n\nWant me to update your build script so it *automatically* sets `CC` and `CXX` for future runs?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "make[2]: Leaving directory '/home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/third_party/nccl/src/device'\nLinking    libnccl.so.2.27.5                   > /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/lib/libnccl.so.2.27.5\nArchiving  libnccl_static.a                    > /home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/build/nccl/lib/libnccl_static.a\nmake[1]: Leaving directory '/home/todd/dev/oss20b_test/pyTorch/pytorch/third_party/nccl/src'\nninja: build stopped: subcommand failed.\n-- Checkout nccl release tag: v2.27.5-1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "You're extremely close — NCCL (the GPU communication library) successfully finished compiling and linking... but then **another step in the PyTorch build failed just *after* NCCL**.\n\nThe output ending with:\n\n> `ninja: build stopped: subcommand failed.`\n\n…but without an obvious error indicates **some other compilation target failed** *earlier in the scrollback* (perhaps one of PyTorch's C++/CUDA ops).\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Next steps:\n\n1. **Scroll back** or check your `torch_build.log` for the *first* error message above that `ninja: build stopped` line. That will tell us which piece is failing.\n\n2. Alternatively, run the build again in **verbose mode**, so we see exactly which target is failing:\n\n```bash\npython setup.py bdist_wheel -v 2>&1 | tee torch_build_verbose.log\n```\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common causes (after NCCL succeeds):\n- Missing OpenMP dev headers (`libomp-dev`)  \n- Missing MKL dev headers  \n- More CUDA arch flags needed  \n- Running out of memory\n\n---\n\nWant me to send you a **cut-down build command** so we only build the *necessary GPU components*, skipping advanced distributed ops like NCCL? That usually avoids these later-stage failures and gives you a functional wheel more quickly."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
