{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "same again.\n$ poetry run python run.py\nLoading tokenizer and model...\ntokenizer_config.json: 1.29kB [00:00, 7.49MB/s]\ntokenizer.model: 100%|████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████| 500k/500k [00:01<00:00, 449kB/s]\ntokenizer.json: 1.84MB [00:00, 19.9MB/s]\nspecial_tokens_map.json: 100%|█████████████████████████████████████████████████████████| 551/551 [00:00<00:00, 6.21MB/s]\nconfig.json: 100%|█████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████| 608/608 [00:00<00:00, 6.66MB/s]\nmodel.safetensors: 100%|████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████| 2.20G/2.20G [00:20<00:00, 109MB/s]\ngeneration_config.json: 100%|██████████████████████████████████████████████████████████| 124/124 [00:00<00:00, 1.43MB/s]\nPrompt: If a farmer has 17 sheep and all but nine die, how many are left? Explain your answer.\n\n=== Response ===\nIf a farmer has 17 sheep and all but nine die, how many are left? Explain your answer.\n(srcEnv) todd@lava:~/dev/oss20b_test$ poetry run python run.py\nLoading tokenizer and model...\nPrompt: If a farmer has 17 sheep and all but nine die, how many are left? Explain your answer.\n\n=== Response ===\nIf a farmer has 17 sheep and all but nine die, how many are left? Explain your answer."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "That’s happening because you're feeding the model only the **user prompt**, but not a conversation **template** that tells it to *generate a reply*.  \n\nMany open-weights LLMs (including TinyLlama, Mistral, Llama-3, etc.) expect prompts to be formatted in a **chat template style**, e.g.:\n\n```\n<|user|> … </s><|assistant|>\n```\n\nWithout that, they think your prompt is *part of the text they should continue*, so they just **keep copying it**.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Fix: wrap your prompt in the model’s expected chat/autoregressive format.\n\nFor TinyLlama (Chat version), use:\n\n```python\nprompt = f\"<|user|>\\n{your_text}\\n<|assistant|>\\n\"\n```\n\nThen call `model.generate(...)` on that.\n\n---\n\n### Here’s a drop-in `run.py` you can paste over your current one:\n```python\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM\n\nmodel_id = \"TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0\"\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_id)\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n    model_id,\n    torch_dtype=\"auto\",\n    device_map=\"auto\"\n).eval()\n\nprompt_raw = input(\"Prompt: \")\n\n# TinyLlama chat formatting\nprompt = f\"<|user|>\\n{prompt_raw}\\n<|assistant|>\\n\"\ninputs = tokenizer(prompt, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(model.device)\n\noutput_ids = model.generate(\n    **inputs,\n    max_new_tokens=128,\n    do_sample=True,\n    temperature=0.7,\n    top_p=0.9\n)\n\nresponse = tokenizer.decode(output_ids[0][inputs[\"input_ids\"].shape[1]:], skip_special_tokens=True)\nprint(\"\\n=== Response ===\")\nprint(response.strip())\n```\n\n---\n\n### Try it again with your farmer prompt — you should now get:\n> **“There are nine sheep left…”** (plus an explanation)\n\nWant me to drop that file directly into your project so you don’t have to copy-paste?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "poetry run python run.py\nusing model: TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0\nLoading tokenizer and model...\nPrompt: If a farmer has 17 sheep and all but nine die, how many are left? Explain your answer.\n\n=== Response ===\nIf a farmer has 17 sheep and all but nine die, how many are left? Explain your answer.\n\n2. 2. What is the formula for calculating the average of a set of numbers? Explain how this formula is used in the problem you will solve.\n\n3. 3. What is the difference between the average and the mode of a set of numbers? Explain how this difference is used in the problem you will solve.\n\n4. 4. What is the expected value of a random variable with a mean of 10 and a standard deviation of 2? Explain how this formula is used in the problem you will solve.\n\n5. 5. What is the variance"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Nice — now it’s *actually generating*, not repeating verbatim 👏\n\nBut what you're seeing now suggests the **chat formatting still isn’t exactly what TinyLlama expects**, so it’s interpreting your user prompt as part of a *multi-turn instruction chain* and responding with *follow-up questions* rather than giving the direct answer.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Recommended tweak\n\nTinyLlama’s chat template expects explicit *assistant role tokens*, like:\n\n```\n<s> <|user|>\n<user message>\n<|assistant|>\n```\n\nTry updating the prompt wrapper to:\n\n```python\nprompt = f\"<s><|user|>\\n{prompt_raw}</s>\\n<|assistant|>\\n\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Updated `run.py` snippet\n\nReplace your formatting line with:\n\n```python\nprompt = f\"<s><|user|>\\n{prompt_raw}</s>\\n<|assistant|>\\n\"\n```\n\n…everything else stays the same.\n\n---\n\nWant me to paste the full corrected file so you can just overwrite and re-run?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "give me the full file, please."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Sure — here’s a complete `run.py` ready to drop into your project:\n\n```python\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM\n\n# You can change this to another HF repo later (e.g., llama-3-8B)\nmodel_id = \"TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0\"\n\nprint(f\"using model: {model_id}\")\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_id)\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n    model_id,\n    torch_dtype=\"auto\",\n    device_map=\"auto\"\n).eval()\n\nprompt_raw = input(\"Prompt: \")\n\n# TinyLlama chat prompt format\nprompt = f\"<s><|user|>\\n{prompt_raw}</s>\\n<|assistant|>\\n\"\ninputs = tokenizer(prompt, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(model.device)\n\noutput_ids = model.generate(\n    **inputs,\n    max_new_tokens=128,\n    do_sample=True,\n    temperature=0.7,\n    top_p=0.9\n)\n\nresponse = tokenizer.decode(\n    output_ids[0][inputs[\"input_ids\"].shape[1]:], \n    skip_special_tokens=True\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n=== Response ===\")\nprint(response.strip())\n```\n\n---\n\n📌 Suggestions:\n- When this works, swap `model_id` to e.g. `\"meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct\"` to upgrade.\n- You can also embed this into toddric’s loop easily once inference is behaving.\n\nWant me to also give you a version that **loops continuously** so you can chat interactively rather than restarting the script for each question?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "poetry run python run.py\nusing model: TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0\nPrompt: If a farmer has 17 sheep and all but nine die, how many are left? Explain your answer.\n\n=== Response ===\nIf a farmer has 17 sheep and all but nine die, the remaining 12 sheep are left. This is because the original 17 sheep were 17-12 = 5. Therefore, the answer to your question is 12."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Boom — that’s exactly what we wanted 🎯\n\n✅ *Model is loading correctly*  \n✅ *Prompt formatting now works*  \n✅ *You’re getting an actual natural-language answer* (even if the math is hilariously wrong 😂)\n\n---\n\n### Next step?\n\nWould you like me to:\n\n- 🔁 Turn this into a **looping chat** (so you can talk to it interactively without restarting the script)?\n- 🚀 Swap in a **stronger model** (e.g. Llama-3 8B) now that your pipeline is proven?\n- 💾 Wrap it into a simple **API endpoint** or background “toddric brain” service?\n\nJust say the word."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Let's go with a looping chat and stronger model."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect — I’ll give you a **drop-in replacement `run.py`** that:\n\n- ✅ Runs as a *looping chat session*\n- 🔁 Keeps conversation history so responses are contextual\n- ⚡ Uses a stronger model by default (**Llama-3-8B-Instruct** — generally fits in 16 GB GPUs at `torch.float16`)\n- 🔄 Can be swapped back to TinyLlama instantly if needed\n\n---\n\n### 📄 **Paste this as your new `run.py`:**\n\n```python\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM\n\n# Choose the model\n# model_id = \"TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0\"\nmodel_id = \"meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct\"\n\nprint(f\"Using model: {model_id}\")\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_id)\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n    model_id,\n    torch_dtype=\"auto\",\n    device_map=\"auto\"\n).eval()\n\nhistory = \"\"  # conversation context\n\nwhile True:\n    user = input(\"\\nYou: \")\n    if user.strip().lower() in {\"quit\", \"exit\"}:\n        break\n\n    # format prompt for llama-3 style chat\n    prompt = f\"<|user|>\\n{user}\\n<|assistant|>\\n\"\n    full_prompt = history + prompt\n\n    inputs = tokenizer(full_prompt, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(model.device)\n\n    output_ids = model.generate(\n        **inputs,\n        max_new_tokens=200,\n        do_sample=True,\n        temperature=0.7,\n        top_p=0.9\n    )\n\n    response = tokenizer.decode(output_ids[0][inputs[\"input_ids\"].shape[1]:],\n                                skip_special_tokens=True).strip()\n\n    print(f\"🦙: {response}\")\n\n    # accumulate chat history\n    history += prompt + response + \"\\n\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Note\nIf `meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct` complains about access or VRAM, you can *instantly swap back* to TinyLlama by uncommenting the other `model_id` line.\n\n---\n\nWant me to also:\n- add **streaming responses (token-by-token)** for responsiveness?\n- enforce a **history cutoff** so things don’t blow up?\n- or add **logging** so you can save conversation transcripts for toddric memory/training?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
