{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "CPU upgrade would require new mobo."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Right — since Rose’s current board is an **Intel Z-490-I (LGA1200)**, you’re locked to **10th/11th-gen Intel** CPUs — meaning the best possible drop-in upgrade is only an **i9-11900K**, which still bottlenecks a 5090 for LLM workloads.\n\nSo if you want the CPU to *truly* match the 5090, you’d need:\n\n---\n\n### 🔄 **New Platform (CPU + Motherboard + possibly RAM)**\n\n#### 🔥 Performance-per-€ sweet spots right now:\n| CPU                   | Platform     | Notes                                          |\n|------------------------|--------------|-----------------------------------------------|\n| **Intel i7-14700K**     | LGA1700 (Z790) | 20 cores (8P+12E), good for inference/training |\n| **Intel i9-14900K**     | LGA1700 (Z790) | Monster performance, higher heat/power        |\n| **AMD 7950X3D**         | AM5 (X670E/B650E) | 16 cores, great cache, very cool/efficient     |\n\n> Note: switching to AMD would mean **new DDR5 RAM** as well.  \nIntel LGA1700 lets you reuse your DDR4 *if* you pick the right Z-790 board.\n\n---\n\n### ⚙️ **Most seamless upgrade path for Rose:**\n\n- **CPU:** Intel i7-14700K  \n- **Mobo:** Z-790 ITX-DDR4 board (eg. ASUS ROG Strix Z790-I Gaming WiFi)  \n- **RAM:** *(reuse existing 64 GB DDR4)*  \n\n→ keeps cost down & drops straight into the Fractal North case you’re already getting\n\n---\n\nWant me to spec that out and show total pricing — **with and without DDR5** — so you can decide if the performance gain is worth it *right now*, or whether to stick with the i7-10700 until later?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
