{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "using nvidia-smi there"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Sure — once you’ve got the RTX 5090 installed in Rose, you’ll be able to use `nvidia-smi` normally to:\n\n- Verify the driver is loaded  \n- Check GPU temperature, power draw, and memory usage  \n- Monitor active processes + VRAM usage during LLM inference  \n\nExample command:\n\n```bash\nwatch -n1 nvidia-smi\n```\n\nThat will update every second so you can see things live.\n\nWant me to give you a cheat-sheet of the most useful `nvidia-smi` commands for LLM work and GPU troubleshooting?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "there's a way to set max power."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Yes — you can *manually set the power limit* on the GPU using `nvidia-smi`, as long as the card’s VBIOS and driver allow it.\n\n### ✅ **Check current power range**\n\n```bash\nnvidia-smi --query-gpu=power.min_limit,power.max_limit,power.default_limit --format=csv\n```\n\nThis shows the **minimum**, **maximum**, and **default** wattage limits supported by your GPU.\n\n### ⚡ **Set a new maximum power limit**\n\n```bash\nsudo nvidia-smi -pl <WATTS>\n```\n\nFor example:\n\n```bash\nsudo nvidia-smi -pl 400\n```\n\n🔐 Requires:\n- NVIDIA driver installed\n- `sudo` permissions\n- Persistence mode usually enabled:  \n  ```bash\n  sudo nvidia-smi -pm 1\n  ```\n\n---\n\nWant me to bundle a small script so you can **auto-set your preferred power cap at boot**?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "and on lava what should it be"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "To set a safe & efficient power cap on **Lava’s GPU**, I just need to know which GPU she’s running.\n\nCan you confirm:\n\n- 👉 **Exact GPU model in Lava** (e.g., *RTX 4070 Laptop*, *RTX 3070 Ti Laptop*, etc.)\n- 👉 Whether you’d prefer *longer battery life & quietness* or *maximum performance even if louder/hotter*\n\nOnce I know those two things, I’ll give you the **recommended power limit range** to set via `nvidia-smi -pl`."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You listed Corsair pc toolkit"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Ah — you're thinking of the **Corsair PC DIY Toolkit** (officially called the **Corsair Premium PC Building Kit**). Here’s what’s actually inside that kit and how it stacks up:\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 **Corsair Premium PC Toolkit – Contents**\n- **Magnetic screwdriver handle**  \n- **20 interchangeable bits**, including:\n  - Phillips (PH0–PH2)\n  - Flathead\n  - Torx (T6–T20)\n  - Hex\n- **Ratchet screwdriver** (for faster screw driving)\n- **Needle-nose pliers**\n- **Flush/side cutters**\n- **Cable comb set** (for sleeved PSU cables)\n- **Angled tweezers**\n- **Spudger/prying tool**\n- **Utility knife**\n- **Zip-ties**\n- **Anti-static wrist strap**\n- **Magnetic parts tray**\n- **Durable soft-shell carry case**\n\n---\n\n### ✅ **Good for:**\n- Mid-to-high-end PC building and upgrades  \n- Cable-managed builds (especially with Corsair PSUs)  \n- Portability (nice zipper case)\n\n### ⚠️ **What it *doesn’t* include:**\n- Thermal paste\n- Alcohol wipes / cleaning supplies\n- Anti-static *mat*\n- Multimeter\n- PC speaker for POST codes\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to:\n- Compare it against other pre-made toolkits (e.g. iFixit Pro, Rosewill, NZXT)?\n- Or just throw you the **best price link** for it in Ireland?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "I'm just looking for a good toolkit for building PCs"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it — if your focus is *building and upgrading desktop PCs*, here are the two best options depending on how “serious” you want to get:\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 **Best Overall: iFixit Pro Tech Toolkit (~€70)**\nIdeal if you want something **high-quality and future-proof**, not just for PCs but any tech repair.\n\n- 64 premium driver bits (Phillips, Torx, hex, etc.)\n- Excellent magnetic screwdriver handle\n- Tweezers, spudgers (for connectors), pry tools\n- Anti-static wrist strap\n- Magnetic tray built into the lid\n- Fantastic quality, lifetime warranty\n\n📌 *Widely regarded as the gold standard for PC builders and techs.*\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 **Budget-Friendly PC-Only Option: Corsair Premium PC Toolkit (~€40–€50)**\nGood if you *only care about PC building* and want a neat carry case.\n\n- Ratcheting magnetic screwdriver\n- All the bits you need for PC screws & standoffs\n- Flush cutters, pliers, tweezers, cable combs\n- Anti-static strap & magnetic parts tray\n\n📌 *Not as versatile as iFixit and tools aren’t as premium — but perfectly fine for PC building.*\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Recommendation\nIf you’re planning on building more than one PC — **go with the iFixit Pro Tech Toolkit**. It’ll cover everything from case screws to GPU teardown and will last you for years.\n\nWant the buying links for Amazon.ie?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Where can I get passport photos in Letterkenny?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "If you're in Letterkenny and need passport photos, here are some convenient and reliable options in town:\n\nbusinesses_map{\"name\":\"Magees One Hour Photo Lab\",\"location\":\"Letterkenny, Co. Donegal, Ireland\",\"description\":\"One-hour passport-size photos (four prints, various countries/visa formats) at 27 Upper Main Street.\",\"cite\":\"turn0search5\"}{\"name\":\"Photo-Me photobooths\",\"location\":\"Letterkenny, Co. Donegal, Ireland\",\"description\":\"Automated booths in e.g. Courtyard (Main Street) and Tesco Supercenter—DFA-approved ID/passport photos with digital code.\",\"cite\":\"turn0search4\"}{\"name\":\"McFadden’s (via pharmacy)\",\"location\":\"Letterkenny, Co. Donegal, Ireland\",\"description\":\"Passport photo service available in-store at a pharmacy (likely McFadden’s near TES­CO area).\",\"cite\":\"turn0search4\"}\n\n---\n\n###  Option Details\n\n- **Magees One Hour Photo Lab**  \n  Located at 27 Upper Main Street, Letterkenny, this photo lab provides a **one-hour service** for standard passport and visa photographs. You’ll receive four prints, in colour or black & white, while you wait. They also cater to various countries and visa specifications.  \n  citeturn0search5\n\n- **Photo-Me Photobooths**  \n  Automated photobooths ideal for quick, self-service passport photos. These are said to be located in **The Courtyard on Main Street** and **Tesco Supercentre** in Letterkenny. They produce DFA-approved photos and often include a digital approval code useful for online passport applications.  \n  citeturn0search4turn0search2\n\n- **McFadden’s Pharmacy**  \n  A local pharmacy offering in-store passport photo services, likely around the Tesco area. It’s a convenient walk-in option, and there’s no appointment required.  \n  citeturn0search4turn0search7\n\n---\n\n###  Quick Comparison\n\n| Option                    | Format               | Speed       | Additional Benefit                            |\n|---------------------------|----------------------|-------------|-----------------------------------------------|\n| Magees One Hour Photo Lab | Lab service (staffed) | ~1 hour     | Four physical prints; supports various visa formats |\n| Photo-Me Photobooths      | Self-service booth    | Immediate   | DFA-approved; digital code for online applications |\n| McFadden’s Pharmacy       | Staffed service      | Walk-in     | Pharmacy convenience, no appointment needed   |\n\n---\n\n###  Choosing the Best Option\n\n- **Need photos faster?**  \n  **Photo-Me booths** offer near-instant prints—perfect if you're in a hurry and confident about getting the framing right yourself.\n\n- **Prefer assistance?**  \n  **Magees** and **McFadden’s** provide staff help. Magees gives a bit more flexibility with formats (e.g. different visa types), while McFadden’s is convenient if you're already near the Tesco area.\n\n---\n\n###  Tips Before You Go\n\n- **Check opening hours**: Magees is open Mon–Wed 9 am–6 pm, Thu–Fri until 7 pm, Sat until 6 pm, Sundays closed (Bank Holidays noon–4 pm) citeturn0search5.  \n- **Bring valid ID**: Even in booths, ID might be needed.\n- **Consider digital code**: For online passport renewals/applications, Photo-Me's digital code can save time.\n\nLet me know if you'd like addresses, opening hours, or directions for any of these locations!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "What are good resources for following AI developments?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "If you're looking to stay on top of AI developments, here's a curated list of the most effective and reliable resources—across formats like blogs, newsletters, reports, aggregators, and policy sites—complete with context so you can tailor your learning path:\n\n---\n\n##  News & Blogs (Industry & Research)\n\n- **OpenAI Blog**, **Google AI Blog**, and **DeepMind Blog** — Official channels for posts on new models, breakthroughs, and research perspectives citeturn0search4turn0search6turn0search13turn0search10.\n\n- **MIT News – Artificial Intelligence** — Offers high-quality, often technical journalism from one of the world's leading research institutions. Examples: August 2025 feature on AI-based protein models and RNA therapies citeturn0search12.\n\n- **Berkeley Artificial Intelligence Research (BAIR) Blog** — Academic-focused content from UC Berkeley about ML, vision, NLP, etc. citeturn0search5turn0search8.\n\n- **KDnuggets** — Trusted source for data science, ML, big data, with a mix of industry news, tutorials, and analysis citeturn0search3turn0search4.\n\n- **AI Magazine (AIMagazine.com)** — Covers news, strategic insights, applications, and interviews across AI, ML, AR/VR sectors citeturn0search2.\n\n- **MarkTechPost** and **Towards Data Science** — Regularly updated, broader-focused blogs covering AI trends, tools, and insights — especially on topics like agentic AI citeturn0search10.\n\n- **AI Weekly**, **This Day in AI**, **TL;DR AI** — Email newsletters and podcasts offering quick digests or weekly roundups of AI news and insights citeturn0search0turn0search9.\n\n- **TechCrunch – AI Section** — Covers startups, ethical issues, and developments in generative AI, ML, and corporate trends citeturn0search7.\n\n- **Techmeme** — An AI-savvy aggregator that delivers near real-time tech headlines and discussions, including AI topics citeturn0search27.\n\n---\n\n##  Authoritative Reports & Data\n\n- **AI Index Reports (2024 & 2025)** — Comprehensive annual analyses offering up-to-date metrics on AI trends—from training costs to hardware, patents, responsible AI adoption, and more citeturn0academia22turn0academia23.\n\n- **IEEE “AI Horizon Scanning” White Paper** — Offers a strategic overview of AI’s technological, hardware, and energy trends, along with regulatory insights citeturn0academia28.\n\n---\n\n##  Policy, Ethics & Societal Impact\n\n- **AI Now Institute** — A non-profit focused on the ethical and social implications of AI; publishes timely reports and frameworks for accountability citeturn0search25.\n\n- **Partnership on AI (PAI)** — Multi-stakeholder initiative offering materials like the AI Incident Database and guidance for safe foundation model deployment citeturn0search32.\n\n- **International Association for Safe and Ethical AI (IASEAI)** — A body that holds conferences on AI safety and ethics (notably held in Paris in February 2025), and publishes research and policy recommendations citeturn0search31.\n\n- **AI Doom Index** — A sentiment-tracking tool measuring public mood about AI developments, updating every 12 hours with data-driven sentiment scores citeturn0search30.\n\n---\n\n##  Newsletters, Podcasts & Multimedia\n\n- **Import AI (Jack Clark)** — Newsletter offering deep dives into AI research and global trends citeturn0news20.\n\n- **Inside My Head (Substack)**, **Visually AI**, **Towards AI**, **The AI Podcast (Nvidia)**, **Learn Prompting**, **MIT AI ML Club (YouTube)** — Engaging generative AI resources ranging from tutorials and explainers to interviews and visual content citeturn0news18.\n\n- **Wired’s Generative AI Resources** — Includes actionable tools and podcasts to develop your skills in prompt design and generative workflows citeturn0news18.\n\n---\n\n##  Sector-Specific Updates\n\n- **Vogue Business AI Tracker** — Weekly AI developments in areas like e-commerce, creative rights, and infrastructure—e.g., ChatGPT checkout features and Meta’s “data centre the size of Manhattan” citeturn0news17.\n\n- **Tech Learning’s AI Literacy for Educators** — Focused educational AI resources for teachers—featuring tools like Digital Promise, GPT for Educators, and newsletters like Future of Being Human citeturn0news19.\n\n- **TechRadar on Open-Source AI** — Coverage of how open-source AI drives transparency, security, and global collaboration—highlighting initiatives like the AI Alliance citeturn0news26.\n\n---\n\n###  Quick Reference Table\n\n| Use Case / Format                  | Recommended Resources                                               |\n|-----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Immediate news updates**        | OpenAI, Google AI, DeepMind blogs; TechCrunch AI; Techmeme; AI Weekly |\n| **In-depth technical & academic** | MIT News AI, BAIR Blog, KDnuggets, AI Magazine                      |\n| **Strategic reports & data**      | AI Index 2024/25, IEEE Horizon Scanning White Paper                 |\n| **Ethics, safety & policy**       | AI Now Institute, PAI, IASEAI, AI Doom Index                        |\n| **Learning & creativity**         | Substack blogs (Inside My Head, Visually AI), Nvidia’s AI Podcast, Learn Prompting, YouTube (MIT AI ML Club) |\n| **Industry angle**                | Vogue Business AI Tracker                                           |\n| **Educational tools (K–12)**      | Tech Learning’s curated resources                                   |\n\n---\n\n###  Getting Started\n\n1. **Sign up for a daily or weekly digest** (e.g., AI Weekly or This Day in AI) for quick updates.\n2. **Pick a research blog** like OpenAI or MIT News to deepen your understanding.\n3. **Follow a report or index** such as the AI Index for macro trends.\n4. **Explore ethics and safety** through AI Now or PAI.\n5. **Consume varied media** like Substack essays, podcasts, or YouTube talks for creativity and practical insights.\n6. **Tailor to your domain**—use education-specific or industry-focused trackers if that’s your focus.\n\nWould you like tailored recommendations based on your background or interests—like entry-level learning, technical deep-dives, policy, or creative AI use? Just say the word!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "What causes turkey neck?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "“Turkey neck” is a common term for the loose, sagging skin and banding that can develop under the chin and along the front of the neck — especially as we age.\n\n### The main causes include:\n\n- **Loss of skin elasticity with age**  \n  As collagen and elastin production decrease over time, skin becomes thinner and less able to “snap back,” so it starts to sag.\n\n- **Muscle weakening (platysma banding)**  \n  The platysma muscle in the neck can loosen and separate into visible vertical bands, which accentuates the drooping skin.\n\n- **Accumulation or redistribution of fat**  \n  Fat pads under the chin may descend or shrink and shift, creating either fullness or hollowing that changes the contour of the neck.\n\n- **Bone loss in the jawline**  \n  As we get older, gradual bone resorption reduces the support structure of the lower face, making skin laxity more apparent.\n\n- **Sun exposure & environmental damage**  \n  UV radiation breaks down collagen and elastin faster, leading to crepey skin texture and increased sagging.\n\n- **Genetics & posture**  \n  Some people are genetically predisposed to weaker neck support tissues, and chronic forward head posture (e.g., looking down at phones) can stretch and weaken the neck skin over time.\n\nWould you like tips on how to prevent or reduce turkey neck — or go over treatment options (from exercises to surgery)?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
