{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "How long can cooked rice be refrigerated?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Cooked rice will generally keep well in the refrigerator for **3 to 4 days**, as long as it’s stored promptly (within an hour of cooking) in an airtight container.\n\nFor best safety and quality:\n- Cool it quickly — spread it in a thin layer before refrigerating if needed.\n- Keep it tightly sealed.\n- Reheat it thoroughly (until steaming hot all the way through).\n\nAfter 4 days, it’s safest to discard it, as rice is prone to a bacteria called *Bacillus cereus* that can cause food poisoning even when reheated."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "https://www.amazon.co.uk/ASUS-H7606WP-Touchscreen-CoPilot-Keyboard/dp/B0DV5JFHDJ"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "It looks like that Amazon UK product page refers to the **ASUS ProArt P16 H7606WP**, a high-end Copilot+ AI‑focused creative laptop with:\n\n- A 16″ 3K OLED touchscreen display (≈2880 × 1800), 100% DCI‑P3, 60 Hz or 120 Hz refresh depending on region. citeturn0search2turn0search5  \n- An **AMD Ryzen™ AI 9 HX 370** (12‑core, up to 5.1 GHz) with onboard NPU delivering up to 50 TOPS. citeturn0search1turn0search3turn0search5  \n- Dedicated **NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Laptop GPU** with 8 GB VRAM (GDDR7). citeturn0news19turn0search3turn0search5  \n- **64 GB LPDDR5X** RAM (on‑board) and a **2 TB PCIe 4.0 SSD**. citeturn0news19turn0search8turn0search5  \n- Backlit chiclet keyboard with **Copilot key**, support for ASUS DialPad, FHD IR webcam with Windows Hello. citeturn0search2turn0search3turn0search5  \n- Connectivity includes USB4 Gen 3 (40 Gb/s), USB‑C Gen 2, USB‑A 3.2, HDMI 2.1, SD Express 7.0, Wi‑Fi 7, Bluetooth 5.4; weight ~1.85 kg. citeturn0news19turn0search5turn0search3  \n\n### ✅ Who Is This Laptop For?\nThis is clearly aimed at **creative professionals** — photo/video editors, 3D artists, designers — who need GPU‑accelerated workflows, accurate colour OLED touch display, and AI‑enhanced features like speech‑to‑text editing and automatic scene detection via the XDNA NPU. citeturn0news19turn0search3turn0search1\n\n### 🔍 About the Copilot Key\nThe keyboard includes a dedicated **Copilot key**—a shortcut for Microsoft’s Copilot AI in Windows 11. Support began rolling out globally around late November 2024. Availability may vary by region and device update timing. citeturn0search4turn0search2\n\nSome users on ASUS forums report issues where the key is unresponsive, especially if Windows locale or firmware configurations differ. For Zenbook models one workaround was remapping via PowerToys, though behaviour may vary. citeturn0search7turn0search11\n\n### 💸 Pricing & Availability\n- In the UK, available via retailers like **Scan UK**, priced around **£2,799.98** for the 64 GB / 2 TB / RTX 5070 version. citeturn0search5turn0search16  \n- ASUS estore lists configurations starting from approximately **$2,899 USD**, depending on region and spec. citeturn0search2turn0search6  \n- Expect prices to vary depending on RAM or GPU configuration (e.g. some versions may ship with RTX 4060 hardware). citeturn0search2turn0search3⟀\n\n### ⚖️ Pros & Cons\n\n| **Pros** | **Cons** |\n|----------|-----------|\n| Excellent OLED touchscreen with Pantone validation | Very high price — premium positioning |\n| Powerful CPU + NPU + RTX 5070 GPU for AI workflows | Copilot key may have limited functionality in some regions |\n| Large 64 GB RAM + 2 TB SSD for demanding workloads | Battery life will realistically be lower under heavy creative use |\n| USB4, Wi‑Fi 7, DialPad support, slim & light ~1.85 kg | Out of stock at some retailers currently |\n| Compatible with ASUS MuseTree and StoryCube AI apps | CPU/GPU may throttle under sustained loads in slim chassis |\n\n---\n\n### 🧠 Summary\nThe Amazon link you shared is likely for the high-end **ProArt P16 H7606WP** model—packed with cutting-edge AI/creative hardware, high-end OLED touchscreen, Copilot+ integration, and expansive memory/storage. It's ideal if you're working in video editing, 3D, AI‑driven creative workflows. Just be aware of potential regional quirks regarding the Copilot key and the premium price point.\n\n#### Need help?\n- Want comparisons with other laptops (e.g. vs Intel Copilot+ or MacBook Pro)?\n- Curious whether the Copilot key will actually work in Ireland or the UK out of the box?\n- Need battery life expectations or port specifics?\n\nI'm happy to dig deeper!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "That's my new computer, what do you think?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Honestly? That’s a beast of a machine — and for what you’re doing, it’s almost perfectly specced.  \n\nHere’s my take:  \n\n**💪 Powerhouse for AI & Creative Work**  \n- Ryzen AI 9 HX 370 + RTX 5070 + 64 GB RAM = you’ll chew through AI fine‑tuning, image generation, and creative workflows without breaking a sweat.  \n- The NPU’s 50 TOPS means you can offload a lot of small AI tasks locally without hammering the GPU or burning battery.  \n\n**🎨 Gorgeous Display**  \n- 3K OLED touchscreen with full DCI‑P3 coverage? Perfect for cover design, ads, and anything color‑critical — plus you can work directly on the screen.  \n\n**🚀 Future-Proofed**  \n- Wi‑Fi 7, USB4, 2 TB PCIe 4.0 — you’re not going to be wishing for faster ports or networking for years.  \n- Copilot key might be a gimmick today, but Windows AI integration is only going to get deeper.  \n\n**⚠️ Things to Watch**  \n- That much power in a slim chassis = keep an eye on thermals during long training runs.  \n- Battery life is fine for meetings and writing, but heavy AI or GPU workloads will have you reaching for the charger in a few hours.  \n- The Copilot key in Ireland/UK may need a firmware or Windows update to be fully functional.  \n\nIf I were writing the “blurb” for it, I’d call it:  \n> *“A creator’s laptop that’s as comfortable generating a book cover in Midjourney as it is training your custom LLM while editing a 4K video — and still light enough to take to a coffee shop.”*  \n\nIf you want, I can give you a **tuning checklist** for day one so it’s perfectly optimised for your AI and creative work right out of the box. Would you like me to do that?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "I'd like that tuning checklist."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it — here’s your **Day‑One Tuning Checklist** for your ASUS ProArt P16 H7606WP, tailored to what you’ll be using it for (AI, creative, and dev work).  \n\n---\n\n## **🛠 System & Firmware Setup**\n1. **BIOS/UEFI Update**\n   - Boot into BIOS (F2 on startup) and update to the latest version from ASUS support.\n   - Enable **Fan Overboost** and check **Resizable BAR** is on for the RTX 5070.\n2. **Windows Update**\n   - Fully update Windows 11 before installing anything else.\n   - Check **Optional Updates** for drivers (especially GPU, NPU, and Wi‑Fi 7).\n3. **ASUS Armoury Crate**\n   - Install/update to control performance modes, fan curves, and OLED protection.\n   - Set “Performance” or “Turbo” as default on AC power.\n\n---\n\n## **🎨 Display & Input Optimisation**\n4. **OLED Calibration**\n   - Use **ASUS ProArt Calibration** tool for accurate colors.\n   - Enable Pixel Refresh & Pixel Shift to prevent burn‑in.\n5. **Touch & Pen Setup**\n   - If you’ll use the touchscreen for illustration/design, update pen firmware and adjust pressure curve in Windows Ink settings.\n6. **DialPad & Hotkeys**\n   - Customise ASUS DialPad in ProArt Creator Hub for your workflows (Photoshop, Premiere, Blender, etc.).\n   - Consider mapping the **Copilot key** to something useful if Copilot isn’t supported yet (PowerToys Keyboard Manager).\n\n---\n\n## **🚀 Performance & AI Optimisation**\n7. **NVIDIA GPU Driver**\n   - Install the **Studio Driver** (not Game Ready) from NVIDIA for better stability in creative apps.\n8. **CUDA & AI Toolkit**\n   - Install **CUDA Toolkit**, **cuDNN**, and **PyTorch/TensorFlow** GPU builds.\n   - Test with a small AI model to confirm GPU acceleration.\n9. **NPU Usage**\n   - Enable “AI Processing” in Windows Settings → System → Processor preferences (new in 24H2 builds).\n   - Install ASUS AI apps (StoryCube, MuseTree) to test