pare their specs, prices, or check availability with a retailer directly!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Is there a 3.0 in the works?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Yes — ENGWE has already **released a “3.0” model**, specifically the **L20 3.0 series**, which includes two versions: **L20 3.0 Boost** and **L20 3.0 Pro**, launched on **April 1, 2025** citeturn0search0turn0search13turn0search10.\n\n---\n\n## 🆕 What’s New in the L20 3.0 Series?\n\n### **Shared Features (Boost & Pro)**  \n- **Compact, foldable 20″ step‑through frame** (folds to ~0.3 m³)  \n- **Full suspension**: dual front and rear shock absorbers for maximum comfort  \n- **20″ × 3.0″ tires**, hydraulic disc brakes, Shimano 7‑speed gearing  \n- **Fast 8A charging** (≈2 hours to full battery)  \n- TÜV-certified for EU compliance citeturn0search1turn0search3  \n\n### **L20 3.0 Boost**  \n- **75 Nm Torque Boost mode** (EU-legal 250 W motor)  \n- Up to **135 km range** on pedal assist  \n- Smooth handling via a torque sensor  \n- Early-bird pricing around **€1,299** (regular €1,399) during launch promotions citeturn0search3turn0search5turn0search1  \n\n### **L20 3.0 Pro**  \n- **100 Nm mid-drive motor**, more torque and efficiency  \n- Larger **720 Wh Samsung battery**, up to **160 km range**  \n- **Integrated IoT anti-theft system**: GPS tracking, app control, motion alerts  \n- Regular price around **€1,799** (~€1,699 early-bird) citeturn0search3turn0search4turn0search1  \n\n---\n\n## 🗓 Was It \"in the works\"?  \nYes — the L20 3.0 models were officially announced in **March 2025** and became available to order starting **April 1, 2025** citeturn0search3turn0search13turn0search10.\n\nSo rather than a future model still in development, this generation is **already released and currently purchasable**.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Summary at a Glance\n\n| Model            | Key Highlights                                             | Launch Price     |\n|------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|------------------|\n| **L20 3.0 Boost** | Boost Mode (75 Nm), torque sensor, ~135 km range          | ~€1,299–1,399    |\n| **L20 3.0 Pro**   | 100 Nm mid-drive, GPS theft-prevention, ~160 km range     | ~€1,699–1,799    |\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Which One Should You Consider?\n\n- For a **comfortable, compact urban e-bike with a power boost function and fast charging**, the **L20 3.0 Boost** is a solid option.\n- If you're after **maximum torque, top-tier range, and smart anti-theft features**, the **L20 3.0 Pro** is designed for you.\n\n---\n\nLet me know if you’d like help checking availability and delivery options (e.g. to Letterkenny), or comparing these with other ENGWE models like Engine Pro 2.0 or M20!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
