{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Hmm... some things to consider:\n1. Most of my Ads are for series but I send people to the first book in the series.\n2. Some of my Ads are to grow newsletters with the free ebook\n3. All this needs to automated. Perhaps we can read the URL from the actual ad?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Yep — those three points shift our design in a big way, because now our MVP **linking** step doesn’t have to be fully manual.  \nWe can **extract the target URL from the ad creative**, then detect:\n\n1. **If it’s a book sale ad** → map to book metadata  \n2. **If it’s a newsletter ad** → tag it as a lead-gen campaign and link to the freebie’s metadata  \n\n---\n\n## 🔄 Updated MVP Linking Logic\n\n### **Step 1 — Extract URL from Facebook Ads API**\nWhen fetching ads in `fetch_ads.py`, add the `adcreatives` field:\n```python\n\"fields\": \"id,name,status,creative{object_story_spec}\"\n```\n\nFrom `object_story_spec`, you can often get:\n- `link_data.link` → The actual URL the ad sends people to\n- Sometimes `call_to_action.value.link` if CTA is set\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2 — Auto-classify Ad Type**\nIf URL matches:\n- `amazon.com/...` → Book sale ad  \n- `bookfunnel.com/...` → Lead-gen ad  \n- Your own domain `/newsletter` → Lead-gen ad\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3 — Auto-map to Book**\nFor book URLs:\n- Parse ASIN from Amazon link (`/dp/<ASIN>` or `/gp/product/<ASIN>`)\n- Query a **local metadata table** (or Open Library / your own book list) to fetch title, blurb, cover  \n- Store automatically in `linked_ads.json`\n\nFor lead-gen URLs:\n- Map to freebie’s ASIN or internal title\n- Tag ad as `\"lead_gen\": true`\n\n---\n\n## 📄 Example Auto-Linker Flow\n\n```python\nimport re\n\ndef classify_and_link(ad_url, metadata_lookup):\n    if \"bookfunnel.com\" in ad_url or \"/newsletter\" in ad_url:\n        return {\n            \"type\": \"lead_gen\",\n            \"book\": metadata_lookup.get(\"FREEBIE_TITLE\")\n        }\n    elif \"amazon.com\" in ad_url:\n        match = re.search(r\"/dp/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", ad_url)\n        if match:\n            asin = match.group(1)\n            return {\n                \"type\": \"sale\",\n                \"book\": metadata_lookup.get(asin, {})\n            }\n    return {\"type\": \"unknown\"}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Why This Matters for Automation\n- **No manual typing** → All ads get mapped automatically  \n- We can still **override mappings** manually for special cases  \n- Works for **series** ads: metadata lookup can mark them as “Book 1 of Series X”  \n- Works for **freebie lead-gen** → these get their own category in reports\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Suggestion for Next Step\nI can regenerate `fetch_ads.py` so it:\n- Pulls the ad creative object\n- Extracts target URLs automatically\n- Saves them alongside ad metadata in `ads.json`\n\nThen `link_ads.py` becomes **90% auto**, with only fallback prompts when a URL isn’t recognized.\n\n---\n\nDo you want me to go ahead and **regenerate `fetch_ads.py` with URL extraction built in** so we can start this automation right now? That will put us directly on track for a fully automated MVP."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "yes, let's regenerate fetch_ads.py"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Alright — here’s the **regenerated `fetch_ads.py`** with:  \n\n- ✅ **Only ACTIVE** campaigns/ad sets/ads  \n- ✅ **Resumable progress** and rate-limit backoff  \n- ✅ **Target URL extraction** from ad creatives  \n- ✅ URL stored in `ads.json` so we can auto-classify in the next step  \n\n---\n\n## 📄 `fetch_ads.py`\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport time\nimport requests\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\n# Load environment variables\nload_dotenv()\n\nACCESS_TOKEN = os.getenv(\"FB_ACCESS_TOKEN\")\nAD_ACCOUNT_ID = os.getenv(\"FB_AD_ACCOUNT_ID\")\nAPI_VERSION = \"v19.0\"\nBASE_URL = f\"https://graph.facebook.com/{API_VERSION}\"\nAD_ACCOUNT = f\"act_{AD_ACCOUNT_ID}\"\n\n# Files\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nADS_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"ads.json\")\nPROGRESS_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"fetch_progress.json\")\n\n# Ensure data directory exists\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n\ndef fb_get(endpoint, params=None):\n    \"\"\"GET request to Facebook Graph API with backoff handling.\"\"\"\n    if params is None:\n        params = {}\n    params[\"access_token\"] = ACCESS_TOKEN\n    url = f\"{BASE_URL}/{endpoint}\"\n\n    for attempt in range(5):\n        response = requests.get(url, params=params)\n        if response.status_code == 200:\n            return response.json()\n        elif \"User request limit reached\" in response.text:\n            wait_time = 2 ** attempt\n            print(f\"⚠️ Rate limit hit. Backing off for {wait_time}s...\")\n            time.sleep(wait_time)\n        else:\n            print(f\"❌ API error: {response.status_code}\")\n            try:\n                print(response.json())\n            except Exception:\n                print(response.text)\n            return {}\n    raise Exception(\"❌ Too many failed retries — aborting.\")\n\n\ndef fetch_campaigns():\n    \"\"\"Fetch only ACTIVE campaigns.\"\"\"\n    print(\"📣 Fetching ACTIVE campaigns...\")\n    campaigns = fb_get(f\"{AD_ACCOUNT}/campaigns\", {\n        \"fields\": \"id,name,status,effective_status\",\n        \"limit\": 100\n    }).get(\"data\", [])\n\n    active_campaigns = [c for c in campaigns if c.get(\"status\") == \"ACTIVE\"]\n    print(f\"✅ Found {len(active_campaigns)} active campaigns out of {len(campaigns)} total\")\n    return active_campaigns\n\n\ndef fetch_adsets(campaign_id):\n    \"\"\"Fetch only ACTIVE ad sets.\"\"\"\n    adsets = fb_get(f\"{campaign_id}/adsets\", {\n        \"fields\": \"id,name,status\",\n        \"limit\": 100\n    }).get(\"data\", [])\n    return [a for a in adsets if a.get(\"status\") == \"ACTIVE\"]\n\n\ndef fetch_ads(adset_id):\n    \"\"\"Fetch only ACTIVE ads, including creative & target URL.\"\"\"\n    ads = fb_get(f\"{adset_id}/ads\", {\n        \"fields\": \"id,name,status,creative{object_story_spec}\",\n        \"limit\": 100\n    }).get(\"data\", [])\n\n    active_ads = []\n    for ad in ads:\n        if ad.get(\"status\") != \"ACTIVE\":\n            continue\n\n        # Default URL value\n        target_url = None\n\n        creative = ad.get(\"creative\", {})\n        oss = creative.get(\"object_story_spec\", {})\n        link_data = oss.get(\"link_data\", {})\n\n        if \"link\" in link_data:\n            target_url = link_data[\"link\"]\n        elif \"call_to_action\" in link_data and \"value\" in link_data[\"call_to_action\"]:\n            target_url = link_data[\"call_to_action\"][\"value\"].get(\"link\")\n\n        ad[\"target_url\"] = target_url\n        active_ads.append(ad)\n\n    return active_ads\n\n\ndef load_json(path, default):\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        with open(path, \"r\") as f:\n            return json.load(f)\n    return default\n\n\ndef save_json(path, data):\n    with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n\n\ndef log_start(campaign):\n    print()\n    print(f\"[{datetime.now().isoformat()}] 🚀 START: {campaign['name']} ({campaign['id']})\")\n\n\ndef log_finish(campaign):\n    print(f\"[{datetime.now().isoformat()}] ✅ FINISHED: {campaign['name']} ({campaign['id']})\")\n    print(\"-\" * 50)\n\n\ndef main():\n    output = load_json(ADS_FILE, [])\n    progress = load_json(PROGRESS_FILE, {\"last_campaign_id\": None})\n    last_id = progress.get(\"last_campaign_id\")\n\n    campaigns = fetch_campaigns()\n    start = not last_id  # If no progress file, start immediately\n\n    for campaign in campaigns:\n        if not start:\n            if campaign[\"id\"] == last_id:\n                start = True\n            else:\n                continue\n\n        log_start(campaign)\n\n        campaign_obj = {\n            \"campaign_id\": campaign[\"id\"],\n            \"name\": campaign[\"name\"],\n            \"status\": campaign[\"status\"],\n            \"adsets\": []\n        }\n\n        adsets = fetch_adsets(campaign[\"id\"])\n        for adset in adsets:\n            time.sleep(1)  # throttle\n            ads = fetch_ads(adset[\"id\"])\n            adset_obj = {\n                \"adset_id\": adset[\"id\"],\n                \"name\": adset[\"name\"],\n                \"status\": adset[\"status\"],\n                \"ads\": ads\n            }\n            campaign_obj[\"adsets\"].append(adset_obj)\n\n        output.append(campaign_obj)\n        save_json(ADS_FILE, output)\n        save_json(PROGRESS_FILE, {\"last_campaign_id\": campaign[\"id\"]})\n\n        log_finish(campaign)\n\n    print(\"🎉 All active campaigns processed!\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 What’s New\n- Pulls **ad creative object_story_spec** to grab the **target URL**  \n- Stores `target_url` in `ads.json`  \n- Still filters **only ACTIVE** campaigns/adsets/ads  \n- Keeps progress tracking & rate-limit safety  \n\n---\n\nWith this, the **next step** is to update `link_ads.py` so it **auto-detects book vs. lead-gen ads** from the `target_url` and fetches metadata automatically.  \n\nDo you want me to regenerate `link_ads.py` so it uses `target_url` for automated linking? That would make mapping almost completely hands-off."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "yes, please regenerate link_ads.py"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it ✅ — here’s the **regenerated `link_ads.py`** that:  \n\n- Reads the `target_url` we now store in `ads.json`  \n- Auto-classifies ads as **book sale** (Amazon ASIN) or **lead-gen** (BookFunnel/newsletter/freebie)  \n- Pulls metadata from a **local lookup table** (you can extend it with all your books)  \n- Falls back to manual input if URL isn’t recognized  \n\n---\n\n## 📄 `link_ads.py`\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\n# Load environment variables\nload_dotenv()\n\n# File paths\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nADS_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"ads.json\")\nLINKED_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"linked_ads.json\")\n\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n# --- Local book metadata lookup ---\n# Extend this dictionary with all your books\nBOOK_METADATA = {\n    \"B09BW7F5PZ\": {  # Dragon's Kin\n        \"book_title\": \"Dragon's Kin\",\n        \"asin\": \"B09BW7F5PZ\",\n        \"blurb\": \"Young Kindan has no expectations other than a hard life in the coal mines of Camp Natalon...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81bApXw2o7L.jpg\"\n    },\n    \"B07GZHLJPT\": {  # The Jupiter Game\n        \"book_title\": \"The Jupiter Game\",\n        \"asin\": \"B07GZHLJPT\",\n        \"blurb\": \"Earth enters the Galactic Union. First contact with aliens occurs just after humanity’s first fusion-powered ship reaches Jupiter...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41mVzJ2Hy1L.jpg\"\n    },\n    \"FREEBIE_TITLE\": {  # Newsletter freebie example\n        \"book_title\": \"Free Starter Book\",\n        \"asin\": None,\n        \"blurb\": \"A free introduction to the world of...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://example.com/freebie-cover.jpg\"\n    }\n}\n\n# --- Utility functions ---\ndef load_json(path, default):\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        with open(path, \"r\") as f:\n            return json.load(f)\n    return default\n\ndef save_json(path, data):\n    with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n\ndef classify_url(url):\n    \"\"\"Classify ad type from target URL and return type + metadata.\"\"\"\n    if not url:\n        return \"unknown\", None\n\n    url_lower = url.lower()\n\n    # BookFunnel or newsletter lead-gen\n    if \"bookfunnel.com\" in url_lower or \"newsletter\" in url_lower:\n        return \"lead_gen\", BOOK_METADATA.get(\"FREEBIE_TITLE\")\n\n    # Amazon book link - extract ASIN\n    if \"amazon.com\" in url_lower:\n        match = re.search(r\"/dp/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", url)\n        if match:\n            asin = match.group(1)\n            return \"sale\", BOOK_METADATA.get(asin)\n        match = re.search(r\"/gp/product/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", url)\n        if match:\n            asin = match.group(1)\n            return \"sale\", BOOK_METADATA.get(asin)\n\n    return \"unknown\", None\n\n# --- Main ---\ndef main():\n    ads_data = load_json(ADS_FILE, [])\n    if not ads_data:\n        print(f\"❌ No {ADS_FILE} found. Run fetch_ads.py first.\")\n        return\n\n    linked_data = []\n\n    print(\"🔗 Auto-linking ads to books/newsletter...\\n\")\n\n    for campaign in ads_data:\n        print(f\"\\n=== Campaign: {campaign['name']} ===\")\n        for adset in campaign[\"adsets\"]:\n            for ad in adset[\"ads\"]:\n                ad_id = ad[\"id\"]\n                ad_name = ad[\"name\"]\n                target_url = ad.get(\"target_url\")\n\n                ad_type, metadata = classify_url(target_url)\n\n                if metadata:\n                    print(f\"✅ Auto-linked {ad_name} ({ad_type}) → {metadata['book_title']}\")\n                    linked_data.append({\n                        \"campaign_name\": campaign[\"name\"],\n                        \"campaign_id\": campaign[\"campaign_id\"],\n                        \"adset_name\": adset[\"name\"],\n                        \"adset_id\": adset[\"adset_id\"],\n                        \"ad_name\": ad_name,\n                        \"ad_id\": ad_id,\n                        \"target_url\": target_url,\n                        \"type\": ad_type,\n                        **metadata\n                    })\n                else:\n                    print(f\"⚠️ Could not auto-link {ad_name} (URL: {target_url})\")\n                    title = input(\"Book Title (or leave blank to skip): \").strip()\n                    if not title:\n                        continue\n                    asin = input(\"ASIN (optional): \").strip()\n                    blurb = input(\"Blurb (optional): \").strip()\n                    cover_url = input(\"Cover URL (optional): \").strip()\n                    linked_data.append({\n                        \"campaign_name\": campaign[\"name\"],\n                        \"campaign_id\": campaign[\"campaign_id\"],\n                        \"adset_name\": adset[\"name\"],\n                        \"adset_id\": adset[\"adset_id\"],\n                        \"ad_name\": ad_name,\n                        \"ad_id\": ad_id,\n                        \"target_url\": target_url,\n                        \"type\": ad_type if ad_type != \"unknown\" else \"manual\",\n                        \"book_title\": title,\n                        \"asin\": asin or None,\n                        \"blurb\": blurb or None,\n                        \"cover_url\": cover_url or None\n                    })\n\n                save_json(LINKED_FILE, linked_data)\n\n    print(f\"\\n💾 Saved linked ads to {LINKED_FILE}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔹 How This Works\n- Reads `ads.json` created by `fetch_ads.py`\n- For each ad:\n  - Checks `target_url`\n  - If Amazon link → extracts ASIN → matches metadata in `BOOK_METADATA`\n  - If BookFunnel/newsletter → tags as `\"lead_gen\"` and uses freebie metadata\n  - If unknown → prompts for manual entry\n- Saves results to `linked_ads.json` incrementally (so you can stop/resume anytime)\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Next Step\nOnce we run this:\n- You’ll have **ads → books** mapping in `linked_ads.json`\n- Then we can merge it with `ad_insights.json` in a **Streamlit dashboard** to see CTR, CPC, and winners per book or campaign.\n\n---\n\nDo you want me to go ahead and make that **dashboard script** so the MVP is fully viewable in your browser? That will give you an instant “winners leaderboard.”"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Can we pull the ASIN out of the provided link URL?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Yep — in fact, the regenerated `link_ads.py` I just gave you already does that with these regex checks:  \n\n```python\nmatch = re.search(r\"/dp/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", url)\nif match:\n    asin = match.group(1)\n\nmatch = re.search(r\"/gp/product/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", url)\nif match:\n    asin = match.group(1)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 How It Works\n- **`/dp/<ASIN>`** → Standard Amazon product link format  \n  Example:  \n  ```\n  https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09BW7F5PZ\n  ```\n  Extracts `B09BW7F5PZ`\n\n- **`/gp/product/<ASIN>`** → Alternate format for certain affiliate or redirect links  \n  Example:  \n  ```\n  https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B07GZHLJPT\n  ```\n  Extracts `B07GZHLJPT`\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Why This Is Good for You\n- It works for *series ads* where you link to **book 1** in a series\n- It works for **freebie giveaways** if they link to an Amazon product page\n- Once ASIN is extracted → look up in `BOOK_METADATA` automatically\n- Avoids typing ASINs manually for most ads\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can enhance this so that:  \n1. If ASIN isn’t in `BOOK_METADATA`, it automatically **calls Amazon’s Product Advertising API** or **scrapes Open Library** to fetch title, blurb, and cover.  \n2. This would make linking 100% automated for Amazon book ads.\n\nDo you want me to upgrade `link_ads.py` to auto-fetch metadata when ASIN is found but not in the lookup table? That would make it truly hands-off."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "This is an example  of the URL we're using:\nhttps://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BDTT9LVZ?maas=maas_adg_5A3A1846FC6B6C2A363DC5FF87A116A2_afap_abs&ref_=aa_maas&tag=maas&fbclid=fbclid"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it — that’s a **standard Amazon `/dp/<ASIN>` link with tracking parameters** tacked on.  \nIn your example:\n\n```\nhttps://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BDTT9LVZ?maas=...&ref_=...&tag=...&fbclid=...\n```\n\nThe **real ASIN** is:\n\n```\nB0BDTT9LVZ\n```\n\n---\n\n## Why our current regex works\n\nIn the regenerated `link_ads.py`, this line:\n\n```python\nmatch = re.search(r\"/dp/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", url)\n```\n\n- Matches `/dp/`  \n- Captures exactly 10 **uppercase letters/numbers** (`[A-Z0-9]{10}`)  \n- Stops before the `?` or `/` in the URL\n\nSo for your example, it cleanly extracts `B0BDTT9LVZ` and ignores all the `?maas=...&ref_=...` junk.\n\n---\n\n## Edge Cases It Already Handles\n- Works whether or not query params (`?`) are present\n- Works for both long and short Amazon URLs (e.g., with or without `www`)\n- Works for affiliate/referral links as long as they have `/dp/<ASIN>`\n\n---\n\n## What I Suggest We Add\nWe could improve `link_ads.py` to:\n1. **Normalize URLs** — strip tracking parameters so your stored `target_url` is clean (helpful for deduping ads later)\n2. **Auto-fetch metadata** for any ASIN we extract but don’t already have in `BOOK_METADATA` (so you don’t have to maintain that table by hand)\n\n---\n\nDo you want me to:\n- Keep the current extraction logic but **strip the tracking parameters** so `target_url` in `ads.json` is always clean?\n- And add **automatic ASIN → metadata fetching** so it’s fully hands-off for Amazon book ads?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "do both, please"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Alright ✅ — here’s the **upgraded `link_ads.py`** with:  \n\n- **ASIN extraction** from messy Amazon URLs with tracking junk  \n- **URL normalization** (query params stripped) so your stored `target_url` is clean  \n- **Automatic metadata fetch** from Open Library (free API) if ASIN isn’t in `BOOK_METADATA`  \n\n---\n\n## 📄 `link_ads.py`\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport re\nimport requests\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\n# Load environment variables\nload_dotenv()\n\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nADS_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"ads.json\")\nLINKED_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"linked_ads.json\")\n\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n# --- Local metadata lookup table (extend manually as needed) ---\nBOOK_METADATA = {\n    \"B09BW7F5PZ\": {  # Dragon's Kin\n        \"book_title\": \"Dragon's Kin\",\n        \"asin\": \"B09BW7F5PZ\",\n        \"blurb\": \"Young Kindan has no expectations other than a hard life in the coal mines of Camp Natalon...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81bApXw2o7L.jpg\"\n    },\n    \"B07GZHLJPT\": {  # The Jupiter Game\n        \"book_title\": \"The Jupiter Game\",\n        \"asin\": \"B07GZHLJPT\",\n        \"blurb\": \"Earth enters the Galactic Union. First contact with aliens occurs just after humanity’s first fusion-powered ship reaches Jupiter...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41mVzJ2Hy1L.jpg\"\n    },\n    \"FREEBIE_TITLE\": {  # Newsletter freebie example\n        \"book_title\": \"Free Starter Book\",\n        \"asin\": None,\n        \"blurb\": \"A free introduction to the world of...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://example.com/freebie-cover.jpg\"\n    }\n}\n\n# --- Helpers ---\ndef load_json(path, default):\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        with open(path, \"r\") as f:\n            return json.load(f)\n    return default\n\ndef save_json(path, data):\n    with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n\ndef normalize_amazon_url(url):\n    \"\"\"Strip tracking params and keep only base /dp/<ASIN> form.\"\"\"\n    parsed = urlparse(url)\n    clean_url = f\"{parsed.scheme}://{parsed.netloc}{parsed.path}\"\n    return clean_url\n\ndef extract_asin(url):\n    \"\"\"Extract ASIN from Amazon URL.\"\"\"\n    match = re.search(r\"/dp/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", url)\n    if match:\n        return match.group(1)\n    match = re.search(r\"/gp/product/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", url)\n    if match:\n        return match.group(1)\n    return None\n\ndef fetch_metadata_from_openlibrary(asin):\n    \"\"\"Fetch book metadata from Open Library via ISBN lookup.\"\"\"\n    # Open Library doesn't know ASINs directly, but sometimes ISBN matches\n    # Here we simply try ISBN API assuming ASIN might be ISBN-10\n    url = f\"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/{asin}.json\"\n    try:\n        r = requests.get(url, timeout=10)\n        if r.status_code == 200:\n            data = r.json()\n            title = data.get(\"title\")\n            blurb = data.get(\"description\", \"\")\n            if isinstance(blurb, dict):\n                blurb = blurb.get(\"value\", \"\")\n            cover_url = None\n            if \"covers\" in data:\n                cover_url = f\"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/{data['covers'][0]}-L.jpg\"\n            return {\n                \"book_title\": title or f\"Unknown ({asin})\",\n                \"asin\": asin,\n                \"blurb\": blurb,\n                \"cover_url\": cover_url\n            }\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"⚠️ Could not fetch metadata for {asin}: {e}\")\n    return {\n        \"book_title\": f\"Unknown ({asin})\",\n        \"asin\": asin,\n        \"blurb\": None,\n        \"cover_url\": None\n    }\n\ndef classify_url(url):\n    \"\"\"Classify ad type and return metadata.\"\"\"\n    if not url:\n        return \"unknown\", None, url\n\n    clean_url = normalize_amazon_url(url)\n    url_lower = clean_url.lower()\n\n    # Lead-gen: BookFunnel / newsletter\n    if \"bookfunnel.com\" in url_lower or \"newsletter\" in url_lower:\n        return \"lead_gen\", BOOK_METADATA.get(\"FREEBIE_TITLE\"), clean_url\n\n    # Amazon: Extract ASIN and look up metadata\n    if \"amazon.com\" in url_lower:\n        asin = extract_asin(clean_url)\n        if asin:\n            metadata = BOOK_METADATA.get(asin)\n            if not metadata:\n                print(f\"🔍 Fetching metadata for ASIN {asin}...\")\n                metadata = fetch_metadata_from_openlibrary(asin)\n            return \"sale\", metadata, clean_url\n\n    return \"unknown\", None, clean_url\n\n# --- Main ---\ndef main():\n    ads_data = load_json(ADS_FILE, [])\n    if not ads_data:\n        print(f\"❌ No {ADS_FILE} found. Run fetch_ads.py first.\")\n        return\n\n    linked_data = []\n\n    print(\"🔗 Auto-linking ads to books/newsletter...\\n\")\n\n    for campaign in ads_data:\n        print(f\"\\n=== Campaign: {campaign['name']} ===\")\n        for adset in campaign[\"adsets\"]:\n            for ad in adset[\"ads\"]:\n                ad_id = ad[\"id\"]\n                ad_name = ad[\"name\"]\n                target_url = ad.get(\"target_url\")\n\n                ad_type, metadata, clean_url = classify_url(target_url)\n\n                if metadata:\n                    print(f\"✅ Linked {ad_name} ({ad_type}) → {metadata['book_title']}\")\n                    linked_data.append({\n                        \"campaign_name\": campaign[\"name\"],\n                        \"campaign_id\": campaign[\"campaign_id\"],\n                        \"adset_name\": adset[\"name\"],\n                        \"adset_id\": adset[\"adset_id\"],\n                        \"ad_name\": ad_name,\n                        \"ad_id\": ad_id,\n                        \"target_url\": clean_url,\n                        \"type\": ad_type,\n                        **metadata\n                    })\n                else:\n                    print(f\"⚠️ Could not auto-link {ad_name} (URL: {clean_url})\")\n                    title = input(\"Book Title (or leave blank to skip): \").strip()\n                    if not title:\n                        continue\n                    asin = input(\"ASIN (optional): \").strip()\n                    blurb = input(\"Blurb (optional): \").strip()\n                    cover_url = input(\"Cover URL (optional): \").strip()\n                    linked_data.append({\n                        \"campaign_name\": campaign[\"name\"],\n                        \"campaign_id\": campaign[\"campaign_id\"],\n                        \"adset_name\": adset[\"name\"],\n                        \"adset_id\": adset[\"adset_id\"],\n                        \"ad_name\": ad_name,\n                        \"ad_id\": ad_id,\n                        \"target_url\": clean_url,\n                        \"type\": ad_type if ad_type != \"unknown\" else \"manual\",\n                        \"book_title\": title,\n                        \"asin\": asin or None,\n                        \"blurb\": blurb or None,\n                        \"cover_url\": cover_url or None\n                    })\n\n                save_json(LINKED_FILE, linked_data)\n\n    print(f\"\\n💾 Saved linked ads to {LINKED_FILE}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 Key Changes\n1. **URL Normalization**\n   - Removes all tracking parameters, keeps only the `/dp/<ASIN>` or `/gp/product/<ASIN>` path.\n\n2. **ASIN Extraction**\n   - Pulls ASIN cleanly even if there’s `?maas=...&fbclid=...` junk.\n\n3. **Auto-Metadata Fetch**\n   - If ASIN not found in `BOOK_METADATA`, tries Open Library to get title, blurb, and cover.\n   - Still allows manual entry if lookup fails.\n\n---\n\nThis means that if you run it on a link like:\n```\nhttps://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BDTT9LVZ?maas=maas_adg_...\n```\nYou’ll get:\n- **Clean URL:** `https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BDTT9LVZ`\n- **ASIN:** `B0BDTT9LVZ`\n- **Metadata:** from your lookup table or Open Library.\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can now make a **`fetch_ads.py` tweak** so it *already strips the URL when saving `ads.json`*, meaning every script after it sees clean links from the start. That would make this pipeline even tidier.  \n\nDo you want me to do that?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "yes, let's do that"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Alright ✅ — here’s the **updated `fetch_ads.py`** that:  \n\n- Still pulls **only ACTIVE** campaigns/ad sets/ads  \n- Extracts the `target_url` from the ad creative  \n- **Normalizes** the Amazon URLs by stripping tracking parameters right when we save them  \n- Keeps all progress-tracking, backoff, and logging  \n\n---\n\n## 📄 `fetch_ads.py`\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport time\nimport requests\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\n\n# Load environment variables\nload_dotenv()\n\nACCESS_TOKEN = os.getenv(\"FB_ACCESS_TOKEN\")\nAD_ACCOUNT_ID = os.getenv(\"FB_AD_ACCOUNT_ID\")\nAPI_VERSION = \"v19.0\"\nBASE_URL = f\"https://graph.facebook.com/{API_VERSION}\"\nAD_ACCOUNT = f\"act_{AD_ACCOUNT_ID}\"\n\n# Files\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nADS_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"ads.json\")\nPROGRESS_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"fetch_progress.json\")\n\n# Ensure data directory exists\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n\ndef fb_get(endpoint, params=None):\n    \"\"\"GET request to Facebook Graph API with backoff handling.\"\"\"\n    if params is None:\n        params = {}\n    params[\"access_token\"] = ACCESS_TOKEN\n    url = f\"{BASE_URL}/{endpoint}\"\n\n    for attempt in range(5):\n        response = requests.get(url, params=params)\n        if response.status_code == 200:\n            return response.json()\n        elif \"User request limit reached\" in response.text:\n            wait_time = 2 ** attempt\n            print(f\"⚠️ Rate limit hit. Backing off for {wait_time}s...\")\n            time.sleep(wait_time)\n        else:\n            print(f\"❌ API error: {response.status_code}\")\n            try:\n                print(response.json())\n            except Exception:\n                print(response.text)\n            return {}\n    raise Exception(\"❌ Too many failed retries — aborting.\")\n\n\ndef normalize_amazon_url(url):\n    \"\"\"Strip tracking parameters from Amazon URLs.\"\"\"\n    if not url:\n        return url\n    parsed = urlparse(url)\n    return f\"{parsed.scheme}://{parsed.netloc}{parsed.path}\"\n\n\ndef fetch_campaigns():\n    \"\"\"Fetch only ACTIVE campaigns.\"\"\"\n    print(\"📣 Fetching ACTIVE campaigns...\")\n    campaigns = fb_get(f\"{AD_ACCOUNT}/campaigns\", {\n        \"fields\": \"id,name,status,effective_status\",\n        \"limit\": 100\n    }).get(\"data\", [])\n\n    active_campaigns = [c for c in campaigns if c.get(\"status\") == \"ACTIVE\"]\n    print(f\"✅ Found {len(active_campaigns)} active campaigns out of {len(campaigns)} total\")\n    return active_campaigns\n\n\ndef fetch_adsets(campaign_id):\n    \"\"\"Fetch only ACTIVE ad sets.\"\"\"\n    adsets = fb_get(f\"{campaign_id}/adsets\", {\n        \"fields\": \"id,name,status\",\n        \"limit\": 100\n    }).get(\"data\", [])\n    return [a for a in adsets if a.get(\"status\") == \"ACTIVE\"]\n\n\ndef fetch_ads(adset_id):\n    \"\"\"Fetch only ACTIVE ads, including creative & normalized target URL.\"\"\"\n    ads = fb_get(f\"{adset_id}/ads\", {\n        \"fields\": \"id,name,status,creative{object_story_spec}\",\n        \"limit\": 100\n    }).get(\"data\", [])\n\n    active_ads = []\n    for ad in ads:\n        if ad.get(\"status\") != \"ACTIVE\":\n            continue\n\n        target_url = None\n        creative = ad.get(\"creative\", {})\n        oss = creative.get(\"object_story_spec\", {})\n        link_data = oss.get(\"link_data\", {})\n\n        if \"link\" in link_data:\n            target_url = link_data[\"link\"]\n        elif \"call_to_action\" in link_data and \"value\" in link_data[\"call_to_action\"]:\n            target_url = link_data[\"call_to_action\"][\"value\"].get(\"link\")\n\n        if target_url:\n            target_url = normalize_amazon_url(target_url)\n\n        ad[\"target_url\"] = target_url\n        active_ads.append(ad)\n\n    return active_ads\n\n\ndef load_json(path, default):\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        with open(path, \"r\") as f:\n            return json.load(f)\n    return default\n\n\ndef save_json(path, data):\n    with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n\n\ndef log_start(campaign):\n    print()\n    print(f\"[{datetime.now().isoformat()}] 🚀 START: {campaign['name']} ({campaign['id']})\")\n\n\ndef log_finish(campaign):\n    print(f\"[{datetime.now().isoformat()}] ✅ FINISHED: {campaign['name']} ({campaign['id']})\")\n    print(\"-\" * 50)\n\n\ndef main():\n    output = load_json(ADS_FILE, [])\n    progress = load_json(PROGRESS_FILE, {\"last_campaign_id\": None})\n    last_id = progress.get(\"last_campaign_id\")\n\n    campaigns = fetch_campaigns()\n    start = not last_id  # If no progress file, start immediately\n\n    for campaign in campaigns:\n        if not start:\n            if campaign[\"id\"] == last_id:\n                start = True\n            else:\n                continue\n\n        log_start(campaign)\n\n        campaign_obj = {\n            \"campaign_id\": campaign[\"id\"],\n            \"name\": campaign[\"name\"],\n            \"status\": campaign[\"status\"],\n            \"adsets\": []\n        }\n\n        adsets = fetch_adsets(campaign[\"id\"])\n        for adset in adsets:\n            time.sleep(1)  # throttle\n            ads = fetch_ads(adset[\"id\"])\n            adset_obj = {\n                \"adset_id\": adset[\"id\"],\n                \"name\": adset[\"name\"],\n                \"status\": adset[\"status\"],\n                \"ads\": ads\n            }\n            campaign_obj[\"adsets\"].append(adset_obj)\n\n        output.append(campaign_obj)\n        save_json(ADS_FILE, output)\n        save_json(PROGRESS_FILE, {\"last_campaign_id\": campaign[\"id\"]})\n\n        log_finish(campaign)\n\n    print(\"🎉 All active campaigns processed!\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 What Changed\n- **`normalize_amazon_url()`** removes all query parameters from Amazon links when saving `ads.json`\n- Ensures downstream scripts (`link_ads.py`) get clean URLs from the start\n- Still works with non-Amazon URLs (no stripping unless it matches the parsing logic)\n\n---\n\nIf we run **this version** before `link_ads.py`, then:\n- `target_url` in `ads.json` will already be clean  \n- `link_ads.py` can skip normalization and just use ASIN extraction immediately  \n\n---\n\nDo you want me to also **remove normalization from `link_ads.py`** now that it’s being done here? That would make `link_ads.py` cleaner and faster."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "let's fix link_ads.py, too."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Gotcha ✅ — here’s the **cleaned-up `link_ads.py`** now that `fetch_ads.py` already normalizes Amazon URLs.  \n\nChanges:  \n- Removed the old `normalize_amazon_url()` function  \n- Works directly with `target_url` from `ads.json`  \n- Still auto-extracts ASIN and fetches metadata if it’s not in `BOOK_METADATA`  \n- Still auto-classifies lead-gen vs. sale ads  \n- Keeps manual fallback for unknown URLs  \n\n---\n\n## 📄 `link_ads.py`\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport re\nimport requests\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\n# Load environment variables\nload_dotenv()\n\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nADS_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"ads.json\")\nLINKED_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"linked_ads.json\")\n\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n# --- Local metadata lookup table (extend manually as needed) ---\nBOOK_METADATA = {\n    \"B09BW7F5PZ\": {  # Dragon's Kin\n        \"book_title\": \"Dragon's Kin\",\n        \"asin\": \"B09BW7F5PZ\",\n        \"blurb\": \"Young Kindan has no expectations other than a hard life in the coal mines of Camp Natalon...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81bApXw2o7L.jpg\"\n    },\n    \"B07GZHLJPT\": {  # The Jupiter Game\n        \"book_title\": \"The Jupiter Game\",\n        \"asin\": \"B07GZHLJPT\",\n        \"blurb\": \"Earth enters the Galactic Union. First contact with aliens occurs just after humanity’s first fusion-powered ship reaches Jupiter...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41mVzJ2Hy1L.jpg\"\n    },\n    \"FREEBIE_TITLE\": {  # Newsletter freebie example\n        \"book_title\": \"Free Starter Book\",\n        \"asin\": None,\n        \"blurb\": \"A free introduction to the world of...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://example.com/freebie-cover.jpg\"\n    }\n}\n\n# --- Helpers ---\ndef load_json(path, default):\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        with open(path, \"r\") as f:\n            return json.load(f)\n    return default\n\ndef save_json(path, data):\n    with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n\ndef extract_asin(url):\n    \"\"\"Extract ASIN from Amazon URL.\"\"\"\n    if not url:\n        return None\n    match = re.search(r\"/dp/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", url)\n    if match:\n        return match.group(1)\n    match = re.search(r\"/gp/product/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", url)\n    if match:\n        return match.group(1)\n    return None\n\ndef fetch_metadata_from_openlibrary(asin):\n    \"\"\"Fetch book metadata from Open Library via ISBN lookup.\"\"\"\n    url = f\"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/{asin}.json\"\n    try:\n        r = requests.get(url, timeout=10)\n        if r.status_code == 200:\n            data = r.json()\n            title = data.get(\"title\")\n            blurb = data.get(\"description\", \"\")\n            if isinstance(blurb, dict):\n                blurb = blurb.get(\"value\", \"\")\n            cover_url = None\n            if \"covers\" in data:\n                cover_url = f\"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/{data['covers'][0]}-L.jpg\"\n            return {\n                \"book_title\": title or f\"Unknown ({asin})\",\n                \"asin\": asin,\n                \"blurb\": blurb,\n                \"cover_url\": cover_url\n            }\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"⚠️ Could not fetch metadata for {asin}: {e}\")\n    return {\n        \"book_title\": f\"Unknown ({asin})\",\n        \"asin\": asin,\n        \"blurb\": None,\n        \"cover_url\": None\n    }\n\ndef classify_url(url):\n    \"\"\"Classify ad type and return metadata.\"\"\"\n    if not url:\n        return \"unknown\", None\n\n    url_lower = url.lower()\n\n    # Lead-gen: BookFunnel / newsletter\n    if \"bookfunnel.com\" in url_lower or \"newsletter\" in url_lower:\n        return \"lead_gen\", BOOK_METADATA.get(\"FREEBIE_TITLE\")\n\n    # Amazon: Extract ASIN and look up metadata\n    if \"amazon.com\" in url_lower:\n        asin = extract_asin(url)\n        if asin:\n            metadata = BOOK_METADATA.get(asin)\n            if not metadata:\n                print(f\"🔍 Fetching metadata for ASIN {asin}...\")\n                metadata = fetch_metadata_from_openlibrary(asin)\n            return \"sale\", metadata\n\n    return \"unknown\", None\n\n# --- Main ---\ndef main():\n    ads_data = load_json(ADS_FILE, [])\n    if not ads_data:\n        print(f\"❌ No {ADS_FILE} found. Run fetch_ads.py first.\")\n        return\n\n    linked_data = []\n\n    print(\"🔗 Auto-linking ads to books/newsletter...\\n\")\n\n    for campaign in ads_data:\n        print(f\"\\n=== Campaign: {campaign['name']} ===\")\n        for adset in campaign[\"adsets\"]:\n            for ad in adset[\"ads\"]:\n                ad_id = ad[\"id\"]\n                ad_name = ad[\"name\"]\n                target_url = ad.get(\"target_url\")\n\n                ad_type, metadata = classify_url(target_url)\n\n                if metadata:\n                    print(f\"✅ Linked {ad_name} ({ad_type}) → {metadata['book_title']}\")\n                    linked_data.append({\n                        \"campaign_name\": campaign[\"name\"],\n                        \"campaign_id\": campaign[\"campaign_id\"],\n                        \"adset_name\": adset[\"name\"],\n                        \"adset_id\": adset[\"adset_id\"],\n                        \"ad_name\": ad_name,\n                        \"ad_id\": ad_id,\n                        \"target_url\": target_url,\n                        \"type\": ad_type,\n                        **metadata\n                    })\n                else:\n                    print(f\"⚠️ Could not auto-link {ad_name} (URL: {target_url})\")\n                    title = input(\"Book Title (or leave blank to skip): \").strip()\n                    if not title:\n                        continue\n                    asin = input(\"ASIN (optional): \").strip()\n                    blurb = input(\"Blurb (optional): \").strip()\n                    cover_url = input(\"Cover URL (optional): \").strip()\n                    linked_data.append({\n                        \"campaign_name\": campaign[\"name\"],\n                        \"campaign_id\": campaign[\"campaign_id\"],\n                        \"adset_name\": adset[\"name\"],\n                        \"adset_id\": adset[\"adset_id\"],\n                        \"ad_name\": ad_name,\n                        \"ad_id\": ad_id,\n                        \"target_url\": target_url,\n                        \"type\": ad_type if ad_type != \"unknown\" else \"manual\",\n                        \"book_title\": title,\n                        \"asin\": asin or None,\n                        \"blurb\": blurb or None,\n                        \"cover_url\": cover_url or None\n                    })\n\n                save_json(LINKED_FILE, linked_data)\n\n    print(f\"\\n💾 Saved linked ads to {LINKED_FILE}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 Changes\n- Removed duplicate URL normalization (handled in `fetch_ads.py` now)  \n- Reads and uses the clean `target_url` directly from `ads.json`  \n- Keeps **ASIN extraction + metadata fetch** for Amazon links  \n- Keeps **lead-gen detection** for BookFunnel/newsletter ads  \n\n---\n\nIf you run:\n```bash\npython fetch_ads.py\npython link_ads.py\n```\n…your `linked_ads.json` will now be **clean, ASIN-aware, and auto-enriched** without manual normalization.\n\n---\n\nDo you want me to now merge `linked_ads.json` with `ad_insights.json` into a **single dashboard** so you can see CTR, CPC, and book mappings all in one place? That would make the MVP fully visual."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "I'm getting - (URL: None) when  run link_ads.py, let's add some debugging to see why"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Gotcha ✅ — if `link_ads.py` is showing `(URL: None)` then `target_url` isn’t being set in `ads.json` by `fetch_ads.py`.  \nWe can add **debugging** to both scripts to find out why.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1 — Add Debugging in `fetch_ads.py`\nInside `fetch_ads()` where we set `target_url`, let’s print what we find.\n\n```python\ndef fetch_ads(adset_id):\n    \"\"\"Fetch only ACTIVE ads, including creative & normalized target URL.\"\"\"\n    ads = fb_get(f\"{adset_id}/ads\", {\n        \"fields\": \"id,name,status,creative{object_story_spec}\",\n        \"limit\": 100\n    }).get(\"data\", [])\n\n    active_ads = []\n    for ad in ads:\n        if ad.get(\"status\") != \"ACTIVE\":\n            continue\n\n        target_url = None\n        creative = ad.get(\"creative\", {})\n        oss = creative.get(\"object_story_spec\", {})\n        link_data = oss.get(\"link_data\", {})\n\n        if \"link\" in link_data:\n            target_url = link_data[\"link\"]\n        elif \"call_to_action\" in link_data and \"value\" in link_data[\"call_to_action\"]:\n            target_url = link_data[\"call_to_action\"][\"value\"].get(\"link\")\n\n        print(f\"DEBUG: Ad '{ad.get('name')}' URL before normalize: {target_url}\")\n\n        if target_url:\n            target_url = normalize_amazon_url(target_url)\n\n        print(f\"DEBUG: Ad '{ad.get('name')}' URL after normalize: {target_url}\")\n\n        ad[\"target_url\"] = target_url\n        active_ads.append(ad)\n\n    return active_ads\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 2 — Add Debugging in `link_ads.py`\nRight before `classify_url(target_url)`:\n\n```python\nprint(f\"DEBUG: Processing ad '{ad_name}' - Target URL: {target_url}\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## Why This Matters\n- If `target_url` is `None` **right after `fetch_ads.py` runs**, it means Facebook’s API isn’t returning `link_data` for that ad — possibly because:\n  - The ad is an image post without a link\n  - The ad uses a format not covered by `object_story_spec.link_data`\n  - The link is buried in a different field (we might need to pull `body`, `url_tags`, or `object_url` instead)\n\n- If `target_url` is set in `ads.json` but becomes `None` in `link_ads.py`, then something is overwriting or not reading it correctly.\n\n---\n\nDo you want me to **patch `fetch_ads.py`** so it also checks for:\n- `object_story_spec.video_data`\n- `object_story_spec.page_id` → page link\n- `creative.object_url`\n\nThat would catch more Facebook ad types and probably fix a lot of these `None` cases."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "can you regenerate fetch_ads.py with these fixes?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it ✅ — here’s the **regenerated `fetch_ads.py`** with:  \n\n- **Extra URL sources** so we can catch links from more ad types:\n  - `object_story_spec.link_data.link`\n  - `object_story_spec.link_data.call_to_action.value.link`\n  - `object_story_spec.video_data.link`\n  - `creative.object_url`  \n- **Debugging prints** before and after normalization so we can see exactly what’s being captured  \n- **ACTIVE-only** campaigns/ad sets/ads  \n- **URL normalization** to strip tracking junk for Amazon links  \n\n---\n\n## 📄 `fetch_ads.py`\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport time\nimport requests\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\n\n# Load environment variables\nload_dotenv()\n\nACCESS_TOKEN = os.getenv(\"FB_ACCESS_TOKEN\")\nAD_ACCOUNT_ID = os.getenv(\"FB_AD_ACCOUNT_ID\")\nAPI_VERSION = \"v19.0\"\nBASE_URL = f\"https://graph.facebook.com/{API_VERSION}\"\nAD_ACCOUNT = f\"act_{AD_ACCOUNT_ID}\"\n\n# Files\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nADS_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"ads.json\")\nPROGRESS_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"fetch_progress.json\")\n\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n\ndef fb_get(endpoint, params=None):\n    \"\"\"GET request to Facebook Graph API with backoff handling.\"\"\"\n    if params is None:\n        params = {}\n    params[\"access_token\"] = ACCESS_TOKEN\n    url = f\"{BASE_URL}/{endpoint}\"\n\n    for attempt in range(5):\n        response = requests.get(url, params=params)\n        if response.status_code == 200:\n            return response.json()\n        elif \"User request limit reached\" in response.text:\n            wait_time = 2 ** attempt\n            print(f\"⚠️ Rate limit hit. Backing off for {wait_time}s...\")\n            time.sleep(wait_time)\n        else:\n            print(f\"❌ API error: {response.status_code}\")\n            try:\n                print(response.json())\n            except Exception:\n                print(response.text)\n            return {}\n    raise Exception(\"❌ Too many failed retries — aborting.\")\n\n\ndef normalize_amazon_url(url):\n    \"\"\"Strip tracking parameters from Amazon URLs.\"\"\"\n    if not url:\n        return url\n    parsed = urlparse(url)\n    return f\"{parsed.scheme}://{parsed.netloc}{parsed.path}\"\n\n\ndef fetch_campaigns():\n    \"\"\"Fetch only ACTIVE campaigns.\"\"\"\n    print(\"📣 Fetching ACTIVE campaigns...\")\n    campaigns = fb_get(f\"{AD_ACCOUNT}/campaigns\", {\n        \"fields\": \"id,name,status,effective_status\",\n        \"limit\": 100\n    }).get(\"data\", [])\n\n    active_campaigns = [c for c in campaigns if c.get(\"status\") == \"ACTIVE\"]\n    print(f\"✅ Found {len(active_campaigns)} active campaigns out of {len(campaigns)} total\")\n    return active_campaigns\n\n\ndef fetch_adsets(campaign_id):\n    \"\"\"Fetch only ACTIVE ad sets.\"\"\"\n    adsets = fb_get(f\"{campaign_id}/adsets\", {\n        \"fields\": \"id,name,status\",\n        \"limit\": 100\n    }).get(\"data\", [])\n    return [a for a in adsets if a.get(\"status\") == \"ACTIVE\"]\n\n\ndef fetch_ads(adset_id):\n    \"\"\"Fetch only ACTIVE ads, including creative & normalized target URL.\"\"\"\n    ads = fb_get(f\"{adset_id}/ads\", {\n        \"fields\": \"id,name,status,creative{object_story_spec,object_url}\",\n        \"limit\": 100\n    }).get(\"data\", [])\n\n    active_ads = []\n    for ad in ads:\n        if ad.get(\"status\") != \"ACTIVE\":\n            continue\n\n        target_url = None\n        creative = ad.get(\"creative\", {})\n        oss = creative.get(\"object_story_spec\", {})\n\n        # Try link_data.link\n        if \"link_data\" in oss and \"link\" in oss[\"link_data\"]:\n            target_url = oss[\"link_data\"][\"link\"]\n\n        # Try link_data.call_to_action.value.link\n        elif \"link_data\" in oss and \"call_to_action\" in oss[\"link_data\"]:\n            target_url = oss[\"link_data\"][\"call_to_action\"][\"value\"].get(\"link\")\n\n        # Try video_data.link\n        elif \"video_data\" in oss and \"link\" in oss[\"video_data\"]:\n            target_url = oss[\"video_data\"][\"link\"]\n\n        # Try creative.object_url\n        elif creative.get(\"object_url\"):\n            target_url = creative[\"object_url\"]\n\n        print(f\"DEBUG: Ad '{ad.get('name')}' raw URL: {target_url}\")\n\n        if target_url:\n            target_url = normalize_amazon_url(target_url)\n        print(f\"DEBUG: Ad '{ad.get('name')}' normalized URL: {target_url}\")\n\n        ad[\"target_url\"] = target_url\n        active_ads.append(ad)\n\n    return active_ads\n\n\ndef load_json(path, default):\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        with open(path, \"r\") as f:\n            return json.load(f)\n    return default\n\n\ndef save_json(path, data):\n    with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n\n\ndef log_start(campaign):\n    print()\n    print(f\"[{datetime.now().isoformat()}] 🚀 START: {campaign['name']} ({campaign['id']})\")\n\n\ndef log_finish(campaign):\n    print(f\"[{datetime.now().isoformat()}] ✅ FINISHED: {campaign['name']} ({campaign['id']})\")\n    print(\"-\" * 50)\n\n\ndef main():\n    output = load_json(ADS_FILE, [])\n    progress = load_json(PROGRESS_FILE, {\"last_campaign_id\": None})\n    last_id = progress.get(\"last_campaign_id\")\n\n    campaigns = fetch_campaigns()\n    start = not last_id  # If no progress file, start immediately\n\n    for campaign in campaigns:\n        if not start:\n            if campaign[\"id\"] == last_id:\n                start = True\n            else:\n                continue\n\n        log_start(campaign)\n\n        campaign_obj = {\n            \"campaign_id\": campaign[\"id\"],\n            \"name\": campaign[\"name\"],\n            \"status\": campaign[\"status\"],\n            \"adsets\": []\n        }\n\n        adsets = fetch_adsets(campaign[\"id\"])\n        for adset in adsets:\n            time.sleep(1)  # throttle\n            ads = fetch_ads(adset[\"id\"])\n            adset_obj = {\n                \"adset_id\": adset[\"id\"],\n                \"name\": adset[\"name\"],\n                \"status\": adset[\"status\"],\n                \"ads\": ads\n            }\n            campaign_obj[\"adsets\"].append(adset_obj)\n\n        output.append(campaign_obj)\n        save_json(ADS_FILE, output)\n        save_json(PROGRESS_FILE, {\"last_campaign_id\": campaign[\"id\"]})\n\n        log_finish(campaign)\n\n    print(\"🎉 All active campaigns processed!\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 Changes\n1. **Extra URL extraction logic** for:\n   - `link_data.link`\n   - `link_data.call_to_action.value.link`\n   - `video_data.link`\n   - `creative.object_url`\n2. **Debug prints** for:\n   - Raw URL before normalization\n   - Normalized URL after stripping tracking params\n3. Still **ACTIVE-only** and keeps **resume + rate limit backoff**.\n\n---\n\nIf you run this now:\n```bash\npython fetch_ads.py\n```\nYou should see exactly why some ads were coming through with `(URL: None)` in `link_ads.py`.\n\n---\n\nDo you want me to also tweak `link_ads.py` to **warn if an ad has no URL** before trying to classify it? That would make it easier to spot and fix gaps."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "yes, let's tweak link_ads.py too"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Alright ✅ — here’s the **tweaked `link_ads.py`** so that:  \n\n- It **warns clearly** if `target_url` is `None` before classification  \n- Skips classification if there’s no URL and keeps going  \n- Still does ASIN extraction, metadata lookup, and lead-gen detection when a URL exists  \n\n---\n\n## 📄 `link_ads.py`\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport re\nimport requests\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\n# Load environment variables\nload_dotenv()\n\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nADS_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"ads.json\")\nLINKED_FILE = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"linked_ads.json\")\n\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n# --- Local metadata lookup table (extend manually as needed) ---\nBOOK_METADATA = {\n    \"B09BW7F5PZ\": {  # Dragon's Kin\n        \"book_title\": \"Dragon's Kin\",\n        \"asin\": \"B09BW7F5PZ\",\n        \"blurb\": \"Young Kindan has no expectations other than a hard life in the coal mines of Camp Natalon...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81bApXw2o7L.jpg\"\n    },\n    \"B07GZHLJPT\": {  # The Jupiter Game\n        \"book_title\": \"The Jupiter Game\",\n        \"asin\": \"B07GZHLJPT\",\n        \"blurb\": \"Earth enters the Galactic Union. First contact with aliens occurs just after humanity’s first fusion-powered ship reaches Jupiter...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41mVzJ2Hy1L.jpg\"\n    },\n    \"FREEBIE_TITLE\": {  # Newsletter freebie example\n        \"book_title\": \"Free Starter Book\",\n        \"asin\": None,\n        \"blurb\": \"A free introduction to the world of...\",\n        \"cover_url\": \"https://example.com/freebie-cover.jpg\"\n    }\n}\n\n# --- Helpers ---\ndef load_json(path, default):\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        with open(path, \"r\") as f:\n            return json.load(f)\n    return default\n\ndef save_json(path, data):\n    with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n\ndef extract_asin(url):\n    \"\"\"Extract ASIN from Amazon URL.\"\"\"\n    if not url:\n        return None\n    match = re.search(r\"/dp/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", url)\n    if match:\n        return match.group(1)\n    match = re.search(r\"/gp/product/([A-Z0-9]{10})\", url)\n    if match:\n        return match.group(1)\n    return None\n\ndef fetch_metadata_from_openlibrary(asin):\n    \"\"\"Fetch book metadata from Open Library via ISBN lookup.\"\"\"\n    url = f\"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/{asin}.json\"\n    try:\n        r = requests.get(url, timeout=10)\n        if r.status_code == 200:\n            data = r.json()\n            title = data.get(\"title\")\n            blurb = data.get(\"description\", \"\")\n            if isinstance(blurb, dict):\n                blurb = blurb.get(\"value\", \"\")\n            cover_url = None\n            if \"covers\" in data:\n                cover_url = f\"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/{data['covers'][0]}-L.jpg\"\n            return {\n                \"book_title\": title or f\"Unknown ({asin})\",\n                \"asin\": asin,\n                \"blurb\": blurb,\n                \"cover_url\": cover_url\n            }\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"⚠️ Could not fetch metadata for {asin}: {e}\")\n    return {\n        \"book_title\": f\"Unknown ({asin})\",\n        \"asin\": asin,\n        \"blurb\": None,\n        \"cover_url\": None\n    }\n\ndef classify_url(url):\n    \"\"\"Classify ad type and return metadata.\"\"\"\n    if not url:\n        return \"unknown\", None\n\n    url_lower = url.lower()\n\n    # Lead-gen: BookFunnel / newsletter\n    if \"bookfunnel.com\" in url_lower or \"newsletter\" in url_lower:\n        return \"lead_gen\", BOOK_METADATA.get(\"FREEBIE_TITLE\")\n\n    # Amazon: Extract ASIN and look up metadata\n    if \"amazon.com\" in url_lower:\n        asin = extract_asin(url)\n        if asin:\n            metadata = BOOK_METADATA.get(asin)\n            if not metadata:\n                print(f\"🔍 Fetching metadata for ASIN {asin}...\")\n                metadata = fetch_metadata_from_openlibrary(asin)\n            return \"sale\", metadata\n\n    return \"unknown\", None\n\n# --- Main ---\ndef main():\n    ads_data = load_json(ADS_FILE, [])\n    if not ads_data:\n        print(f\"❌ No {ADS_FILE} found. Run fetch_ads.py first.\")\n        return\n\n    linked_data = []\n\n    print(\"🔗 Auto-linking ads to books/newsletter...\\n\")\n\n    for campaign in ads_data:\n        print(f\"\\n=== Campaign: {campaign['name']} ===\")\n        for adset in campaign[\"adsets\"]:\n            for ad in adset[\"ads\"]:\n                ad_id = ad[\"id\"]\n                ad_name = ad[\"name\"]\n                target_url = ad.get(\"target_url\")\n\n                # Warn if URL is missing\n                if not target_url:\n                    print(f\"⚠️ WARNING: Ad '{ad_name}' has no target URL — skipping\")\n                    continue\n\n                print(f\"DEBUG: Processing ad '{ad_name}' with URL: {target_url}\")\n\n                ad_type, metadata = classify_url(target_url)\n\n                if metadata:\n                    print(f\"✅ Linked {ad_name} ({ad_type}) → {metadata['book_title']}\")\n                    linked_data.append({\n                        \"campaign_name\": campaign[\"name\"],\n                        \"campaign_id\": campaign[\"campaign_id\"],\n                        \"adset_name\": adset[\"name\"],\n                        \"adset_id\": adset[\"adset_id\"],\n                        \"ad_name\": ad_name,\n                        \"ad_id\": ad_id,\n                        \"target_url\": target_url,\n                        \"type\": ad_type,\n                        **metadata\n                    })\n                else:\n                    print(f\"⚠️ Could not auto-link {ad_name} (URL: {target_url})\")\n                    title = input(\"Book Title (or leave blank to skip): \").strip()\n                    if not title:\n                        continue\n                    asin = input(\"ASIN (optional): \").strip()\n                    blurb = input(\"Blurb (optional): \").strip()\n                    cover_url = input(\"Cover URL (optional): \").strip()\n                    linked_data.append({\n                        \"campaign_name\": campaign[\"name\"],\n                        \"campaign_id\": campaign[\"campaign_id\"],\n                        \"adset_name\": adset[\"name\"],\n                        \"adset_id\": adset[\"adset_id\"],\n                        \"ad_name\": ad_name,\n                        \"ad_id\": ad_id,\n                        \"target_url\": target_url,\n                        \"type\": ad_type if ad_type != \"unknown\" else \"manual\",\n                        \"book_title\": title,\n                        \"asin\": asin or None,\n                        \"blurb\": blurb or None,\n                        \"cover_url\": cover_url or None\n                    })\n\n                save_json(LINKED_FILE, linked_data)\n\n    print(f\"\\n💾 Saved linked ads to {LINKED_FILE}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 What’s New\n- **Warning for missing URLs** before classification  \n- **Debug print** shows the URL being processed for each ad  \n- If no URL, the ad is **skipped entirely** (avoids `(URL: None)` clutter)  \n- Keeps all ASIN extraction and metadata logic intact  \n\n---\n\nIf we now run:\n```bash\npython fetch_ads.py\npython link_ads.py\n```\n…you’ll get clear messages telling you **which ads are missing URLs and why**.  \n\n---\n\nDo you want me to also make `fetch_ads.py` **log which URL source worked** (`link_data`, `video_data`, or `object_url`)? That would help us know if we’re covering all the formats you use in ads."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "you're looking in the wrong place for URL. Can you write a script to enumerate all the attributes of an ad?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Yep — if we want to stop guessing where Facebook hides the URL, we need a **deep dump** of the ad object straight from the Graph API so we can see *everything* available.  \n\nHere’s a quick `enumerate_ad_fields.py` that:  \n- Pulls **all fields** for one or more ads  \n- Dumps the raw JSON so we can inspect the exact structure and find the correct URL path  \n\n---\n\n## 📄 `enumerate_ad_fields.py`\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport requests\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\nload_dotenv()\n\nACCESS_TOKEN = os.getenv(\"FB_ACCESS_TOKEN\")\nAD_ACCOUNT_ID = os.getenv(\"FB_AD_ACCOUNT_ID\")\nAPI_VERSION = \"v19.0\"\nBASE_URL = f\"https://graph.facebook.com/{API_VERSION}\"\nAD_ACCOUNT = f\"act_{AD_ACCOUNT_ID}\"\n\n# Output folder\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n\ndef fb_get(endpoint, params=None):\n    if params is None:\n        params = {}\n    params[\"access_token\"] = ACCESS_TOKEN\n    url = f\"{BASE_URL}/{endpoint}\"\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params)\n    r.raise_for_status()\n    return r.json()\n\n\ndef enumerate_ads():\n    \"\"\"Fetch all ads and dump raw JSON for inspection.\"\"\"\n    print(\"📥 Fetching ads (no filtering)...\")\n\n    ads = fb_get(f\"{AD_ACCOUNT}/ads\", {\n        \"fields\": \",\".join([\"id\", \"name\", \"creative\", \"status\", \"ad_review_feedback\"]),\n        \"limit\": 10  # adjust if you want more\n    }).get(\"data\", [])\n\n    output_path = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"ads_raw.json\")\n    with open(output_path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(ads, f, indent=2)\n\n    print(f\"✅ Saved raw ad dump to {output_path}\")\n    print(\"💡 Open this file and search for 'http' or 'link' to find URL fields.\")\n\n    return ads\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    ads = enumerate_ads()\n    print(f\"🔍 Found {len(ads)} ads in raw dump.\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## How to Use\n1. Run:\n   ```bash\n   python enumerate_ad_fields.py\n   ```\n2. Open `data/ads_raw.json` in your editor  \n3. Search for:\n   - `\"http\"`\n   - `\"link\"`\n   - `\"object_url\"`\n   - `\"url\"`\n\nYou’ll see exactly which attribute your ads store the destination link in — whether it’s inside `creative.object_story_spec`, `object_url`, `link_data`, or somewhere unexpected.\n\n---\n\n💡 Once we confirm the real field path from this dump, I can patch `fetch_ads.py` so it **always** pulls the URL from the right place.  \n\nDo you want me to **also** make this dump grab *every single field Facebook allows* for the ad object? That would give us the most complete map possible."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "yeah... that didn't work. You are listing the fields you want which defeats the purpose of finding all fields."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Ah — yep, you’re right.  \nIf we hardcode `\"fields\": ...`, we’re back to guessing.  \nTo truly **enumerate all ad attributes**, we need to:  \n\n1. Ask the Graph API for the ad object **without specifying any fields** so it returns *only* `id` and `name` (that’s default behavior)  \n2. Use Facebook’s **`metadata=1`** query parameter to get a list of *available fields* for the object type  \n3. Call the API **again** requesting *all those fields* at once so we see the entire structure\n\n---\n\n## 📄 `enumerate_all_ad_fields.py`\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport requests\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\nload_dotenv()\n\nACCESS_TOKEN = os.getenv(\"FB_ACCESS_TOKEN\")\nAD_ACCOUNT_ID = os.getenv(\"FB_AD_ACCOUNT_ID\")\nAPI_VERSION = \"v19.0\"\nBASE_URL = f\"https://graph.facebook.com/{API_VERSION}\"\nAD_ACCOUNT = f\"act_{AD_ACCOUNT_ID}\"\n\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n\ndef fb_get(endpoint, params=None):\n    if params is None:\n        params = {}\n    params[\"access_token\"] = ACCESS_TOKEN\n    url = f\"{BASE_URL}/{endpoint}\"\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params)\n    r.raise_for_status()\n    return r.json()\n\n\ndef get_all_ad_fields(sample_ad_id):\n    \"\"\"Fetch the full list of available fields for the ad object.\"\"\"\n    meta = fb_get(f\"{sample_ad_id}\", {\"metadata\": 1})\n    fields = meta.get(\"metadata\", {}).get(\"fields\", [])\n    field_names = [f[\"name\"] for f in fields]\n    return field_names\n\n\ndef dump_full_ad(ad_id, field_list):\n    \"\"\"Dump all ad fields for a single ad.\"\"\"\n    fields_param = \",\".join(field_list)\n    ad_data = fb_get(ad_id, {\"fields\": fields_param})\n    out_path = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, f\"ad_{ad_id}_full.json\")\n    with open(out_path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(ad_data, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"✅ Full ad dump saved to {out_path}\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    print(\"📥 Fetching a sample ad ID...\")\n    ads = fb_get(f\"{AD_ACCOUNT}/ads\", {\"limit\": 1}).get(\"data\", [])\n    if not ads:\n        print(\"❌ No ads found.\")\n        return\n\n    sample_ad_id = ads[0][\"id\"]\n    print(f\"Using sample ad ID: {sample_ad_id}\")\n\n    print(\"🔍 Getting all available fields...\")\n    all_fields = get_all_ad_fields(sample_ad_id)\n    print(f\"Found {len(all_fields)} fields.\")\n\n    print(\"📥 Dumping full ad data...\")\n    dump_full_ad(sample_ad_id, all_fields)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n## How It Works\n1. **Gets a sample ad ID** from your account (just grabs the first ad found)\n2. Calls `/{ad_id}?metadata=1` → returns all possible fields for the ad object\n3. Calls `/{ad_id}?fields=<ALL_FIELDS>` → dumps a complete JSON to `data/ad_<id>_full.json`\n4. You can then search for `http` or `link` to find where the real destination URL is stored\n\n---\n\nIf we run this, we’ll know exactly:\n- Which Facebook field contains your ad’s URL\n- Whether it’s buried in creative, object_story_spec, tracking specs, or somewhere else\n\n---\n\nDo you want me to make this script **loop through multiple ads** so we see if the URL field varies by ad format? That could matter if you run both image link ads and video ads."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "why are we using \"v19.0\" of graph.facebook.com when it's currently at 23.0?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Yeah — good catch.  \nWe shouldn’t be on `v19.0` unless we have a specific reason (like maintaining compatibility with an older integration).  \n\nThe Facebook Marketing / Graph API **version** in the URL controls:  \n- Which fields & endpoints are available  \n- Which ones are deprecated / removed  \n- How certain fields are formatted in responses  \n\n---\n\n### 📌 Why We’re on `v19.0` in your scripts now\n- I think it came from the **earlier snippets you and I started from** (possibly copied from an older tutorial or example)\n- We just never bumped it while adding features  \n\n---\n\n### 📌 Why you should switch to `v23.0`\n- **Latest features:** v23.0 has new fields and endpoints  \n- **Deprecation safety:** Old versions get sunsetted — Facebook supports ~2 years of versions before deprecation  \n- **Better coverage:** You’re currently chasing the ad URL issue — the latest version may return more consistent creative object fields\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ But a small warning\n- Upgrading may change the **structure** of some fields (especially `object_story_spec`)  \n- A few fields we request might be renamed or moved — we’ll see errors if that happens, and we can patch quickly\n\n---\n\n### 🔄 How to update\nIn all scripts, replace:\n```python\nAPI_VERSION = \"v19.0\"\n```\nwith:\n```python\nAPI_VERSION = \"v23.0\"\n```\n\nThat’s literally it — no other code changes required **unless** Facebook has moved or removed something we’re calling.  \n\n---\n\n💡 My suggestion:  \nRun the **`enumerate_all_ad_fields.py`** I just wrote using `v23.0`.  \nThat way we’ll confirm the **real** URL location in the current API before we touch `fetch_ads.py` again.\n\n---\n\nDo you want me to go ahead and **regenerate that ad field enumerator script** now set to `v23.0` and able to check multiple ads at once? That would answer your URL mystery in one run."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
