ields by default**, even if we try `metadata=1`.  \nThe *actual* URL you want isn’t stored directly on the ad object — it’s almost always inside the **creative object** that the ad points to.  \n\nRight now, your dump shows things like:\n```json\n\"creative\": {\n  \"id\": \"1019126353676382\"\n}\n```\nThat means we need to **follow that creative ID** and inspect the creative object with all its fields.\n\n---\n\n## Plan to Find the URL\n\n1. Get a **list of ad creatives** linked to your ads.  \n2. For each creative, ask for **`metadata=1`** to get *all* fields.  \n3. Fetch the creative with all fields to see exactly where the destination link lives.\n\n---\n\n## 📄 enumerate_all_creative_fields.py\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport requests\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\n# Load env vars\nload_dotenv()\n\nACCESS_TOKEN = os.getenv(\"FB_ACCESS_TOKEN\")\nAD_ACCOUNT_ID = os.getenv(\"FB_AD_ACCOUNT_ID\")\nAPI_VERSION = \"v23.0\"\nBASE_URL = f\"https://graph.facebook.com/{API_VERSION}\"\nAD_ACCOUNT = f\"act_{AD_ACCOUNT_ID}\"\n\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n\ndef fb_get(endpoint, params=None):\n    if params is None:\n        params = {}\n    params[\"access_token\"] = ACCESS_TOKEN\n    url = f\"{BASE_URL}/{endpoint}\"\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params)\n    r.raise_for_status()\n    return r.json()\n\n\ndef get_all_fields(object_id):\n    \"\"\"Fetch all available fields for a given object via metadata=1.\"\"\"\n    meta = fb_get(f\"{object_id}\", {\"metadata\": 1})\n    fields = meta.get(\"metadata\", {}).get(\"fields\", [])\n    return [f[\"name\"] for f in fields]\n\n\ndef dump_full_object(object_id, fields, label):\n    \"\"\"Fetch object with all fields and dump to file.\"\"\"\n    fields_param = \",\".join(fields)\n    data = fb_get(object_id, {\"fields\": fields_param})\n    out_path = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, f\"{label}_{object_id}_full.json\")\n    with open(out_path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"✅ Dumped {label} {object_id} to {out_path}\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    print(\"📥 Fetching up to 5 ads...\")\n    ads = fb_get(f\"{AD_ACCOUNT}/ads\", {\"fields\": \"id,name,creative\", \"limit\": 5}).get(\"data\", [])\n    if not ads:\n        print(\"❌ No ads found.\")\n        return\n\n    for ad in ads:\n        ad_id = ad[\"id\"]\n        ad_name = ad.get(\"name\", \"No Name\")\n        creative_id = ad.get(\"creative\", {}).get(\"id\")\n        print(f\"\\n🔍 Ad: {ad_name} ({ad_id}) - Creative ID: {creative_id}\")\n\n        if not creative_id:\n            print(\"⚠️ No creative linked — skipping.\")\n            continue\n\n        print(f\"📑 Getting all creative fields for {creative_id}...\")\n        creative_fields = get_all_fields(creative_id)\n        print(f\"  Found {len(creative_fields)} creative fields.\")\n\n        dump_full_object(creative_id, creative_fields, \"creative\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n### What This Does\n- Pulls up to **5 ads** with `id`, `name`, and `creative.id`.\n- For each creative:\n  1. Gets **all available field names** using `metadata=1`.\n  2. Fetches the creative with **all fields**.\n  3. Dumps the raw creative JSON to `data/creative_<id>_full.json`.\n\n---\n\n### Next Steps\nOnce we run this, we search inside the creative JSON files for:\n- `\"link\"`\n- `\"url\"`\n- `\"object_url\"`\n- `\"call_to_action\"`\n- `\"object_story_spec\"`\n\nThat will tell us **exactly** where the link is for your ads.\n\n---\n\nDo you want me to make this script **follow video creatives** too, in case you’re running any video ads? That way we can map both static and video ad URLs in one pass."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
