ponsored_message%2Cname%2Cobject_id%2Cobject_store_url%2Cobject_story_id%2Cobject_story_spec%2Cobject_type%2Cobject_url%2Cpage_welcome_message%2Cphoto_album_source_object_story_id%2Cplace_page_set_id%2Cplatform_customizations%2Cplayable_asset_id%2Cportrait_customizations%2Cproduct_data%2Cproduct_set_id%2Crecommender_settings%2Creferral_id%2Cregional_regulation_disclaimer_spec%2Csource_facebook_post_id%2Csource_instagram_media_id%2Cstatus%2Ctemplate_url%2Ctemplate_url_spec%2Cthreads_user_id%2Cthumbnail_id%2Cthumbnail_url%2Ctitle%2Curl_tags%2Cuse_page_actor_override%2Cvideo_id&access_token=EAAKWo0WDUcUBPNm5SiNixrGZAP9OjYEZAtbDnTc3idnxNSeQEgLr48q9lbZBbZB8oTqZAruZCjBMyIWADKJEZBwRElgOYJmQw70qlF3Y43e68BVURkaN6dCRNlNMdAaBskId1S2aWD3ZBxPVKxx7CBubXnxz85l1IZCtNAX9qZAjEkoh9Qu0EZBZCObN9K5HHw2enuZCGPZBiZBIMicRnYeQvKPJZBDMA9jZB"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Ah — I see exactly why that blew up.  \nFacebook’s Graph API has a **URL length limit**, and when we try to request *all* 69 fields in one go for a creative, the `fields` parameter becomes too long and triggers a `400 Bad Request`.\n\n---\n\n### Fix:\nWe can fetch **all fields in batches** (e.g., 15–20 at a time) and merge the results into a single JSON.  \nThat way:\n- No single request is too long\n- We still get all fields\n\n---\n\n## 📄 enumerate_all_creative_fields.py (patched for batching)\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport requests\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\nfrom math import ceil\n\n# Load env vars\nload_dotenv()\n\nACCESS_TOKEN = os.getenv(\"FB_ACCESS_TOKEN\")\nAD_ACCOUNT_ID = os.getenv(\"FB_AD_ACCOUNT_ID\")\nAPI_VERSION = \"v23.0\"\nBASE_URL = f\"https://graph.facebook.com/{API_VERSION}\"\nAD_ACCOUNT = f\"act_{AD_ACCOUNT_ID}\"\n\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n\ndef fb_get(endpoint, params=None):\n    if params is None:\n        params = {}\n    params[\"access_token\"] = ACCESS_TOKEN\n    url = f\"{BASE_URL}/{endpoint}\"\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params)\n    r.raise_for_status()\n    return r.json()\n\n\ndef get_all_fields(object_id):\n    \"\"\"Fetch all available fields for a given object via metadata=1.\"\"\"\n    meta = fb_get(f\"{object_id}\", {\"metadata\": 1})\n    fields = meta.get(\"metadata\", {}).get(\"fields\", [])\n    return [f[\"name\"] for f in fields]\n\n\ndef dump_full_object(object_id, fields, label, batch_size=20):\n    \"\"\"Fetch object with all fields in batches to avoid URL length limit.\"\"\"\n    merged_data = {}\n    total_batches = ceil(len(fields) / batch_size)\n\n    for i in range(0, len(fields), batch_size):\n        batch = fields[i:i+batch_size]\n        fields_param = \",\".join(batch)\n        print(f\"   📦 Fetching batch {i//batch_size + 1}/{total_batches} ({len(batch)} fields)\")\n        data = fb_get(object_id, {\"fields\": fields_param})\n        merged_data.update(data)\n\n    out_path = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, f\"{label}_{object_id}_full.json\")\n    with open(out_path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(merged_data, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"✅ Dumped {label} {object_id} to {out_path}\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    print(\"📥 Fetching up to 5 ads...\")\n    ads = fb_get(f\"{AD_ACCOUNT}/ads\", {\"fields\": \"id,name,creative\", \"limit\": 5}).get(\"data\", [])\n    if not ads:\n        print(\"❌ No ads found.\")\n        return\n\n    for ad in ads:\n        ad_id = ad[\"id\"]\n        ad_name = ad.get(\"name\", \"No Name\")\n        creative_id = ad.get(\"creative\", {}).get(\"id\")\n        print(f\"\\n🔍 Ad: {ad_name} ({ad_id}) - Creative ID: {creative_id}\")\n\n        if not creative_id:\n            print(\"⚠️ No creative linked — skipping.\")\n            continue\n\n        print(f\"📑 Getting all creative fields for {creative_id}...\")\n        creative_fields = get_all_fields(creative_id)\n        print(f\"  Found {len(creative_fields)} creative fields.\")\n\n        dump_full_object(creative_id, creative_fields, \"creative\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 What Changed\n- **Batching**: Splits the list of creative fields into chunks (default 20 fields per request)  \n- **Merging**: Combines all batches into a single JSON output file  \n- **Output**: Still saves one `creative_<id>_full.json` per creative for easy searching\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 How to Use\n```bash\npython enumerate_all_creative_fields.py\n```\nThen open the JSON(s) in `data/` and search for `\"http\"` or `\"link\"` to locate the destination URL fields.\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can also have this script **automatically scan the resulting JSONs** and highlight *all* fields containing URLs so we can skip the manual search step.  \nThat way we’ll instantly know the exact field to pull in `fetch_ads.py`.  \n\nDo you want me to add that auto-URL-finder?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "📥 Fetching up to 5 ads...\n\n🔍 Ad: Winner 1A - Music - Copy 2 (120219330415450146) - Creative ID: 2153239648435068\n📑 Getting all creative fields for 2153239648435068...\n  Found 69 creative fields.\n   📦 Fetching batch 1/4 (20 fields)\n   📦 Fetching batch 2/4 (20 fields)\n   📦 Fetching batch 3/4 (20 fields)\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/todd/fabams/Enum_ACF.py\", line 80, in <module>\n    main()\n    ~~~~^^\n  File \"/home/todd/fabams/Enum_ACF.py\", line 76, in main\n    dump_full_object(creative_id, creative_fields, \"creative\")\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/todd/fabams/Enum_ACF.py\", line 46, in dump_full_object\n    data = fb_get(object_id, {\"fields\": fields_param})\n  File \"/home/todd/fabams/Enum_ACF.py\", line 26, in fb_get\n    r.raise_for_status()\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\n  File \"/home/todd/fenv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/requests/models.py\", line 1026, in raise_for_status\n    raise HTTPError(http_error_msg, response=self)\nrequests.exceptions.HTTPError: 400 Client Error: Bad Request for url: https://graph.facebook.com/v23.0/2153239648435068?fields=object_id%2Cobject_store_url%2Cobject_story_id%2Cobject_story_spec%2Cobject_type%2Cobject_url%2Cpage_welcome_message%2Cphoto_album_source_object_story_id%2Cplace_page_set_id%2Cplatform_customizations%2Cplayable_asset_id%2Cportrait_customizations%2Cproduct_data%2Cproduct_set_id%2Crecommender_settings%2Creferral_id%2Cregional_regulation_disclaimer_spec%2Csource_facebook_post_id%2Csource_instagram_media_id%2Cstatus&access_token=EAAKWo0WDUcUBPNm5SiNixrGZAP9OjYEZAtbDnTc3idnxNSeQEgLr48q9lbZBbZB8oTqZAruZCjBMyIWADKJEZBwRElgOYJmQw70qlF3Y43e68BVURkaN6dCRNlNMdAaBskId1S2aWD3ZBxPVKxx7CBubXnxz85l1IZCtNAX9qZAjEkoh9Qu0EZBZCObN9K5HHw2enuZCGPZBiZBIMicRnYeQvKPJZBDMA9jZB"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it — the 400 in the **third batch** means some of the creative fields Facebook reports in `metadata=1` aren’t actually retrievable for that creative.  \nThis is annoyingly common — the metadata endpoint lists “possible” fields for the object type, but many fields are only valid for specific ad formats.  \n\n---\n\n### 🔹 How we fix it\nInstead of blindly requesting every field Facebook lists, we:\n1. Request **each field individually**  \n2. Keep the ones that return **200 OK**  \n3. Merge the results into the full JSON dump  \n\nIt’s slower, but it guarantees **no 400 errors** and we’ll still get all valid fields for that creative.\n\n---\n\n## 📄 enumerate_all_creative_fields.py (safe mode)\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nimport requests\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\n# Load env vars\nload_dotenv()\n\nACCESS_TOKEN = os.getenv(\"FB_ACCESS_TOKEN\")\nAD_ACCOUNT_ID = os.getenv(\"FB_AD_ACCOUNT_ID\")\nAPI_VERSION = \"v23.0\"\nBASE_URL = f\"https://graph.facebook.com/{API_VERSION}\"\nAD_ACCOUNT = f\"act_{AD_ACCOUNT_ID}\"\n\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"data\"\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n\ndef fb_get(endpoint, params=None):\n    \"\"\"Basic GET request with error handling.\"\"\"\n    if params is None:\n        params = {}\n    params[\"access_token\"] = ACCESS_TOKEN\n    url = f\"{BASE_URL}/{endpoint}\"\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params)\n    if r.status_code == 400:\n        return None\n    r.raise_for_status()\n    return r.json()\n\n\ndef get_all_fields(object_id):\n    \"\"\"Fetch all available fields for a given object via metadata=1.\"\"\"\n    meta = fb_get(f\"{object_id}\", {\"metadata\": 1})\n    fields = meta.get(\"metadata\", {}).get(\"fields\", [])\n    return [f[\"name\"] for f in fields]\n\n\ndef dump_full_object_safe(object_id, fields, label):\n    \"\"\"Fetch object field-by-field to avoid 400 errors.\"\"\"\n    merged_data = {}\n    valid_fields = []\n\n    for f in fields:\n        resp = fb_get(object_id, {\"fields\": f})\n        if resp is not None:\n            merged_data.update(resp)\n            valid_fields.append(f)\n        else:\n            print(f\"⚠️ Skipping field '{f}' — not available for this creative.\")\n\n    out_path = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, f\"{label}_{object_id}_full.json\")\n    with open(out_path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(merged_data, f, indent=2)\n\n    print(f\"✅ Dumped {label} {object_id} to {out_path}\")\n    print(f\"📋 Valid fields: {len(valid_fields)} / {len(fields)}\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    print(\"📥 Fetching up to 5 ads...\")\n    ads = fb_get(f\"{AD_ACCOUNT}/ads\", {\"fields\": \"id,name,creative\", \"limit\": 5}).get(\"data\", [])\n    if not ads:\n        print(\"❌ No ads found.\")\n        return\n\n    for ad in ads:\n        ad_id = ad[\"id\"]\n        ad_name = ad.get(\"name\", \"No Name\")\n        creative_id = ad.get(\"creative\", {}).get(\"id\")\n        print(f\"\\n🔍 Ad: {ad_name} ({ad_id}) - Creative ID: {creative_id}\")\n\n        if not creative_id:\n            print(\"⚠️ No creative linked — skipping.\")\n            continue\n\n        print(f\"📑 Getting all creative fields for {creative_id}...\")\n        creative_fields = get_all_fields(creative_id)\n        print(f\"  Found {len(creative_fields)} creative fields.\")\n\n        dump_full_object_safe(creative_id, creative_fields, \"creative\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 Changes\n- **Requests each field individually** instead of batching  \n- **Skips invalid fields** (logs them) so no 400 errors  \n- Outputs a clean JSON with only valid data for that creative  \n\n---\n\nOnce you run this:\n```bash\npython enumerate_all_creative_fields.py\n```\nYou can open the `data/creative_<id>_full.json` and search for `\"http\"` or `\"link\"`.  \nWe’ll finally know **exactly** where the destination URL is for your ads.\n\n---\n\nDo you want me to also have this **automatically scan for all fields containing URLs** and print them out after the dump? That way you don’t have to manually search the JSON."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
