e\" in link_data[\"call_to_action\"]:\n    target_url = link_data[\"call_to_action\"][\"value\"].get(\"link\")\n```\n\nThat would catch:\n- Regular link ads  \n- Carousel/multi-image ads  \n- CTA-button ads with a link  \n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can regenerate `fetch_ads.py` so it:  \n1. Pulls **`child_attachments.link`** and **CTA value links**  \n2. Logs which path produced the link (so we know what’s working)  \n3. Keeps the Amazon normalization  \n\nThat would probably make `target_url` show up for these `None` cases.  \nDo you want me to regenerate it that way?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
