{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "please prepare the README.md guide"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here you go — **Todd LLM Avatar README.md guide** — first edition 🚀\n\n---\n\n# Todd LLM Avatar — Build Guide\n\nA step-by-step pipeline to create a personal LLM avatar of Todd McCaffrey, using:\n\n✅ ChatGPT conversation history  \n✅ Email corpus (coming soon)  \n✅ Novel/story corpus (coming soon)  \n\n---\n\n## Pipeline overview\n\n```plaintext\nExport ChatGPT ZIP\n↓\nchat_parser.py → parsed.json\n↓\nquality_filter.py → filtered_all_chats.txt → filtered.json\n↓\nprep_for_embeddings.py → embeddings_ready.jsonl\nprep_for_finetune.py  → finetune_ready.jsonl\n↓\nRAG → ChromaDB / Ollama / LM Studio\nFine-tune → Axolotl + QLoRA → new model\n↓\nRun Todd LLM Avatar locally!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 1 — Export ChatGPT data\n\n1️⃣ Go to [chat.openai.com](https://chat.openai.com)  \n2️⃣ Bottom-left → profile → Settings  \n3️⃣ **Data Controls** → Export Data  \n4️⃣ Download ZIP from email  \n5️⃣ Extract → `conversations.json`\n\n---\n\n## Step 2 — Parse ChatGPT data\n\n```bash\npython3 chat_parser.py --input conversations.json --output Output/parsed.json --split\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 3 — Quality filter\n\n```bash\npython3 quality_filter.py --input Output/parsed.json --output Output/filtered.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 4 — Prepare embeddings\n\n```bash\npython3 prep_for_embeddings.py --input Output/filtered.json --output Output/embeddings_ready.jsonl\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 5 — Prepare fine-tune data\n\n```bash\npython3 prep_for_finetune.py --input Output/filtered.json --output Output/finetune_ready.jsonl\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 6a — Run local RAG with Ollama\n\n```bash\nollama create todd-rag -f ./Modelfile\n# Load embeddings into Ollama API\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 6b — Run RAG with ChromaDB\n\n```python\n# See chromadb_loader.py example\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 6c — Fine-tune Todd LLM with Axolotl\n\nExample `config.yml`:\n\n```yaml\nbase_model: meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B\ndataset:\n  path: output/finetune_ready.jsonl\nadapter: qlora\nlora_r: 16\nlora_alpha: 32\noutput_dir: output/todd-llama3-8b\nsequence_len: 4096\ntrain_batch_size: 4\neval_batch_size: 4\ngradient_accumulation_steps: 8\nnum_train_epochs: 3\nlearning_rate: 5e-5\n```\n\nTrain:\n\n```bash\naxolotl train config.yml\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 7 — Run Todd LLM in LM Studio\n\n1️⃣ Load `Meta-Llama-3-8B`  \n2️⃣ Load `embeddings_ready.jsonl` as memory  \n3️⃣ OR load fine-tuned `todd-llama3-8b` model  \n4️⃣ Chat with Todd Avatar!\n\n---\n\n# Notes\n\n- **1861 fine-tune items** = excellent first fine-tune size  \n- **1812 embedding docs** = great for first RAG  \n- Can expand with **email** + **novel** corpus next  \n\n---\n\n# Next milestones\n\n✅ Combine with **email cleaning pipeline**  \n✅ Combine with **novel/story corpus**  \n✅ Test **Mistral 7B** vs **LLaMA 3 8B**  \n✅ Build simple **FastAPI Todd LLM server** (API serving Todd Avatar)\n\n---\n\n🚀 You are now ready to launch Todd LLM Avatar v0.1!\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can now:\n\n✅ Package this as a small GitHub repo for you (so it’s versioned)  \n✅ Add full example `Modelfile`, Chroma loader, Axolotl config  \n✅ Add a `requirements.txt`\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to prep the repo structure for you next? 🚀  \nIt’ll make it easier to track your work + share later.  \nJust say **yes**. 🎁"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "so... what sort of machine do you recommend for $3000? $4000? Remember, I'll build it."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great question — since you will **build it yourself** (which saves $$ vs prebuilt), here’s what I recommend — tuned for your *actual goal*: **Todd LLM Avatar**, meaning:\n\n✅ Run **Mistral 7B**, **LLaMA 3 8B**, maybe even **LLaMA 3 70B** one day  \n✅ Fine-tune with Axolotl  \n✅ Run embeddings / RAG locally  \n✅ Leave on all day (quiet, cool, stable)  \n✅ 2+ years future-proof\n\n---\n\n### 🏆 Build at ~$3000 USD (budget for now, upgradeable later)\n\n| Component      | Part |\n|----------------|------|\n| **CPU**        | Ryzen 9 7950X3D (no change — best for AI work) |\n| **MB**         | ASUS ProArt X670E or ASUS ROG Strix X670E |\n| **RAM**        | 64 GB DDR5 6000 CL30 (start here — upgrade to 128 GB later) |\n| **GPU**        | RTX 4080 Super 16 GB (great for LLaMA 8B/13B) |\n| **SSD**        | 2 TB Samsung 990 Pro NVMe |\n| **Cooler**     | Arctic Liquid Freezer III 360 A-RGB |\n| **PSU**        | 1000W Platinum or Gold |\n| **Case**       | Fractal North XL / BeQuiet 802 / Lian Li |\n\n---\n\n**What you get for ~$3000:**\n\n✅ Run **Mistral 7B** and **LLaMA 3 8B** at *full speed*  \n✅ Fine-tune Mistral 7B fast  \n✅ Run embeddings over full chat + email corpus  \n✅ Future upgrade to RTX 4090 and 128 GB RAM when needed\n\n---\n\n### 🏅 Build at ~$4000 USD (ideal long-term)\n\n| Component      | Part |\n|----------------|------|\n| **CPU**        | Ryzen 9 7950X3D |\n| **MB**         | ASUS ProArt X670E |\n| **RAM**        | 128 GB DDR5 6000 CL30 |\n| **GPU**        | RTX 4090 24 GB |\n| **SSD**        | 2 TB Samsung 990 Pro + 2 TB Crucial T700 |\n| **Cooler**     | Arctic LF III 360 |\n| **PSU**        | 1000W–1200W Platinum |\n| **Case**       | BeQuiet / Fractal / Lian Li |\n\n---\n\n**What you get for ~$4000:**\n\n✅ Run **LLaMA 70B** locally if you want  \n✅ Full fine-tune of 8B/13B/33B models  \n✅ Run 70B q4_K_M quant fine-tunes  \n✅ Huge embeddings (entire life corpus — chat + email + books)  \n✅ Basically future-proof for 3 years+\n\n---\n\n### Summary:\n\n| Budget | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| ~$3000 | Amazing 7B/8B system now; upgrade later for 70B |\n| ~$4000 | No compromise — full Todd Avatar LLM system |\n\n---\n\n### Honest advice:\n\nIf you’re already doing this work **and doing MSc Cyberpsych + books + LLM Avatar**:  \n👉 **Build the $4000 system** — it’ll last through 2027  \n👉 $3000 is a great start, but you’ll want to add 128 GB RAM + 4090 later anyway\n\n---\n\n### Example part pricing today (Ireland/DE):\n\n| Part            | € (current June 2025) |\n|-----------------|-----------------------|\n| 7950X3D         | ~€650                  |\n| ASUS X670E ProArt| ~€450                 |\n| 128 GB DDR5 kit | ~€600–€700             |\n| RTX 4090        | ~€2300–€2500           |\n| Arctic LF 360   | ~€150                  |\n| Samsung 990 Pro | ~€200                  |\n| PSU 1000W       | ~€200                  |\n| Case            | ~€200                  |\n\n→ Total €3500–€4000 (≅ $4000–$4300 USD) — depending on GPU\n\n---\n\nIf you tell me:\n\n✅ Budget ceiling right now  \n✅ Timeframe (July? August?)  \n✅ Want a ready PCPartPicker IE/UK list?\n\n…I’ll prep the exact **build BOM** for you.\n\n---\n\n**Summary advice**:  \n👉 If this is a tool for your LLM research / writing — aim for ~$4000 build now → no regrets later!\n\n---\n\nWant me to prep a full PCPartPicker list + 3K vs 4K BOM? 🚀  \nJust say **go**!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "prep the install guide"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "**Excellent — here is your first edition:**  \n\n# 🚀 **Todd LLM Avatar Workstation — Ubuntu 24.04 Install Guide**\n\n---\n\n## 🏆 **Why Ubuntu 24.04 LTS?**\n\n✅ Best performance for LLaMA 3 / Mistral / QLoRA  \n✅ Full Axolotl + Ollama + LM Studio stack  \n✅ NVIDIA driver support = perfect  \n✅ No Windows/WSL slowdown  \n✅ Stable for 3+ years — great for your MSc work + Todd LLM\n\n---\n\n## ✅ **1. Install Ubuntu 24.04 LTS**\n\n1️⃣ Download ISO:  \n👉 [https://ubuntu.com/download/desktop](https://ubuntu.com/download/desktop)  \n→ Ubuntu Desktop 24.04 LTS\n\n2️⃣ Flash USB:  \n👉 Use **Rufus** (Windows) or **balenaEtcher** (Mac/Linux)\n\n3️⃣ Install with:  \n- EXT4 filesystem  \n- 2 TB SSD → root + home  \n- Enable automatic updates  \n- **Disable Snap for core Python tools** (see below)\n\n---\n\n## ✅ **2. Post-install essentials**\n\n```bash\nsudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y\nsudo apt install -y build-essential git curl wget unzip python3-pip python3-venv\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ **3. NVIDIA Driver & CUDA**\n\n1️⃣ Install NVIDIA driver (Ubuntu 24.04 default works great):\n\n```bash\nsudo ubuntu-drivers autoinstall\n```\n\n2️⃣ Reboot:\n\n```bash\nsudo reboot\n```\n\n3️⃣ Verify:\n\n```bash\nnvidia-smi\n```\n\n→ Should show **RTX 4090** or 4080/4070 Super\n\n---\n\n4️⃣ Install CUDA Toolkit 12.4:\n\n```bash\nsudo apt install -y nvidia-cuda-toolkit\nnvcc --version\n```\n\n→ Should show **CUDA 12.4+**\n\n---\n\n## ✅ **4. PyTorch (LLaMA / Axolotl / Ollama)**\n\nCreate virtualenv (recommended):\n\n```bash\npython3 -m venv ~/llm-env\nsource ~/llm-env/bin/activate\npip install --upgrade pip\n```\n\nInstall PyTorch with CUDA:\n\n```bash\npip install torch torchvision torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124\n```\n\nVerify:\n\n```bash\npython -c \"import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available())\"\n```\n\n→ Should print `True`\n\n---\n\n## ✅ **5. Install Ollama**\n\n```bash\ncurl https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh\n```\n\n→ Adds ollama CLI\n\n---\n\n## ✅ **6. Install LM Studio (GUI)**\n\nDownload AppImage:  \n👉 [https://lmstudio.ai](https://lmstudio.ai)  \n→ Run as AppImage\n\n---\n\n## ✅ **7. Install Axolotl + QLoRA**\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/OpenAccess-AI-Collective/axolotl.git\ncd axolotl\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ **8. Install ChromaDB**\n\n```bash\npip install chromadb\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ **9. (Optional) Disable Snap for Python tools**\n\n```bash\nsudo apt purge snapd\nsudo apt autoremove --purge\nsudo apt install -y python3 python3-pip python3-venv\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 **Summary**\n\nAfter this:\n\n✅ RTX 4090 fully accelerated  \n✅ Python 3.12  \n✅ Axolotl + QLoRA ready  \n✅ Ollama ready  \n✅ LM Studio ready  \n✅ ChromaDB ready  \n✅ Full Todd LLM Avatar pipeline — GO!\n\n---\n\n## 📋 **Checklist**\n\n| Step                     | Status |\n|--------------------------|--------|\n| Ubuntu 24.04 LTS install  | ✅     |\n| NVIDIA drivers            | ✅     |\n| CUDA 12.4                 | ✅     |\n| PyTorch + CUDA            | ✅     |\n| Ollama                    | ✅     |\n| LM Studio                 | ✅     |\n| Axolotl                   | ✅     |\n| ChromaDB                  | ✅     |\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can now:\n\n✅ Write a **Markdown PDF \"Todd Avatar LLM Workstation Build Guide\"** (ready to print)  \n✅ Prep a **PCPartPicker link** — ready to order\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to generate the PDF version of this guide?  \nYou’re going to have the *perfect* Todd Avatar machine 🚀.  \nJust say **yes** — I’ll prep the PDF. ✅"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
