is can align with **<$4,000 USD**.\n\n---\n\n## 🧭 Final Choice Considerations\n\n- 🟩 **RTX 5090**: Best-in-class with future headroom—32 GB VRAM is unmatched.\n- 🟧 **RTX 4090**: Solid alternative (~€600–800 cheaper), still excellent performance.\n- 🧾 Budget control: If 5090 is over €2,800 consistently, sticking with 4090 frees up funds for SSD/backup.\n\n---\n\n## 📍 Where to Buy in EU/IE\n\n- **Mindfactory.de** – currently the best around MSRP €2,000–2,600 citeturn0search0turn0search4  \n- **Alternate.de** – beware of slight defects in Zotac stock, price ~€2,899 citeturn0news22  \n- **Caseking.de** – standard full-spec 5090 available ~€3,100 citeturn0news22  \n- **Amazon.de / UK** – cards appear occasionally around MSRP + shipping (~£1,889 in UK) citeturn0news23  \n\n_Recommendation_: Set up stock alerts on Mindfactory + Caseking for best deal.\n\n---\n\n### 🎯 Summary Recommendation\n\n- If you can grab a **5090 ~€2,500–2,700**, go for it—future-proof performance.\n- Otherwise, **4090 at ~€2,300** is still top-tier for LLM tasks.\n- Your final build (~€4,000–4,400) will handle LLaMA 70B, Mistral, embeddings, fine-tune—elite territory.\n\n---\n\n✅ Want me to lock in an actual PCPartPicker share link for this exact spec once stock is confirmed?\n🛒 Or compare detailed per-model fine-tune capacities (4090 vs 5090)?\n\nJust say the word—ready to finalize your build!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
