{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "is there a way to take that layout and turn it into a script? In fact, to take any tree layout and build the structure?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Yes — you can turn any directory layout into a working folder structure using a simple **Python script** that:\n\n- Reads a tree-like string\n- Creates directories and files accordingly\n\n---\n\n## 🧰 Here's Your Tree-to-Folder Script\n\n```python\nimport os\n\nstructure = \"\"\"\navatar-eval-suite/\n├── app.py\n├── prompts/\n│   ├── todd_eval_prefilled.jsonl\n│   └── todd_eval_blank.jsonl\n├── outputs/\n│   └── results.csv\n├── utils/\n│   └── io.py\n├── requirements.txt\n└── README.md\n\"\"\"\n\ndef create_structure(base_dir: str, structure_text: str):\n    current_dir = base_dir\n    for line in structure_text.strip().splitlines():\n        indent = len(line) - len(line.lstrip(\" │├└─\"))\n        name = line.strip(\" │├└─\")\n        if name.endswith(\"/\"):\n            current_dir = os.path.join(base_dir, *[\"..\" for _ in range(indent // 4)])  # reset path depth\n            path = os.path.join(current_dir, name.rstrip(\"/\"))\n            os.makedirs(path, exist_ok=True)\n            current_dir = path\n        else:\n            file_path = os.path.join(current_dir, name)\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(file_path), exist_ok=True)\n            with open(file_path, \"w\") as f:\n                f.write(\"\")  # Empty stub\n\n# Usage\ncreate_structure(\".\", structure)\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Output\n\nRunning this script will:\n- Make the `avatar-eval-suite/` directory\n- Create all subfolders and placeholder files\n- Ready for you to fill in content\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to:\n- Run this right now and zip the created repo?\n- Or modify the script to work from any `.txt` layout input?\n\nLet’s build your dev toolbox while we’re at it."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
