{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Okay, great! Now, how do we go from this to either a set of statements or a set of questions?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Excellent question — you're ready for the next step in transforming raw Wikipedia knowledge into usable **LLM memory input**, either as:\n\n- ✅ **Declarative statements** (for fine-tuning or embedding knowledge)\n- ✅ **Questions/answers** (for RAG, quizzes, evals, or Socratic interaction)\n\n---\n\n## 🔁 From Wikipedia Text to Statements or Questions\n\n### 🧠 Step 1: Use NLP to Split the Text\nUse `nltk` or `spacy` to break the summary into clean, well-formed **sentences**.\n\n```python\nimport nltk\nnltk.download('punkt')\nfrom nltk.tokenize import sent_tokenize\n\nsentences = sent_tokenize(summary_text)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🧾 Step 2A: Convert to Statements\n\nYou can now output each sentence as a “fact” or statement. Example:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"role\": \"system\",\n  \"content\": \"Anne McCaffrey was the first woman to win a Hugo Award for fiction.\"\n}\n```\n\nFor fine-tuning:\n```jsonl\n{\"prompt\": \"Who was the first woman to win a Hugo Award for fiction?\", \"completion\": \"Anne McCaffrey.\"}\n```\n\n---\n\n### ❓ Step 2B: Generate Questions (with Answers)\n\nHere you use a **question-generation model or prompt template**:\n\n**Template-based approach:**\n\n```python\nfor sentence in sentences:\n    if \"was born\" in sentence:\n        q = \"When was Anne McCaffrey born?\"\n        a = sentence.split(\"was born\")[1].strip('. ')\n        print(f\"Q: {q}\\nA: {a}\")\n```\n\n**Or use a model:**\n```python\nfrom transformers import pipeline\nqg = pipeline(\"text2text-generation\", model=\"valhalla/t5-base-qg-hl\")\n\nquestions = qg(f\"highlight: {sentence}\")\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🧰 Tool Mode: Auto-generator Script\n\nWould you like a script that:\n- Reads `toddmccaffrey.json`\n- Tokenizes to sentences\n- Outputs a JSONL file of either:\n  - Statements\n  - QA pairs\n\n…with a CLI s