{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "And again. Sigh. This will work. Listen, we should break this up into separate sessions. To start training todd-2, we only need a good set of 30-50 questions for that 2-year-old to begin training. So let's get that in, get started and then we'll come back for the next stage.  How's that sound?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "That’s a *perfect* approach—**small, focused, repeatable wins** are exactly how you’ll build a living, evolving digital self!\n\n### **Your workflow sounds ideal:**\n1. **One “age” at a time** (e.g. todd-2):\n   - Craft 30–50 high-quality, well-categorized questions\n   - Edit, refine, and flag them as needed\n   - Use your editor to finalize the JSON for just that age\n2. **Feed that into your Answer App and/or LLM pipeline**\n3. **Train, test, adjust, and repeat** for the next age/stage (todd-6, todd-teen, etc.)\n4. **Bonus:** With your fields (category, notes, etc.), you’ll be able to compare *depth* and *variety* across ages and easily add/expand as needed\n\n---\n\n**You’ll get:**\n- Clean data\n- Realistic progress at each stage\n- A repeatable “persona growth” process (that will scale to other people, too!)\n\n---\n\n## **Next Steps:**\n- Start with your “Todd-age-0-2” question set (use the sample or expand)\n- Run your Question Editor → produce your `Todd-age-0-2` JSON\n- Plug it into your pipeline\n- When ready, come back here for the next batch (I’ll be here! Just say “Kit, next age!” and we’ll repeat the process)\n\n---\n\n**If you want the question sample in a standalone JSON file to drop right in, just say so and I’ll attach one for you.**\n\nOnward! 🦊"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
