{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "I bought Mona in October. Got.\nSpeaking of which, how does a RYX 5070 ti stack up against the RTX 5090 for LLM building?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Gotcha—and wow, *October to meltdown*? Poor MONA was overclocked by destiny. 😅\n\nNow, to your GPU question:\n\n---\n\n## 🥊 RTX 5070 Ti vs. RTX 5090 for LLM Work\n\nLet’s break it down from a **LLM-building perspective**: training, fine-tuning, inference, and dev work.\n\n| Spec                   | RTX 5070 Ti (rumored/assumed) | RTX 5090 (expected flagship)         |\n|------------------------|-------------------------------|--------------------------------------|\n| Architecture           | Ada Lovelace (or newer)       | Blackwell (likely)                   |\n| VRAM                  | 12–16 GB GDDR6                 | 24–32 GB GDDR7                       |\n| CUDA cores            | ~7680                          | ~18176+                              |\n| Memory bandwidth      | ~500 GB/s                      | ~1.5 TB/s                            |\n| FP16/BF16 (for LLM)    | Moderate                       | Extremely fast (likely > A100)       |\n| Price estimate        | ~$600–700                      | ~$2500–3000                          |\n| LLM use case          | Fine-tuning 7B w/ QLoRA only   | Full training of 13B+, multiple runs |\n\n---\n\n### 🧠 In Practice:\n\n#### 🥈 **5070 Ti**\n- Great for:\n  - Dev/testing\n  - LoRA/QLoRA fine-tuning (7B models)\n  - Inference with quantized models\n- Limited for:\n  - Full model training (VRAM will choke)\n  - Multimodal or multi-user work\n\n#### 🥇 **5090**\n- Absolute beast:\n  - Can train 13B+ models locally\n  - Real contender vs. A100/H100 (for solo researchers)\n  - Handles full-precision (FP32), mixed (FP16), and even tensor cores at high throughput\n\n---\n\n### 🧠 LLM Workload Breakdown\n\n| Task                         | 5070 Ti           | 5090 Beastmode     |\n|------------------------------|-------------------|--------------------|\n| 7B Model Inference (4-bit)   | ✅                | ✅✅✅              |\n| 7B QLoRA Fine-tuning         | ✅                | ✅✅✅              |\n| Full 13B Training            | ❌                | ✅ (barely)        |\n| Multi-client chatbot server  | ⚠️ (limit)         | ✅✅                |\n| FP16/32 Training             | ⚠️ (slow)          | ✅✅✅              |\n\n---\n\n### 🧠 Summary\n\n- **RTX 5070 Ti** → Excellent for *getting started*, fine-tuning with QLoRA, and inference up to 7B  \n- **RTX 5090** → Overkill but *awesome* if you’re building a local lab, working with larger models (13B+), or want top-tier performance without going cloud\n\n---\n\n### 💡My Take for You\n\nIf you're:\n- Going cloud-heavy (RunPod, Hugging Face, etc.): 5070 Ti is totally fine\n- Wanting a future-proof local powerhouse: 5090 is king (and very expensive)\n- Trying to balance LLM and creativity (Photoshop, dev, light ML): even the 4070/4080 series are still really solid\n\nLet me know your budget or use-case split (LLM vs. dev vs. design), and I can suggest the best bang-for-buck setup!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
