{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "I'd prefer stick with qotd.foxxelabs.com if that's possible. Can you run me through the steps to get it into Digital Ocean and configured to our Cloudfare foxxelabs.com?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Absolutely, Todd! Using a subdomain like **qotd.foxxelabs.com** is a smart, cost-effective way to host your QOTD API on DigitalOcean and manage DNS with Cloudflare. Here’s your step-by-step guide:\n\n---\n\n# Deploy `qotd.foxxelabs.com` on DigitalOcean App Platform + Configure Cloudflare DNS\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Prepare Your QOTD API Repo\n\n- Ensure your QOTD API is pushed to GitHub with a proper `requirements.txt` and a production-ready run command (e.g., using Gunicorn or your chosen WSGI server).\n- Confirm it listens on the default port (usually 8000) and reads environment variables for config.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Create the App on DigitalOcean App Platform\n\n1. Log into DigitalOcean dashboard → **Apps** → **Create App**.\n2. Connect your GitHub repo containing QOTD API code.\n3. Select the branch to deploy (e.g., `main`).\n4. App Platform should detect it’s a Python app; if not, choose **Python** manually.\n5. Configure:\n   - **Build Command:**  \n     ```\n     pip install -r requirements.txt\n     ```\n   - **Run Command:**  \n     ```\n     gunicorn qotdapi.wsgi\n     ```  \n     *(replace `qotdapi` with your project name)*\n6. Add any necessary environment variables (e.g., Django secret key, DB URL if applicable).\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Add the Custom Domain in DigitalOcean\n\n1. In your new App’s dashboard, go to **Settings → Domains**.\n2. Click **Add Domain** and enter:  \n   ```\n   qotd.foxxelabs.com\n   ```\n3. DigitalOcean will generate the DNS records you need to add to Cloudflare.\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Configure DNS in Cloudflare\n\n1. Log in to Cloudflare dashboard.\n2. Select your domain: `foxxelabs.com`.\n3. Go to the **DNS** tab.\n4. Add a **CNAME** record:  \n   - **Name:** `qotd`  \n   - **Target:** The hostname DigitalOcean gave you (usually something like `cname.digitaloceanspaces.com` or your app URL)  \n   - Make sure the **Proxy status** is set to **Proxied** (orange cloud) for CDN and SSL.\n5. Save the record.\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: SSL/TLS Settings on Cloudflare\n\n- In Cloudflare dashboard, navigate to **SSL/TLS**.\n- Set SSL Mode to **Full (strict)** (assuming DigitalOcean app has Let’s Encrypt cert).\n- Enable **Always Use HTTPS** and **Automatic HTTPS Rewrites**.\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Wait for Propagation & Deploy\n\n- DNS changes usually propagate within minutes to a couple of hours.\n- DigitalOcean will automatically provision SSL for your custom domain.\n- Your app will be available at:  \n  ```\n  https://qotd.foxxelabs.com\n  ```\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Test and Verify\n\n- Visit `https://qotd.foxxelabs.com` to confirm your API is live and secure.\n- Check DigitalOcean App logs for any errors.\n- Test API endpoints.\n\n---\n\n## Bonus: Automate Deployment\n\n- Every push to your GitHub repo’s chosen branch will trigger a new build and deployment automatically.\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can generate:\n\n- Exact commands and environment variable templates.\n- Cloudflare DNS record screenshots or export config.\n- Troubleshooting tips for common DNS and SSL issues.\n\n---\n\nReady to start adding the subdomain to DigitalOcean and Cloudflare now?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
