{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Rats! Can't confirm on qotd until that's completed. I'm really keen to get both it and surveyhub deployed today.  That gives me proof of ability and a calling card site (also it lets us start generating surveys and that's a huge win)."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Totally understand, Todd — getting that export done is the immediate bottleneck, but once it's complete, you’ll have a clear path to deploy both SurveyHub and the QOTD API today!\n\n---\n\n## Quick Game Plan for After Export Completes\n\n### 1. **SurveyHub Deployment**\n- Finalize environment variables (DB, Redis, SMTP2GO).\n- Fix STATIC_ROOT and ensure static files serve properly.\n- Deploy to DigitalOcean App Platform with managed Postgres and Redis.\n- Add your domain (`foxxelabs.com`), configure DNS in Cloudflare.\n- Verify Celery worker runs.\n\n### 2. **QOTD API Deployment**\n- Connect Git repo to DigitalOcean App Platform.\n- Add subdomain `qotd.foxxelabs.com` in App Platform.\n- Set DNS CNAME in Cloudflare to point to DigitalOcean app.\n- Set SSL to Full (strict) in Cloudflare.\n- Test API.\n\n### 3. **Early Survey Generation**\n- Once SurveyHub is live, start creating and distributing surveys.\n- Use the newsletter system to collect respondents and grow your list.\n\n---\n\n## I’ll be ready to help with:\n\n- Step-by-step deployment guides  \n- DNS and SSL configuration  \n- Debugging any build/deploy errors  \n- Setting up Celery and background tasks  \n- Survey setup and newsletter integration\n\n---\n\n**Keep me posted as soon as your export finishes — we’ll hit the ground running!**"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
