th recent HuggingFace, PyTorch, and LLM workflows (especially with big models and LoRA adapters):\n\n```\nNotImplementedError: Cannot copy out of meta tensor; no data! Please use torch.nn.Module.to_empty() instead of torch.nn.Module.to() when moving module from meta to a different device.\n```\n\n---\n\n## **What does it mean?**\n\n- Some model weights **remain on the \"meta\" device** (i.e., placeholder, not real RAM/GPU).\n- This is a recent change in HuggingFace Transformers to enable **\"low RAM\" loading**—but many trainer/utilities aren’t yet compatible.\n- The `Trainer` tries to move the model to the GPU/CPU, but some parameters aren’t loaded (\"meta\" tensors), so `.to()` fails.\n\n---\n\n## **How to fix?**\n\n**Short answer:**  \nYou must ensure all weights are loaded onto a real device (CPU/GPU) **before** passing to `Trainer`.\n\n---\n\n### **Checklist of solutions:**\n\n1. **Load your model with `low_cpu_mem_usage=False` (if you have enough RAM):**\n\n   ```python\n   model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n       model_name,\n       low_cpu_mem_usage=False,   # <-- Add this!\n       torch_dtype=torch.float16, # Or bfloat16, as appropriate\n       device_map=None            # Explicitly load on CPU by default\n   )\n   ```\n   - This will **fully load the weights** into RAM and avoid \"meta\" tensors.\n\n2. **If you must use `device_map=\"auto\"` or `low_cpu_mem_usage=True` (low RAM),**\n   - You may need to **\"materialize\"** the model before passing to `Trainer`.\n   - But most users with RAM > model size can just set `low_cpu_mem_usage=False`.\n\n3. **Check if you are using `peft` (for LoRA):**\n   - Some PEFT workflows have their own model loading requirements.\n\n4. **If you’re using quantization (like bitsandbytes):**\n   - Make sure you use the correct arguments for `from_pretrained`.\n\n---\n\n### **Example:**\n\n```python\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer\n\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n    \"mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.1\",\n    low_cpu_mem_usage=False,   # <-- disables meta tensors\n    torch_dtype=torch.float16, # or omit if not using\n)\n\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.1\")\n# ...rest of your LoRA setup...\n```\n\n---\n\n### **If you *must* use \"meta\" tensors (RAM constrained, advanced):**\nYou must **materialize** the weights before Trainer.  \nBut for most workflows, simply **disable** `low_cpu_mem_usage` (i.e., set `low_cpu_mem_usage=False`).\n\n---\n\n## **What to do:**\n\n1. **Edit your model loading code to include `low_cpu_mem_usage=False`.**\n2. **Rerun your script.**\n3. **If you still see errors, paste your model loading code here for a tweak!**\n\n---\n\n## **Final Tip:**  \nIf your GPU RAM is low, use smaller models, or upgrade to a machine with more RAM/VRAM.\n\n---\n\n**Try the above fix and let me know if it runs!  \nIf it still fails, paste the snippet of code where you load your model.**"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
