      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/todd/linux/Projects/todd/Con00/wereEnv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/django/apps/config.py\", line 212, in create\n    raise ImproperlyConfigured(\ndjango.core.exceptions.ImproperlyConfigured: Cannot import 'WeRead'. Check that 'weread.apps.WereadConfig.name' is correct."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "**Classic Django renaming gotcha!**  \nDjango is still looking for `WeRead` somewhere (probably in your `INSTALLED_APPS` or, more likely, in your `weread/apps.py` file).\n\n---\n\n## **How to Fix:**\n\n### 1. **Check `INSTALLED_APPS` in `settings.py`**\n\n- Make sure you have **`'weread'`** (all lowercase), not `'WeRead'`.\n\n```python\nINSTALLED_APPS = [\n    # ...\n    \"rest_framework\",\n    \"weread\",  # <-- must be all lowercase and match folder name\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Fix `weread/apps.py`**\n\n- Open `weread/apps.py`.  \n  By default, Django generates this for a new app:\n\n```python\nfrom django.apps import AppConfig\n\nclass WereadConfig(AppConfig):\n    default_auto_field = 'django.db.models.BigAutoField'\n    name = 'weread'  # <-- THIS MUST MATCH your folder name and INSTALLED_APPS\n```\n\n- If it says `name = 'WeRead'` or `name = 'Wearead'`, change it to all lowercase:  \n  ```python\n  name = 'weread'\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Remove Any `WeRead` Artifacts**\n\n- If you see old folders or pycache directories like `WeRead/` or `WeRead/__pycache__`, you can safely delete them.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Restart Your Shell/Environment**\n\n- Sometimes, VSCode or other editors keep old pycache files open.  \n  After fixing the files above, run:\n  ```bash\n  find . -name \"__pycache__\" -exec rm -rf {} +\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Try Again**\n\n```bash\npython manage.py makemigrations\npython manage.py migrate\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Summary Checklist**\n- Folder is named `weread`\n- App is called `'weread'` everywhere (not `'WeRead'`)\n- `weread/apps.py` says `name = 'weread'`\n- `INSTALLED_APPS` is lowercase: 