{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "okay, let's try that."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect — here is the ready-to-go script for you:\n\n---\n\n### `extract_quotes_from_rtf.py`\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport json\nfrom striprtf.striprtf import rtf_to_text\n\n# Set your input + output files here:\nINPUT_RTF = \"Ellay 025 indent.rtf\"\nOUTPUT_JSON = \"ellay_quotes_from_rtf.json\"\n\n# Load RTF file\nwith open(INPUT_RTF, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\") as f:\n    rtf_content = f.read()\n\n# Extract plain text\nplain_text = rtf_to_text(rtf_content)\n\n# Split into lines and strip whitespace\nlines = [line.strip() for line in plain_text.split('\\n') if line.strip()]\n\n# Heuristics for good quotes:\n# - Dialogue (starts with “ or \")\n# - Punchy one-liners (short narrative sentences)\nquote_candidates = []\n\nfor line in lines:\n    if len(line) < 20:\n        continue\n    # Dialogue\n    if re.match(r'^[“\"](.*)[”\"]$', line):\n        quote_candidates.append(line)\n    # Short narrative sentences (under 140 chars, ends with .!?)\n    elif len(line) < 140 and line[-1] in '.!?':\n        if not re.match(r'^Chapter \\d+', line, re.I):\n            quote_candidates.append(line)\n\n# Deduplicate\nquote_candidates = list(dict.fromkeys(quote_candidates))\n\n# Limit to 50 best\nselected_quotes = quote_candidates[:50]\n\n# Format for QOTD app\nellay_quotes = [\n    {\n        \"quote\": quote,\n        \"author\": \"ELLAY: The First AI\",\n        \"url\": \"\",\n        \"source\": \"ELLAY Novel\"\n    }\n    for quote in selected_quotes\n]\n\n# Save JSON\nwith open(OUTPUT_JSON, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump(ellay_quotes, f, indent=4, ensure_ascii=False)\n\nprint(f\"✅ Extracted {len(ellay_quotes)} quotes to {OUTPUT_JSON}\")\n```\n\n---\n\n### How to run it:\n\n1️⃣ Install the needed package:\n\n```bash\npip install striprtf\n```\n\n2️⃣ Place this script in the same folder as your `.rtf` file  \n(or edit `INPUT_RTF` to point to the right place)\n\n3️⃣ Run:\n\n```bash\npython extract_quotes_from_rtf.py\n```\n\n---\n\n**Result:**  \nYou’ll get: `ellay_quotes_from_rtf.json` — ready to import into your QOTD app.\n\n---\n\n**Would you also like me to generate:**  \n✅ a version that can pull **more than 50** (say, 100 or 200)  \n✅ a version that lets you choose \"voice\" or \"tag\" per batch  \n✅ a version that outputs line numbers / locations (so you can track source in your text)\n\nJust say *yes, please!* 🚀  \nWant me to package the script into a full zip and upload for you? I can do that too!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "first, let's swtch it up to take ANY filename (in .rtf format) and output <filename>_quotd.json\n(and you've got a bit of a problem with ZIP, so let's not)\nCan you roll in the \"voice\" \"tag\" on the command line? How do you plan to handle line numbers/locations?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great upgrades — here’s how I would design it for you:\n\n---\n\n### 🛠 Features:\n\n✅ **Any filename** as argument:\n\n```bash\npython extract_quotes_from_rtf.py Ellay025-indent.rtf\n```\n\n→ output: `Ellay025-indent_qotd.json`\n\n✅ Optional **voice** + **tag** on command line:\n\n```bash\npython extract_quotes_from_rtf.py Ellay025-indent.rtf --voice \"ELLAY: The First AI\" --tag \"ELLAY Novel\"\n```\n\n✅ **Line numbers / locations**:  \nRTF files are “stream” — no real line numbers. But:  \n- I can return **line number in extracted plain text**  \n- OR **position** (character offset, % through doc)\n\n**Option 1 (easiest):** add `\"line_number\": NNN` to each quote  \n**Option 2:** add `\"position_percent\": 23.5` — where in doc it appeared\n\n---\n\n### Here's the updated script:\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport json\nimport argparse\nfrom striprtf.striprtf import rtf_to_text\n\n# CLI arguments\nparser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Extract quotes from RTF file for QOTD app.\")\nparser.add_argument(\"filename\", help=\"Input RTF file\")\nparser.add_argument(\"--voice\", default=\"ELLAY: The First AI\", help=\"Voice/author name\")\nparser.add_argument(\"--tag\", default=\"ELLAY Novel\", help=\"Source tag\")\nparser.add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=50, help=\"Max number of quotes\")\nargs = parser.parse_args()\n\n# Output filename: <input>_qotd.json\noutput_json = re.sub(r'\\.rtf$', '_qotd.json', args.filename, flags=re.I)\n\n# Load RTF\nwith open(args.filename, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\") as f:\n    rtf_content = f.read()\n\nplain_text = rtf_to_text(rtf_content)\n\n# Split lines\nlines = [line.strip() for line in plain_text.split('\\n') if line.strip()]\n\n# Build candidates with line numbers\nquote_candidates = []\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    if len(line) < 20:\n        continue\n    # Dialogue\n    if re.match(r'^[“\"](.*)[”\"]$', line):\n        quote_candidates.append((i+1, line))\n    # Punchy one-liner\n    elif len(line) < 140 and line[-1] in '.!?':\n        if not re.match(r'^Chapter \\d+', line, re.I):\n            quote_candidates.append((i+1, line))\n\n# Deduplicate\nseen = set()\nunique_quotes = []\nfor lineno, quote in quote_candidates:\n    if quote not in seen:\n        unique_quotes.append((lineno, quote))\n        seen.add(quote)\n\n# Limit\nselected = unique_quotes[:args.limit]\n\n# Format output\nellay_quotes = [\n    {\n        \"quote\": q,\n        \"author\": args.voice,\n        \"url\": \"\",\n        \"source\": args.tag,\n        \"line_number\": lineno\n    }\n    for lineno, q in selected\n]\n\n# Save JSON\nwith open(output_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump(ellay_quotes, f, indent=4, ensure_ascii=False)\n\nprint(f\"✅ Extracted {len(ellay_quotes)} quotes from {args.filename} → {output_json}\")\n```\n\n---\n\n### Usage examples:\n\n**Default 50 quotes:**\n\n```bash\npython extract_quotes_from_rtf.py Ellay025-indent.rtf\n```\n\n**With custom voice + tag:**\n\n```bash\npython extract_quotes_from_rtf.py Ellay025-indent.rtf --voice \"ELLAY: The First AI\" --tag \"Core Logs\"\n```\n\n**More quotes (say 100):**\n\n```bash\npython extract_quotes_from_rtf.py Ellay025-indent.rtf --limit 100\n```\n\n---\n\n### Line numbers:\n\n- `\"line_number\": NNN` → where it appeared in **plain text**\n- That gives you **traceability** back to the `.rtf`\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to also:\n\n✅ Add **--percent** field (% position through file)  \n✅ Add **verbose mode** to show which quotes were picked  \n✅ Add **random shuffle** so you can re-run and pull different ones\n\n---\n\nIf you say **yes please**, I’ll post full final version 🚀  \nWould you like it?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "yes please. Add a random shuffle, too, please."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "You got it — here is the **final version** with all features:\n\n---\n\n### `extract_quotes_from_rtf.py`\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport json\nimport argparse\nimport random\nfrom striprtf.striprtf import rtf_to_text\n\n# CLI arguments\nparser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Extract quotes from RTF file for QOTD app.\")\nparser.add_argument(\"filename\", help=\"Input RTF file\")\nparser.add_argument(\"--voice\", default=\"ELLAY: The First AI\", help=\"Voice/author name\")\nparser.add_argument(\"--tag\", default=\"ELLAY Novel\", help=\"Source tag\")\nparser.add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=50, help=\"Max number of quotes\")\nparser.add_argument(\"--verbose\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Show selected quotes\")\nargs = parser.parse_args()\n\n# Output filename: <input>_qotd.json\noutput_json = re.sub(r'\\.rtf$', '_qotd.json', args.filename, flags=re.I)\n\n# Load RTF\nwith open(args.filename, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\") as f:\n    rtf_content = f.read()\n\nplain_text = rtf_to_text(rtf_content)\n\n# Split lines\nlines = [line.strip() for line in plain_text.split('\\n') if line.strip()]\ntotal_lines = len(lines)\n\n# Build candidates with line numbers and position %\nquote_candidates = []\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    if len(line) < 20:\n        continue\n    # Dialogue\n    if re.match(r'^[“\"](.*)[”\"]$', line):\n        pos_percent = (i+1) / total_lines * 100\n        quote_candidates.append((i+1, pos_percent, line))\n    # Punchy one-liner\n    elif len(line) < 140 and line[-1] in '.!?':\n        if not re.match(r'^Chapter \\d+', line, re.I):\n            pos_percent = (i+1) / total_lines * 100\n            quote_candidates.append((i+1, pos_percent, line))\n\n# Deduplicate\nseen = set()\nunique_quotes = []\nfor lineno, percent, quote in quote_candidates:\n    if quote not in seen:\n        unique_quotes.append((lineno, percent, quote))\n        seen.add(quote)\n\n# Shuffle so each run is different\nrandom.shuffle(unique_quotes)\n\n# Limit\nselected = unique_quotes[:args.limit]\n\n# Format output\nellay_quotes = [\n    {\n        \"quote\": q,\n        \"author\": args.voice,\n        \"url\": \"\",\n        \"source\": args.tag,\n        \"line_number\": lineno,\n        \"position_percent\": round(percent, 2)\n    }\n    for lineno, percent, q in selected\n]\n\n# Save JSON\nwith open(output_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump(ellay_quotes, f, indent=4, ensure_ascii=False)\n\nprint(f\"✅ Extracted {len(ellay_quotes)} quotes from {args.filename} → {output_json}\")\n\n# Verbose output\nif args.verbose:\n    print(\"\\nSelected Quotes:\\n\")\n    for q in ellay_quotes:\n        print(f\"[Line {q['line_number']} | {q['position_percent']}%] {q['quote']}\\n\")\n```\n\n---\n\n### Recap of new features:\n\n✅ Supports **any filename**  \n✅ Outputs `<filename>_qotd.json`  \n✅ `--voice` and `--tag` CLI args  \n✅ `--limit` (how many quotes)  \n✅ **Shuffles** results (different quotes each run)  \n✅ Adds `\"line_number\"` and `\"position_percent\"` for traceability  \n✅ `--verbose` option to print quotes to terminal\n\n---\n\n### Example run:\n\n```bash\npython extract_quotes_from_rtf.py Ellay025-indent.rtf --voice \"ELLAY: The First AI\" --tag \"Core Logs\" --limit 75 --verbose\n```\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can also add:\n\n✅ Option to output to **custom path**  \n✅ Option to log **all found candidates** to a text file (so you can pick manually)\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to prep the next version with those?  \n**You’ve got a super useful little QOTD quote-extractor now!** 🚀"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
