hip with author & developer Todd McCaffrey — while building the “Django + ChatGPT for Teens” course.\n\n---\n\n**Why this matters:**  \nAI tools like ChatGPT can massively boost the creativity and productivity of educators — and change how we teach and learn.\n\n---\n\nBuilt with ChatGPT 🚀\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✏️ 3️⃣ First Lesson — \"How to Outline Your Course with ChatGPT\"\n\n```markdown\n# Lesson 1 — How to Outline Your Course with ChatGPT\n\n**Objective:**  \nLearn how to use ChatGPT to brainstorm and outline your own online course.\n\n---\n\n## 1️⃣ Choose your course topic\n\n- What do you want to teach?\n- Who is your audience?\n\nExample prompt:  \n> \"I want to create a beginner course on X for Y audience. Help me brainstorm an outline.\"\n\n---\n\n## 2️⃣ Identify learning outcomes\n\nPrompt:  \n> \"What are good learning outcomes for a course on X?\"\n\n---\n\n## 3️⃣ Build a section structure\n\nPrompt:  \n> \"Please suggest 6–10 sections for a course on X.\"\n\n---\n\n## 4️⃣ Refine with ChatGPT\n\n- Ask:  \n  - \"What are typical mistakes learners make?\"  \n  - \"What interactive projects could students build?\"\n\n---\n\n## 5️⃣ Save your draft\n\nBy end of Lesson 1 you will have:  \n✅ Course topic  \n✅ Audience  \n✅ Outcomes  \n✅ Section list  \n✅ Ideas for projects\n\n---\n\n## Next: How to structure content and learning objectives (Lesson 2)\n\n```\n\n---\n\n✅ All delivered! 🚀  \n✅ Tracking BOTH COURSES now:\n\n1️⃣ Django + ChatGPT for Teens — **Project Memory saved**  \n2️⃣ How to Design a Course with ChatGPT — **Meta-Course Project Memory saved**\n\n---\n\n**Next:**\n\nIf you want, I can now:\n\n✅ Generate **course calendars** (6 weeks / 8 weeks) for both  \n✅ Draft **Teacher Guide** for the teen course  \n✅ Draft **Final Showcase checklist** (what students present)  \n✅ Draft **Meta-course Final Project Template** (how learners design their own course with ChatGPT)\n\n---\n\nShall I? 🚀  \nYou are building two awesome and truly *leading-edge* courses!  