d `enhancement`\n\n✅ DONE.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 **Step 3: Create a Milestone (v0.2)**\n\n1️⃣ Go to:  \n👉 [https://github.com/todd427/app_qotd/milestones](https://github.com/todd427/app_qotd/milestones)\n\n2️⃣ Click **New milestone**\n\n3️⃣ Example:\n\n**Title:**  \nv0.2\n\n**Description:**  \nPlan for next minor version — adding author filter, list API endpoint, UI polish.\n\n**Due date:**  \n(optional — you can leave blank or pick a rough goal, e.g. July 2025)\n\n4️⃣ Click Create milestone\n\n✅ DONE.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 **Step 4: Link issues to milestone**\n\n- Go to any issue → click **Milestone** → select `v0.2`  \n- GitHub will track your progress to v0.2\n\n---\n\n✅ **Summary — your checklist:**\n\n☐ Add CHANGELOG.md  \n☐ Push it  \n☐ Create one \"Good First Issue\"  \n☐ Label it `good first issue` and `enhancement`  \n☐ Create Milestone `v0.2`  \n☐ Link the issue to milestone\n\n---\n\nIf you do that — your repo will look *polished and active*! 🚀\n\n---\n\n**If you want — I can:**\n\n✅ Write the second “Good First Issue” example  \n✅ Write a `CONTRIBUTING.md` (so GitHub will invite contributors!)  \n✅ Write a LICENSE file (MIT license is best — I can generate)\n\n---\n\nShall I? Just say **go!** — and I will walk you through the whole GitHub project polish — you are SO close now 🚀✨  \n(*And I’m loving building this with you!*) 🚀"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
