nlocked\n  File \"<frozen importlib._bootstrap>\", line 935, in _load_unlocked\n  File \"<frozen importlib._bootstrap_external>\", line 995, in exec_module\n  File \"<frozen importlib._bootstrap>\", line 488, in _call_with_frames_removed\n  File \"/home/todd/linux/src/surveyhub/surveyhub/settings/drd.py\", line 13, in <module>\n    raise RuntimeError(\"SECRET_KEY environment variable is not set!\")\nRuntimeError: SECRET_KEY environment variable is not set!"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Your debug output is **very helpful**. Here’s what we know and what to fix:\n\n---\n\n### **What’s Happening**\n\n- **Your code prints:**\n    - `os.path.dirname(__file__)` is `/home/todd/linux/src/surveyhub/surveyhub/settings`\n    - The `dotenv_path` resolved is `/home/todd/linux/src/surveyhub/surveyhub/settings/../.env.local`\n    - So, **your code is looking for `.env.local` in `/home/todd/linux/src/surveyhub/surveyhub/.env.local`**\n    - **BUT**, your actual `.env.local` is almost certainly in your project root (`/home/todd/linux/src/surveyhub/.env.local`), not in the inner `surveyhub` dir.\n\n---\n\n### **What’s the Problem?**\n\n**You're loading the environment file from the wrong location.**\n\nYour current code does:\n```python\ndotenv_path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), '..', dotenv_file)\n```\nThat expands to:  \n`/home/todd/linux/src/surveyhub/surveyhub/settings/../.env.local`  \nWhich is:  \n`/home/todd/linux/src/surveyhub/surveyhub/.env.local`  \n\n**But your .env.local is here:**  \n`/home/todd/linux/src/surveyhub/.env.local`\n\n---\n\n## **How to Fix**\n\n### 1. **Correct the Path to .env.local**\nChange your `drd.py` so the dotenv path is relative to the project root, like this:\n\n```python\nimport os\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\n# Go two levels up from settings/\nBASE_DIR = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(__file__)))  # surveyhub/\ndotenv_file = os.environ.get(\"DJANGO_ENV_FILE\", \".env.local\")\ndotenv_path = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, dotenv_file)\nprint(\"Looking for dotenv at:\", dotenv_path)\nload_dotenv(dotenv_path=dotenv_path)\n\nSECRET_KEY = os.environ.get(\"SECRET_KEY\")\nif not SECRET_KEY:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"SECRET_KEY environment variable is not set!\")\n```\n- Now it will correctly look in `/home/todd/linux/src/surveyhub/.env.local`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Alternatively, move your `.env.local`**\n\nIf you want to keep the current code, you could move `.env.local` into `/home/todd/linux/src/surveyhub/surveyhub/`.  \n**But it's more standard to keep it in the project root**.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Check for Success**\n\nAfter changing the path, rerun:\n\n```bash\npython manage.py runserver --settings=surveyhub.settings.drd\n```\n\nYou should see the correct value printed, and **no error** about the missing `SECRET_KEY`.\n\n---\n\n## **TL;DR**\n\n- **Fix your `dotenv_path`** so it points to your project root, not inside `settings/`.\n- **Best practice:** Keep your `.env.local` in the project root (alongside `manage.py`).\n\n---\n\nWant the exact code block to copy into `drd.py`? Let me know if so!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
