{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "for the loaddata, don't we need to specify the settings? \"--settings=surveyhub.settings.drd\", right?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "**Yes, absolutely!**  \nIf you’re running with a non-default settings module (like your custom `drd` for debug with Postgres), always specify it with `--settings=surveyhub.settings.drd`.\n\nSo, your loaddata command should be:\n\n```bash\npython manage.py loaddata quiz_fixture.json --settings=surveyhub.settings.drd\n```\n\n**General rule:**  \nWhenever you’re running a Django management command and not using the default `settings.py`, you should add `--settings=...` to be sure you’re operating on the right database and config.\n\nIf you don’t specify it, Django uses the default from `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` (often `surveyhub.settings`), which may point to your SQLite DB or dev settings.\n\n---\n\n**Migration Checklist Update:**\n\n- Add `--settings=surveyhub.settings.drd` to any management command when using a custom settings file.\n\nLet me know if you want this update reflected in your running checklist!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
