{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "if [[ \"$ACTION\" =~ ^(prod|drd|local|custom)$ ]]; then\nprepDocker.sh: 87: Syntax error: \"(\" unexpected (expecting \"then\")"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "That error usually means your shell is using **`sh`**, not **`bash`**.  \n**`[[ ... =~ ... ]]`** and the use of **parentheses in the regex** are Bash-specific features—they **do not work in `/bin/sh`**.\n\n### How to Fix\n\n1. **Shebang**  \n   The **very first line** of your script **must** be:\n   ```bash\n   #!/bin/bash\n   ```\n   Not `#!/bin/sh` and not missing.\n\n2. **How you run it**  \n   Always run your script like this (so it uses Bash):\n   ```bash\n   ./prepDocker.sh\n   ```\n   **or:**\n   ```bash\n   bash prepDocker.sh\n   ```\n   If you run it as:\n   ```bash\n   sh prepDocker.sh\n   ```\n   It will use `/bin/sh` which **does not support Bash features**.\n\n3. **Double-check script permissions:**\n   ```bash\n   chmod +x prepDocker.sh\n   ```\n\n4. **If you must support `/bin/sh`:**\n   - Use `case ... esac` instead of `[[ ... =~ ... ]]`,  \n   - Or just use plain `[` `]` tests (less powerful).\n\n---\n\n## Example\n**Wrong:**\n```bash\nif [[ \"$ACTION\" =~ ^(prod|drd|local|custom)$ ]]; then\n```\n**Right (bash only):**\n```bash\nif [[ \"$ACTION\" =~ ^(prod|drd|local|custom)$ ]]; then\n```\n**Right (POSIX, works in sh):**\n```bash\ncase \"$ACTION\" in\n  prod|drd|local|custom)\n    # do stuff\n    ;;\nesac\n```\n\n---\n\n### **TL;DR**\n\n- Make sure your script starts with `#!/bin/bash`\n- Do **not** run it with `sh prepDocker.sh`\n- Use `bash prepDocker.sh` or `./prepDocker.sh`\n\n---\n\nIf you follow those, your script should work.  \nLet me know if you still get errors!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
