{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "File \"/home/todd/linux/src/pics/classifier/management/commands/scanimages.py\", line 2, in <module>\n    from classifier.utils import scan_and_upload_images_from_path\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'classifier.utils'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Boom — that's the real issue! 🧨 Django can’t find `classifier.utils` because you haven’t actually created a `utils.py` file in the `classifier/` directory.\n\nLet’s fix that cleanly.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Fix: Create `utils.py` in `classifier/`\n\nRun this:\n\n```bash\ntouch classifier/utils.py\n```\n\nThen open `classifier/utils.py` and move or copy this function into it:\n\n```python\nimport os\nfrom django.core.files import File\nfrom classifier.models import Image\nfrom .views import classify_image  # or wherever your classify_image function lives\n\ndef scan_and_upload_images_from_path(root_dir):\n    for root, _, files in os.walk(root_dir):\n        for filename in files:\n            if filename.lower().endswith(('.png', '.jpg', '.jpeg', '.gif', '.bmp')):\n                full_path = os.path.join(root, filename)\n                relative_path = os.path.relpath(full_path, root_dir)\n                try:\n                    with open(full_path, 'rb') as f:\n                        image_instance = Image()\n                        image_instance.file.save(relative_path.replace(os.sep, '_'), File(f), save=False)\n                        image_instance.label = classify_image(image_instance.file.path)\n                        image_instance.save()\n                        print(f\"Uploaded and classified: {relative_path} -> {image_instance.label}\")\n                except Exception as e:\n                    print(f\"Failed to upload {relative_path}: {e}\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Then: Try again\n\n```bash\npython manage.py scanimages ~/Downloads\n```\n\nAnd this time… it should work 🎉\n\nWant me to generate the `utils.py` file automatically for you?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
