{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "where does my classify_image function live"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great question — based on your current code setup (from the canvas), your `classify_image` function is defined directly in the same file that contains your views and model:\n\n### 📍 Location:\nIt's currently in the main `classifier/views.py` (or a combined logic file), like this:\n\n```python\n# inside classifier/views.py or similar\n\nmodel = MobileNetV2(weights='imagenet')\n\ndef classify_image(img_path):\n    img = keras_image.load_img(img_path, target_size=(224, 224))\n    x = keras_image.img_to_array(img)\n    x = np.expand_dims(x, axis=0)\n    x = preprocess_input(x)\n    preds = model.predict(x)\n    return decode_predictions(preds, top=1)[0][0][1]  # Top label\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Best Practice: Move `classify_image` to `utils.py`\n\nSince it's a utility function and not a view, let’s move it from your views module to `classifier/utils.py`.\n\n---\n\n### ✂️ In `classifier/utils.py`, paste at the top:\n\n```python\nfrom tensorflow.keras.applications.mobilenet_v2 import preprocess_input, decode_predictions, MobileNetV2\nfrom tensorflow.keras.preprocessing import image as keras_image\nimport numpy as np\n\nmodel = MobileNetV2(weights='imagenet')\n\ndef classify_image(img_path):\n    img = keras_image.load_img(img_path, target_size=(224, 224))\n    x = keras_image.img_to_array(img)\n    x = np.expand_dims(x, axis=0)\n    x = preprocess_input(x)\n    preds = model.predict(x)\n    return decode_predictions(preds, top=1)[0][0][1]\n```\n\nNow both `scan_and_upload_images_from_path()` and `classify_image()` live in `utils.py`.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Update Any Files Using `classify_image`\n\nIn `views.py`, change:\n\n```python\nfrom .views import classify_image\n```\n\nto:\n\n```python\nfrom .utils import classify_image\n```\n\n---\n\nOnce you've done that, everything will be properly modular and Django will be able to locate all the pieces