tance = super().save(commit=False)\\n        selected_tags = self.cleaned_data.get('tags_field', [])\\n        instance.tags = ', '.join(sorted(set(selected_tags)))\\n        if commit:\\n            instance.save()\\n        return instance\\n\\n# Views for listing and editing images with multi-tag filters, sort\n\nYou're trying to push to GitHub and got this error:\n\n```\nERROR: Permission to todd427/pics.git denied to deploy key\nfatal: Could not read from remote repository.\n```\n\nThis means your Git push is being blocked because it's using a **deploy key** instead of your personal key or GitHub login.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Fix: Use Your Personal SSH Key or HTTPS\n\n### Option 1: Use **HTTPS** instead of SSH\n\nReplace your remote with an HTTPS URL:\n\n```bash\ngit remote set-url origin https://github.com/todd427/pics.git\n```\n\nThen try:\n\n```bash\ngit push --set-upstream origin main\n```\n\nYou'll be prompted for your **GitHub username and a personal access token (PAT)**, not your password.\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Use a Valid SSH Key\n\nIf you want to use SSH (recommended for long term), do this:\n\n1. **Check your current SSH key:**\n   ```bash\n   cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub\n   ```\n\n2. **Copy the output** and add it to GitHub:\n   - Go to: https://github.com/settings/keys\n   - Click **“New SSH key”**\n   - Paste your key and name it (e.g., `mona-dev`)\n\n3. Verify it:\n   ```bash\n   ssh -T git@github.com\n   ```\n\n   You should see:\n   > Hi todd427! You've successfully authenticated.\n\n4. Then push:\n   ```bash\n   git push --set-upstream origin main\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### Want to Start Fresh?\n\nIf you'd rather clone the repo fresh with HTTPS:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/todd427/pics.git\ncd pics\n```\n\n---\n\nWould you like help switching to the HTTPS method or checking your SSH keys?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
