*—and this is the real cause of your `\"not found in manifest/items, skipping\"` warnings and the final **lxml.etree.ParserError: Document is empty**.\n\n### Here’s why:\n- InDesign puts `<itemref idref=\"Cody-s_War_-_test-1\" linear=\"yes\"/>` in the `<spine>`.\n- That refers to a manifest item `<item id=\"Cody-s_War_-_test-1\" href=\"Cody%27s_War_-_test-1.xhtml\" .../>`\n- **EbookLib’s `book.spine` yields tuples** like `('Cody-s_War_-_test-1', 'yes')`\n- You **must use the manifest `id`** as your spine reference, NOT the file name, NOT a tuple.\n\n**But right now your code is accidentally looking for manifest IDs as tuples** like `('Cody-s_War_-_test-1', 'yes')`, which won’t ever match your manifest items.\n\n---\n\n## **What’s the solution?**\n- **Extract the manifest idref from the tuple.**\n- **Ignore the second element (\"yes\") in the tuple.**\n- **Map your XHTML docs by ID.**\n- **Assemble the new spine using those IDs (and objects).**\n\n---\n\n### **Here’s the fixed spine-assembly loop:**\n\nReplace this block:\n```python\nspine_ids = [entry for entry in book.spine if entry != \"nav\"]\n# Insert our signature page after the first item (second page)\nnew_spine_ids = [spine_ids[0], \"signature_page\"] + spine_ids[1:]\n\n# Build the new spine list of objects (can include 'nav' at start if present)\nnew_spine = []\nif book.spine and book.spine[0] == \"nav\":\n    new_spine.append(\"nav\")\nfor idref in new_spine_ids:\n    doc = id_to_doc.get(idref)\n    if doc:\n        new_spine.append(doc)\n    else:\n        print(f\"Warning: {idref} not found in manifest/items, skipping.\")\n```\n\nWith this:\n```python\n# Helper: flatten spine entries to just manifest ids\ndef get_idref(entry):\n    if entry == \"nav\":\n        return \"nav\"\n    elif isinstance(entry, tuple):\n        return entry[0]  # ID is first element\n    else:\n        return entry\n\nspine_ids = [get_idref(entry) for entry in book.spine if get_idref(entry) != \"nav\"]\n\n# Insert signature page after the first\nnew_spine_ids = [spine_ids[0], \"signature_page\"] + spine_ids[1:]\n\n# Map all XHTML docs by ID\nid_to_doc = {item.get_id(): item for item in book.get_items() if getattr(item, \"media_type\", \"\") == \"application/xhtml+xml\"}\nid_to_doc[\"signature_page\"] = sig_page\n\n# Build the new spine\nnew_spine = [\"nav\"] if any(get_idref(e) == \"nav\" for e in book.spine) else []\nfor idref in new_spine_ids:\n    doc = id_to_doc.get(idref)\n    if doc:\n        new_spine.append(doc)\n    else:\n        print(f\"Warning: {idref} not found in manifest/items, skipping.\")\n\nbook.spine = new_spine\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Summary**\n- Always extract the manifest ID (`entry[0]` from a tuple) when reading `book.spine`.\n- Use manifest IDs, not file names or tuples, for matching and for the new spine.\n\n---\n\n## **Super Simple Drop-In (Full Loop)**\n**Replace your spine extraction/loop with this:**\n\n```python\ndef get_idref(entry):\n    if entry == \"nav\":\n        return \"nav\"\n    elif isinstance(entry, tuple):\n        return entry[0]\n    else:\n        return entry\n\nspine_ids = [get_idref(entry) for entry in book.spine if get_idref(entry) != \"nav\"]\nnew_spine_ids = [spine_ids[0], \"signature_page\"] + spine_ids[1:]\n\nid_to_doc = {item.get_id(): item for item in book.get_items() if getattr(item, \"media_type\", \"\") == \"application/xhtml+xml\"}\nid_to_doc[\"signature_page\"] = sig_page\n\nnew_spine = [\"nav\"] if any(get_idref(e) == \"nav\" for e in book.spine) else []\nfor idref in new_spine_ids:\n    doc = id_to_doc.get(idref)\n    if doc:\n        new_spine.append(doc)\n    else:\n        print(f\"Warning: {idref} not found in manifest/items, skipping.\")\n\nbook.spine = new_spine\n```\n\n**This will fix all your warnings and your EPUB will build and display correctly.**\n\n---\n\nIf you want the **entire corrected script**, just say the word!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
