ser)\n                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/todd/linux/src/hubEnv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/lxml/html/__init__.py\", line 738, in document_fromstring\n    raise etree.ParserError(\nlxml.etree.ParserError: Document is empty"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "You are still hitting the **\"Document is empty\"** error, and it's still pointing at `ebooklib.ITEM_DOCUMENT`, which is a red flag—**that code is calling a symbol that does not exist in recent EbookLib versions.**\n\n---\n\n## **Why is this still happening?**\n\nBecause somewhere in your **EbookLib installation or script**, there’s still a line like:\n```python\nbook.get_items_of_type(ebooklib.ITEM_DOCUMENT)\n```\n**This will always fail** on EbookLib ≥0.18 (or most recent pypi releases).  \nAlso, your own script is probably not the source—**the problem is in EbookLib itself** or a plugin/script using that symbol.\n\n---\n\n## **What's really causing your error?**\n\n### 1. **At least one XHTML file in your EPUB is empty (or contains no `<body>`).**\n   - This makes `lxml` (used by EbookLib) choke with `ParserError: Document is empty`.\n\n### 2. **EbookLib (or your code) is referencing `ebooklib.ITEM_DOCUMENT`**, which does not exist.\n\n---\n\n## **How do you fix this?**\n\n### **Step 1: Patch your EPUB so no XHTML is empty.**\n\n**Quick and dirty:**\n```python\nfor item in book.get_items_of_type('application/xhtml+xml'):\n    content = item.get_body_content()\n    if not content or content.strip() == b'' or content.strip() == '':\n        print(f\"⚠️ Document {item.get_id()} ({item.file_name}) is empty! Patching...\")\n        item.set_content(b\"\"\"<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><title>Blank</title></head><body>&#160;</body></html>\"\"\")\n```\n**This ensures all your XHTML files have _something_ in the body.**\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Make sure your script NEVER references `ebooklib.ITEM_DOCUMENT`.**\n\n**Update all such calls to:**\n```python\nbook.get_items_of_type('application/xhtml+xml')\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: If you're not calling `ebooklib.ITEM_DOCUMENT` but still get the error, your EbookLib version is old or your code is importing it somewhere.**\n- Try updating EbookLib with `pip install --upgrade EbookLib`\n- Double-check your imports and the actual file being run (sometimes people have a local `ebooklib.py`!).\n\n---\n\n## **Summary Table**\n\n| Problem                                 | Solution                              |\n|------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|\n| Some XHTML files are empty               | Patch with minimal valid content      |\n| Script calls `ebooklib.ITEM_DOCUMENT`    | Use `'application/xhtml+xml'` instead |\n| Still failing?                          | Upgrade EbookLib, check code imports  |\n\n---\n\n## **Want a full working script that:**\n- **Scans for empty XHTML files and patches them**\n- **Never uses `ebooklib.ITEM_DOCUMENT`**\n- **Works with modern EbookLib**\n?\n**Say the word and I’ll write it, ready-to-paste.**\n\n---\n\n### **But for now:**\nPatch the empty docs and eliminate any use of `ebooklib.ITEM_DOCUMENT`.  \nThat will 100% solve your current error."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
