own, or you get “missing image” icons.\n\n---\n\n## **How To Fix**\n\n### **1. Always Replace the Image at the Correct Path**\n- **Make sure** your script finds the image by **manifest path** and replaces `OEBPS/image/signature.png`, not `EPUB/image/signature.png`.\n\n### **2. Match the Image Dimensions and Transparency**\n- Try to **resize** your new signature image to 500 × 500 px and **save as 32bpp PNG** (with alpha channel—even if you don’t use transparency, just to match).\n\n### **3. Double-check the Manifest and References**\n- Your XHTML and manifest must point to the new image path and filename exactly.\n\n---\n\n## **Summary Table**\n\n| File                | Path                   | Size        | Color  | Transparency |  \n|---------------------|------------------------|-------------|--------|--------------|  \n| **Original**        | OEBPS/image/signature.png | 500x500 px  | 32bpp | Yes          |  \n| **Replacement**     | EPUB/image/signature.png | 1000x1000 px| 24bpp | No           |  \n\n---\n\n## **Action Steps**\n\n1. **Regenerate** your replacement signature.png as 500×500 px, 32bpp PNG (can use GIMP, Photoshop, or Pillow).\n2. **Make sure** the script replaces the image in the exact folder (`OEBPS/image/signature.png`).\n3. **Verify** the manifest and XHTML references the correct image path.\n\n---\n\nIf you want a script to automatically check the EPUB structure, or want help automating the resize/convert, let me know!  \nWant a sample script for resizing and saving as 32bpp PNG?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "yeah, it's using EPUB instead of OEBPS for everything, why is that?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great observation!  \n**Why is your replacement image (and possibly other content) in `EPUB/` instead of `OEBPS/`?**\n\n### **What’s Happening?**\n\n- **EPUBs are ZIP files** with a set folder structure.  \n  - Standard convention (especially with InDesign and many editors) is to use `OEBPS/` as the root for all book content, images, and XHTML.\n  - Some tools (including **ebooklib**, if you don’t tell it otherwise) will use `EPUB/` or even put files at the ZIP root.\n\n**When you use `ebooklib.epub` to modify or create an EPUB, by default:**\n- It uses the folder `EPUB/` internally for its content unless you explicitly set `book.FOLDER_NAME = \"OEBPS\"` or otherwise configure it.\n\n### **What’s the Consequence?**\n\n- **If your original EPUB uses `OEBPS/` for images and XHTML,**  \n  but `ebooklib` saves or replaces content in `EPUB/`,  \n  **the book now has two parallel folder structures.**\n- Your XHTML still references `OEBPS/image/signature.png`, but your script replaces/creates `EPUB/image/signature.png`.  \n  **Result:** You don’t see your new image. In the worst case, the book has doubled assets, broken links, or layout weirdness.\n\n---\n\n## **How to Fix This**\n\n**You want to use the same folder name as your original EPUB (`OEBPS`) when writing the book.**\n\n**Just add this line after loading your book:**\n\n```python\nbook.FOLDER_NAME = 'OEBPS'\n```\n\n### **Example Fix in Your Script:**\n\n```python\nbook = epub.read_epub(epub_path)\nbook.FOLDER_NAME = 'OEBPS'  # Force ebooklib to write to OEBPS, not EPUB\n```\n\nNow, when you use `epub.write_epub`, it’ll replace and write everything in `OEBPS/` instead of `EPUB/`.\n\n---\n\n## **Summary Table**\n\n| Situation      | Folder Used   | Fix Needed?           |\n|----------------|--------------|-----------------------|\n| Original EPUB  | OEBPS/       | Set `book.FOLDER_NAME = 'OEBPS'` |\n| ebooklib default| EPUB/        | Set `book.FOLDER_NAME = 'OEBPS'` |\n\n---\n\n## **Next Steps**\n\n1. **Update your script:** Add `book.FOLDER_NAME = 'OEBPS'` after loading the EPUB.\n2. **Replace the image again.**\n3. **Open the EPUB and verify**: All references and images are in `OEBPS/`, and the signature appears as expected.\n\n---\n\n**Let me know if you want the full updated script or a quick step-by-step!**"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "please, let's get a fully updated script, call it swapper.py"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Absolutely! Here’s a clean, direct script called `swapper.py` that will:\n\n- Open your EPUB.\n- Find the first occurrence of `signature.png` in the `OEBPS/image/` folder.\n- Replace it with your new `signature.png`.\n- Save the EPUB, preserving the original folder structure.\n\n---\n\n## `swapper.py`\n\n```python\nimport sys\nimport os\nfrom ebooklib import epub\n\ndef replace_signature_image(epub_path, new_signature_path):\n    # Read EPUB\n    book = epub.read_epub(epub_path)\n    # Set the folder name to OEBPS to match original EPUB structure\n    book.FOLDER_NAME = 'OEBPS'\n    \n    # Find all images in OEBPS/image/\n    found = False\n    for item in book.get_items():\n        if item.get_type() == epub.ITEM_IMAGE and item.file_name.lower().endswith('signature.png'):\n            print(f\"Replacing image at: {item.file_name}\")\n            # Read new image data\n            with open(new_signature_path, 'rb') as imgf:\n                new_img = imgf.read()\n            item.content = new_img\n            found = True\n            break\n\n    if not found:\n        print(\"❌ Could not find signature.png in EPUB to replace.\")\n        return\n\n    # Write out new epub\n    out_path = os.path.splitext(epub_path)[0] + \"_swapped.epub\"\n    epub.write_epub(out_path, book)\n    print(f\"✅ Saved new EPUB as {out_path}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    if len(sys.argv) != 3:\n        print(\"Usage: python swapper.py book.epub new_signature.png\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n    epub_path = sys.argv[1]\n    signature_path = sys.argv[2]\n    if not os.path.isfile(epub_path):\n        print(f\"EPUB not found: {epub_path}\")\n        sys.exit(2)\n    if not os.path.isfile(signature_path):\n        print(f\"Signature image not found: {signature_path}\")\n        sys.exit(3)\n    replace_signature_image(epub_path, signature_path)\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Usage**\n\n```sh\npython swapper.py \"Cody.epub\" \"signature.png\"\n```\n\n- **Output:** `Cody_swapped.epub`\n- The script only replaces the first matching `signature.png` (in any subfolder), but you can adapt if you have multiple.\n- The folder structure is preserved as long as you set `book.FOLDER_NAME = 'OEBPS'`.\n\n---\n\n**Let me know if you want it to:**\n- Replace multiple images,\n- Take a different folder,\n- Or run extra checks (size, bit-depth, etc.)\n\nReady to go!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
