{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "2025/06/19 10:21:05 NOTICE: Make sure your Redirect URL is set to \"http://127.0.0.1:53682/\" in your custom config.\n2025/06/19 10:21:05 ERROR : Failed to open browser automatically (exec: \"xdg-open\": executable file not found in $PATH) - please go to the following link: http://127.0.0.1:53682/auth?state=8ToHJglbOlCCCObYOH7gPw\n2025/06/19 10:21:05 NOTICE: Log in and authorize rclone for access\n2025/06/19 10:21:05 NOTICE: Waiting for code..."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "✅ That’s working exactly right — this happens because you’re in **WSL**, and WSL doesn’t have a \"native browser\" — so rclone can’t auto-launch the browser.\n\nNo problem — you simply:\n\n1️⃣ Copy this link:\n\n```  \nhttp://127.0.0.1:53682/auth?state=8ToHJglbOlCCCObYOH7gPw\n```\n\n---\n\n2️⃣ Open your **Windows browser (Firefox, Chrome, Edge, etc)**  \n→ Paste the link into the browser.\n\n---\n\n3️⃣ The browser will show the Google login — **IMPORTANT: pick the correct Google account**  \n(the one where your images and main Drive are)\n\n---\n\n4️⃣ Once you \"Allow\" → rclone will automatically complete the flow and finish config.\n\n---\n\nThen:\n\n```bash\nrclone about gdrive:\n```\n\nYou should now see:\n\n```\nTotal: 15 GiB (or more)\n```\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**  \n✅ That message is normal in WSL — browser just can’t auto-launch  \n✅ You simply open the URL manually  \n✅ After login, rclone will update your gdrive remote\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to prep a full **auto-mount script** for you once this is done?  \nYou’re about 1 minute from success! 🚀"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Access blocked: bookmarks has not completed the Google verification process\ntodd427@gmail.com"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "**Bingo — now we found the root cause.**\n\nThis happens because you are using **rclone \"gdrive\" remote WITHOUT a client ID** → in this case, Google sometimes rejects the default app (\"rclone\") for \"unverified\" apps.\n\n---\n\n### Why did this just happen?\n\n→ You are using the *default rclone client ID*  \n→ Google is now much stricter — **if your account has 2FA, old Drive API tokens, or extra security, it will block that default app.**\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 How to fix:\n\n**Two options:**\n\n---\n\n**Option 1 — Easiest:**  \nUse `rclone authorize` in a separate Windows terminal (powershell) — this will bypass the WSL browser problem:\n\n```powershell\nrclone authorize \"drive\"\n```\n\n→ Will open browser  \n→ You log in with correct account  \n→ It will output a token — copy/paste it into your WSL rclone config.\n\n---\n\n**Option 2 — Better long-term:**  \nCreate your own **Google Drive API Client ID** (takes 3-5 mins):\n\n✅ No more \"Access blocked\"  \n✅ Better Drive quota  \n✅ Works with multiple machines\n\n---\n\n---\n\n**If you want, I can give you step-by-step for Option 2** — very easy, you just:\n\n1️⃣ Go to [https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials)  \n2️⃣ Create new OAuth Client ID  \n3️⃣ Paste the ID and secret into rclone config\n\n→ Done forever — no more auth problems!\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**  \nRight now you hit:\n\n```\nAccess blocked: bookmarks has not completed the Google verification process\n```\n\nBecause: using default rclone app ID → blocked.\n\n---\n\nWould you like:\n\n1️⃣ Quick-fix (Option 1)  \n2️⃣ Proper permanent fix (Option 2 — my recommendation)\n\nJust tell me — I can paste the exact steps 🚀.  \n(You’re 1-2 mins from fully working system now!) 🚀🚀🚀"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "API key\n.\nIdentifies your project using a simple API key to check quota and access\nOAuth client ID\n.\nRequests user consent so your app can access the user's data\nService account\n.\nEnables server-to-server, app-level authentication using robot accounts\nHelp me choose\n.\nAsks a few questions to help you decide which type of credential to use"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "✅ Good — that’s exactly the right screen!\n\nYou want to select:\n\n👉 **OAuth client ID**  \n*(“Requests user consent so your app can access the user’s data”)*\n\n---\n\nThat is the correct choice for rclone → because **you will log in as yourself** and give rclone permission to access *your Google Drive*.\n\n---\n\nAfter that, if it asks:\n\n**Configure consent screen**\n\n→ Choose **External** → Save → just fill required fields:  \n- App name (can be \"rclone\")  \n- Email (your own)\n\n---\n\nThen back to:  \n**Create OAuth Client ID**  \n→ Choose **Desktop app**  \n→ Name: \"rclone\"\n\n---\n\nThen you will get:\n\n```\nClient ID: xxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com  \nClient Secret: xxxxx\n```\n\n→ Copy these into `rclone config`\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to stay here with you and guide you through?  \nWe are right at the final step 🚀 — just say **Go!** 🚀."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
