{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Access blocked: rcloneMona has not completed the Google verification process\ntodd427@gmail.com"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Excellent — now I see exactly what’s happening. Let me explain:\n\nYou created your **own OAuth client (perfect)**, but:\n\n👉 Google requires that for *new* OAuth clients → you must go through **Google Verification** (aka OAuth App Verification)  \n👉 Until you do this, *only “test users” you add can use it*, otherwise you'll get:\n\n```\nAccess blocked: rcloneMona has not completed the Google verification process\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 The simple fix:\n\n✅ Go back to:  \n👉 [Google Cloud Console — OAuth Consent Screen](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials/consent)\n\n---\n\n✅ In that screen:\n\n1️⃣ Set Publishing Status = \"Testing\"  \n2️⃣ Add your email (`todd427@gmail.com`) to **Test Users**  \n3️⃣ Save\n\n---\n\nNow when you run rclone config again → **Google will allow the auth for test users**.  \n\n---\n\n### Why this happens:\n\nGoogle started requiring **verification for new OAuth apps** after 2022 → it’s very normal — no problem — we just mark the app as \"Testing\" and add yourself as a test user → done.\n\n---\n\n### Summary:\n\n✅ You already created the OAuth client — perfect  \n✅ Now go to \"OAuth Consent Screen\", set to Testing, add yourself as Test User  \n✅ Then rclone config → will work\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to paste exact step-by-step?  \nYou are literally 1 min from DONE 🚀 — this is the final block.  \nShall I write it out for you? Just say **Go!** 🚀."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
