{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "just tell me the mount command"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here’s the correct **mount command** for you now:\n\n```bash\nrclone mount gdrive: ~/google --vfs-cache-mode writes --daemon\n```\n\n---\n\n**Breakdown:**\n\n✅ `gdrive:` → your working remote name  \n✅ `~/google` → mount point (directory to view your Drive)  \n✅ `--vfs-cache-mode writes` → required so you can write files  \n✅ `--daemon` → runs in background\n\n---\n\nIf you ever need to **unmount**:\n\n```bash\nfusermount3 -u ~/google\n```\n\n(or)\n\n```bash\numount ~/google\n```\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can also give you a small script like:\n\n```bash\nmount_gdrive.sh\nunmount_gdrive.sh\n```\n\nJust say **Go** — but you are ready now 🚀."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "wrong. got the old mount."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Ah — excellent catch — you are right — **your new gdrive remote now uses your own Client ID + correct Drive (2 TB)** → but the *old mount might still be running* in background.\n\nLet’s clean and remount — very easy:\n\n---\n\n### 1️⃣ First — unmount (to clear old mount):\n\n```bash\nfusermount3 -u ~/google\n```\n\nor if that fails:\n\n```bash\numount ~/google\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2️⃣ Then — fresh mount with your new, good gdrive:\n\n```bash\nrclone mount gdrive: ~/google --vfs-cache-mode full --dir-cache-time 12h --poll-interval 1m --buffer-size 512M --daemon\n```\n\n---\n\n### Why this version:\n\n✅ `--vfs-cache-mode full` → much better for large files / images  \n✅ `--dir-cache-time 12h` → keep directory listing cached for 12h (much faster)  \n✅ `--poll-interval 1m` → auto-refresh every 1 min  \n✅ `--buffer-size 512M` → better streaming performance  \n✅ `--daemon` → background the mount\n\n---\n\n**Now when you run:**\n\n```bash\nls ~/google\n```\n\n→ You should see all your Drive folders (2 TB).\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**\n\n👉 The old mount was pointing to the “wrong” account — that’s why you still saw the old folders.  \n👉 After unmount + clean mount — you will see the correct Drive.\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to give you a ready-to-use:\n\n✅ `mount_gdrive.sh`  \n✅ `unmount_gdrive.sh`\n\n?  \nJust say **Go!** 🚀 — very handy."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
