{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "how can we use smtp2go"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great choice! **SMTP2GO** is a reliable transactional email service with a generous free tier, and it integrates easily into Django via SMTP.\n\n---\n\n## 📬 How to Use **SMTP2GO** with Django\n\n### ✅ Step 1: Create an SMTP2GO Account\n- Go to [smtp2go.com](https://www.smtp2go.com/)\n- Create a free account\n- Under **Settings → Users & API Keys**, create a new SMTP username/password\n- Note the SMTP server (e.g., `mail.smtp2go.com`)\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Step 2: Update `settings.py` in Django\n```python\n# settings.py\n\nEMAIL_BACKEND = 'django.core.mail.backends.smtp.EmailBackend'\nEMAIL_HOST = 'mail.smtp2go.com'  # or mail.smtp2go.eu (check your region)\nEMAIL_PORT = 587\nEMAIL_USE_TLS = True\nEMAIL_HOST_USER = 'your_smtp2go_username'\nEMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD = 'your_smtp2go_password'\nDEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL = 'Your Name <you@yourdomain.com>'\n```\n\nOptional (for staging/dev):\n```python\n# Development email backend (prints to console instead)\n# EMAIL_BACKEND = 'django.core.mail.backends.console.EmailBackend'\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Step 3: Send a Test Email\n```python\nfrom django.core.mail import send_mail\n\nsend_mail(\n    subject='SMTP2GO Test',\n    message='It works!',\n    from_email='you@yourdomain.com',\n    recipient_list=['someone@example.com']\n)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔐 Tips for Production Use\n\n| Action | Why |\n|--------|-----|\n| ✅ Add SPF/DKIM records to your DNS | Improves deliverability |\n| 🔐 Use environment variables for SMTP creds | Avoid secrets in code |\n| 📈 Monitor delivery logs on SMTP2GO dashboard | Track issues and success |\n| 🧪 Use a console backend for local/dev | Avoid accidental spam |\n\n---\n\n### Want to use it with `django-allauth` or your contact forms?\n\nIt’s the **same as with SendGrid via SMTP** — no changes to AllAuth required. All email that Django sends (signup confirmations, resets, etc.) will go through SMTP2GO as long as your `EMAIL_*` settings are configured correctly.\n\n---\n\nWould you like:\n- A zip with `smtp2go_email_utils.py` for structured sending?\n- A switchable config for both SendGrid and SMTP2GO?\n\nLet me know and I’ll bundle it up."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
