d@foxxelabs.com>\nTo: good@hobbits.com\nDate: Tue, 17 Jun 2025 03:50:40 -0000\nMessage-ID: <175013224035.5991.1624138517540211756@mona.>\n\nHi there,\n\nWelcome to Foxxe Labs! We’re thrilled to have you.\n\nFeel free to explore, test, and create with confidence.\n\n— The Foxxe Team\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Getting the welcome email **twice** means it was likely triggered from **two different code paths** — both calling `send_welcome_email(user)` during the same signup.\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 In Your Code\n\nYou have **two places** that call `send_welcome_email(user)`:\n\n#### In `CustomAccountAdapter`:\n```python\ndef save_user(self, request, user, form, commit=True):\n    print(\"🚀 CustomAccountAdapter: save_user triggered\")\n    user = super().save_user(request, user, form, commit)\n    self.send_welcome_email(user)  # ✅ CALLED HERE\n    return user\n```\n\n#### In `NoSignupFormAdapter` (for social logins):\n```python\ndef save_user(self, request, sociallogin, form=None):\n    print(\"🚀 NoSignupFormAdapter: save_user triggered\")\n    ...\n    self.send_welcome_email(user)  # ✅ CALLED HERE\n    return user\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Explanation\n\nIf you're signing up with a **social provider** (e.g. Google), **both** adapters can be triggered:\n- `CustomAccountAdapter.save_user()` (via the base `allauth.account`)\n- `NoSignupFormAdapter.save_user()` (via `allauth.socialaccount`)\n\nHence: **two calls = two emails.**\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ Fix Option 1: Deduplicate in `NoSignupFormAdapter`\n\nAdd a check like this:\n\n```python\ndef save_user(self, request, sociallogin, form=None):\n    print(\"🚀 NoSignupFormAdapter: save_user triggered\")\n    user = sociallogin.user\n    ...\n    if not user.pk:  # only send if user is new\n        self.send_welcome_email(user)\n    return user\n```\n\nOr set a flag:\n```python\nif not hasattr(user, \"_welcome_email_sent\"):\n    self.send_welcome_email(user)\n    user._welcome_email_sent = True\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ Fix Option 2: Centralize Email Send\n\nIf you want more control, **only send from one place** (e.g. a post-signup signal), or pass a `send_email=False` flag where needed.\n\n---\n\nWould you like help setting up a signal-based email sender instead (more DRY and reliable)?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "i got the email twice, why"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect — now you're seeing **only one welcome email per signup**, which confirms that:\n\n✅ You're using **email/password signup**,  \n✅ Only `CustomAccountAdapter.save_user()` is running,  \n✅ And the issue of duplicate emails is resolved.\n\n---\n\n### 💡 Why You Got Two Before\n\nWhen you tested earlier, you likely signed up via **social login (e.g., Google)**. That caused both of these to run:\n\n1. `NoSignupFormAdapter.save_user()` → email sent\n2. `CustomAccountAdapter.save_user()` → email sent again\n\nNow that you’re signing up **with email/password**, only `CustomAccountAdapter` is triggered — as expected.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Recommendation (for safety)\n\nIf you *do* want to support both signup flows but prevent duplicate emails, you can **add a protection flag** inside either adapter:\n\n#### Add this before calling `send_welcome_email()`:\n```python\nif not getattr(user, \"_welcome_email_sent\", False):\n    self.send_welcome_email(user)\n    user._welcome_email_sent = True\n```\n\nThat ensures no matter how many places attempt it, the user gets **only one welcome email** per session.\n\n---\n\nWould you like to add an admin toggle or setting to turn off welcome emails in staging/dev automatically?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
