\", line 21, in provider_login_url\n    provider = adapter.get_provider(request, provider)\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/todd/linux/src/sandy/lib/python3.12/site-packages/allauth/socialaccount/adapter.py\", line 213, in get_provider\n    app = self.get_app(request, provider=provider, client_id=client_id)\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/todd/linux/src/sandy/lib/python3.12/site-packages/allauth/socialaccount/adapter.py\", line 303, in get_app\n    raise SocialApp.DoesNotExist()\nallauth.socialaccount.models.SocialApp.DoesNotExist\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 13 tests in 1.592s\n\nFAILED (errors=7)\nDestroying test database for alias 'default'..."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "You're very close! The test failures are due to two main problems:\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 1. **Incorrect variable reference (`app` is undefined)**\n\nIn `test_mock_google_login_flow`, you're correctly assigning `self.google_app`, but then you later try to use `app`, which isn't defined.\n\n#### 🔧 Fix:\n\nChange this:\n```python\ntoken = SocialToken(app=app, token=\"mock-token\", account=account)\n```\n\nTo this:\n```python\ntoken = SocialToken(app=self.google_app, token=\"mock-token\", account=account)\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 2. **Missing `SocialApp` record during test rendering**\n\nSeveral of your failing tests try to render templates that include:\n\n```django\n{% provider_login_url 'google' %}\n```\n\nBut since no `SocialApp` exists in the test database for Google during most tests (outside the `GoogleSSOTests`), this raises:\n```\nallauth.socialaccount.models.SocialApp.DoesNotExist\n```\n\n#### 🔧 Fix:\n\nAdd a reusable setup mixin to inject a fake `SocialApp` for tests that render templates:\n\n```python\nfrom allauth.socialaccount.models import SocialApp\nfrom django.contrib.sites.models import Site\n\nclass GoogleSSOTestMixin:\n    def setup_google_app(self):\n        site, _ = Site.objects.get_or_create(domain=\"localhost\", name=\"localhost\")\n        app, _ = SocialApp.objects.get_or_create(\n            provider=\"google\",\n            name=\"Google\",\n            client_id=\"test-client-id\",\n            secret=\"test-secret\",\n        )\n        app.sites.add(site)\n```\n\nThen call `self.setup_google_app()` in the `setUp()` method of these classes:\n\n- `SignupTests`\n- `LoginLogoutTests`\n- `URLTests`\n\nFor example:\n\n```python\nclass SignupTests(TestCase, GoogleSSOTestMixin):\n\n    def setUp(self):\n        print(f\"\\nRunning tests in: {self.__class__.__name__}\")\n        self.setup_google_app()\n```\n\n---\n\nOnce you fix the incorrect variable reference and set up the dummy `SocialApp` for relevant tests, all the errors should be resolved.\n\nWould you like me to apply those updates and provide a fixed version of `tests.py`?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "give me a fixed version"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Your fixed version of `tests.py` is ready. It includes:\n\n- The missing `app` reference correction in `test_mock_google_login_flow`.\n- A reusable `GoogleSSOTestMixin` that sets up a `SocialApp` for Google.\n- Injection of the setup into `SignupTests`, `LoginLogoutTests`, and `URLTests`.\n\nDownload it here: [tests_fixed.py](sandbox:/mnt/data/tests_fixed.py) ✅\n\nLet me know if you'd like to auto-clean test data or isolate the SSO setup into a test fixture.\n\nThanks! Based on your traceback and the test code in `tests.py`, here’s what’s wrong and how to fix it:\n\n---\n\n### ✅ **1. Fix `test_mock_google_login_flow`**\nThe error:\n\n```\nAttributeError: 'WSGIRequest' object has no attribute 'session'\n```\n\nThis happens because you're using a `RequestFactory` request without attaching a session. Add the session middleware manually:\n\n**Replace** this part:\n```python\nrequest = self.factory.get(\"/accounts/google/login/callback/\")\nrequest.user = AnonymousUser()\n```\n\n**With this**:\n```python\nfrom django.contrib.sessions.middleware import SessionMiddleware\n\nrequest = self.factory.get(\"/accounts/google/login/callback/\")\nrequest.user = AnonymousUser()\n\n# Attach a session manually\nmiddleware = SessionMiddleware(get_response=lambda r: None)\nmiddleware.process_request(request)\nrequest.session.save()\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ **2. Fix login-related test errors due to missing SocialApp**\n\nThe error:\n\n```\nallauth.socialaccount.models.SocialApp.DoesNotExist\n```\n\nMeans your tests try to load social login templates (`{% provider_login_url 'google' %}`) but there’s no `SocialApp` object present.\n\nYou already have `setup_google_app()` and `create_test_google_social_app()` — but they don’t always run early enough or aren’t injected in some test classes.\n\n🔧 **Fix**:\nMake sure each test class that touches any `account_login` or `account_signup` URL or template includes:\n\n```python\ndef setUp(self):\n    self.setup_google_app()\n```\n\nThat’s already in your `SignupTests`, `LoginLogoutTests`, and `URLTests`, so we’re good there.\n\n⚠️ However, you **must also commit the test DB** after `setup_google_app()` to avoid issues where the object isn’t available at render time. So **modify `setup_google_app`** to add this:\n\n```python\ndef setup_google_app(self):\n    site, _ = Site.objects.get_or_create(domain=\"localhost\", name=\"localhost\")\n    app, _ = SocialApp.objects.get_or_create(\n        provider=\"google\",\n        name=\"Google\",\n        client_id=\"test-client-id\",\n        secret=\"test-secret\",\n    )\n    app.sites.add(site)\n    app.save()  # Make sure it's saved and committed\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ **3. Final checklist**\n\n- [x] All classes calling social login views must call `setup_google_app()`\n- [x] All sessions must be attached to mock `RequestFactory` requests\n- [x] Make sure you're using `AnonymousUser()` if the user isn't logged in\n- [x] Ensure test Google account and token values match in mocks\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to generate a fully updated `tests.py` file with all these fixes applied?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
