ded to show which app the template is from!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "there was a python command to list all templates, using get_template(), what is it"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "That message — `\"base.html (remove before production)\"` — is coming from a **hardcoded line in your base template file**, likely something like:\n\n```html\n<p>base.html (remove before production)</p>\n```\n\nIt appears just before or inside your `<body>` block.\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Where to find it\n\nRun this in your project root:\n\n```bash\ngrep -rn 'remove before production' templates/\n```\n\nOr if you're not sure where templates are stored:\n\n```bash\ngrep -rn 'remove before production' .\n```\n\nThis will show you the exact file and line number.\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 How to fix\n\nOpen the file it finds (probably `templates/base.html`) and remove or comment out the line:\n\n```html\n<!-- <p>base.html (remove before production)</p> -->\n```\n\n---\n\nThe rest of your message:\n> `Survey ... Age Group* ... I carefully curate the photos...`\n\nis likely rendered inside a child template that **extends `base.html`**, and you're seeing the full HTML output combined from the base and the specific survey template (e.g. `questionnaire_form.html`, `persquiz.html`, etc.).\n\nLet me know if you'd like help finding which template renders that survey form."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
