{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "how do i get to the results"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great choice — adding a **\"View Results\"** link in the Django admin list view for `Questionnaire` is very handy.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Step 1: Customize the Admin\n\nIn your `surveys/admin.py`, customize the `QuestionnaireAdmin`:\n\n```python\nfrom django.contrib import admin\nfrom django.utils.html import format_html\nfrom django.urls import reverse\n\nfrom .models import Questionnaire, Question, Response\n\nclass QuestionnaireAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):\n    list_display = ('title', 'code', 'view_results_link')\n\n    def view_results_link(self, obj):\n        url = reverse('results_dashboard', args=[obj.code])\n        return format_html('<a href=\"{}\" target=\"_blank\">View Results</a>', url)\n    view_results_link.short_description = \"Results\"\n\nadmin.site.register(Questionnaire, QuestionnaireAdmin)\nadmin.site.register(Question)\nadmin.site.register(Response)\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Step 2: Confirm URL Name\n\nMake sure your `results_dashboard_view` URL pattern has the name `'results_dashboard'`, like:\n\n```python\n# in surveys/urls.py\npath('<str:code>/results/', views.results_dashboard_view, name='results_dashboard'),\n```\n\nAnd your project `urls.py` should include this app:\n\n```python\n# in shore/urls.py or similar\npath('surveys/', include('surveys.urls')),\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Step 3: Restart Server & Visit Admin\n\nNow:\n- Go to `http://localhost:8000/admin/surveys/questionnaire/`\n- You’ll see a **“View Results”** column with links to each dashboard\n\nWant to do the same for export links?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "let's add a link to the admin list view"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Good question — the correct function name depends on how your view is defined.\n\nHere’s how to determine the correct reference:\n\n---\n\n### ✅ If your view is defined like this:\n\n```python\n# surveys/views.py\ndef results_dashboard_view(request, code):\n    ...\n```\n\nThen your `urls.py` should **use the actual function name**:\n\n```python\n# surveys/urls.py\nfrom . import views\n\nurlpatterns = [\n    path('<str:code>/results/', views.results_dashboard_view, name='results_dashboard'),\n]\n```\n\nSo `views.results_dashboard_view` is correct.\n\n---\n\n### ❌ **Not this** (which would be incorrect unless you've renamed it):\n\n```python\npath(..., views.results_dashboard, ...)  # ❌ only correct if your function is actually named `results_dashboard`\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ TL;DR\n\n✔️ Use `views.results_dashboard_view` **if the function is named `results_dashboard_view`** in `views.py`.\n\nIf you want to clean it up, you *can* rename your function to `results_dashboard`, but then you’ll need to update both the function and URL references.\n\n---\n\nWant me to also add an **“Export CSV”** link to the admin view next to the results link?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
