{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Is this going to work:from . import views\n\nurlpatterns = [\n    path('<str:code>/results/', views.results_dashboard_view, name='results_dashboard'),\n]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The error:\n\n```\nReverse for 'results_dashboard' with arguments '('',)' not found.\n```\n\nmeans that Django is trying to render a **\"View Results\"** link for a `Questionnaire` that has a **blank or null `code` field**.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Fix: Guard Against Missing `code` in the Admin\n\nUpdate your `view_results_link` method in `QuestionnaireAdmin` like this:\n\n```python\nfrom django.utils.html import format_html\nfrom django.urls import reverse, NoReverseMatch\n\nclass QuestionnaireAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):\n    list_display = ('title', 'code', 'view_results_link')\n\n    def view_results_link(self, obj):\n        if not obj.code:\n            return \"—\"\n        try:\n            url = reverse('results_dashboard', args=[obj.code])\n            return format_html('<a href=\"{}\" target=\"_blank\">View Results</a>', url)\n        except NoReverseMatch:\n            return \"Invalid code\"\n    view_results_link.short_description = \"Results\"\n```\n\nThis does three things:\n1. Returns an em-dash if `code` is blank.\n2. Tries the `reverse()` call only if `code` is present.\n3. Catches `NoReverseMatch` if something else goes wrong.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Optional: Ensure `code` Is Required\n\nIn your `Questionnaire` model, make sure the `code` field is:\n```python\ncode = models.SlugField(unique=True, blank=False, null=False)\n```\n\nAnd if needed, backfill codes for any existing records via the admin or a quick data migration.\n\n---\n\nAfter making this change, restart your dev server and revisit:\n\n```\nhttp://localhost:8000/admin/surveys/questionnaire/\n```\n\nLet me know if you’d like to also add “Export CSV” as a column."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
