{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "okay, starting with this, can you build me a new survey in my surveys app"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Excellent — let’s fully integrate the **Programmer Experience Questionnaire** into your `surveys` app.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ 1. Python Script to Add the Survey + Questions\n\nWe'll create a management command:  \n`python manage.py load_progexp_questions`\n\n### 🗂 `surveys/management/commands/load_progexp_questions.py`\n\nCreate the directories if needed, then add:\n\n```python\nfrom django.core.management.base import BaseCommand\nfrom surveys.models import Questionnaire, Question\n\nclass Command(BaseCommand):\n    help = 'Load Programmer Experience Questionnaire and its questions'\n\n    def handle(self, *args, **options):\n        qnr, created = Questionnaire.objects.get_or_create(\n            code='progexp',\n            defaults={'title': 'Programmer Experience Questionnaire'}\n        )\n\n        if not created:\n            self.stdout.write(self.style.WARNING(\"Questionnaire already exists. Skipping creation.\"))\n        else:\n            self.stdout.write(self.style.SUCCESS(f\"Created questionnaire: {qnr.title}\"))\n\n        questions = [\n            # Section 1: General Background\n            (\"General Background\", \"First Name:\", \"short_text\"),\n            (\"General Background\", \"Last Name:\", \"short_text\"),\n            (\"General Background\", \"Age:\", \"number\"),\n            (\"General Background\", \"Years of experience:\", \"select\"),\n            (\"General Background\", \"Primary language:\", \"short_text\"),\n            (\"General Background\", \"Other languages (check all that apply):\", \"checkbox_multiple\"),\n\n            # Section 2: Problem-Solving & Algorithms\n            (\"Problem-Solving & Algorithms\", \"Can you implement basic algorithms?\", \"select\"),\n            (\"Problem-Solving & Algorithms\", \"Used complex data structures?\", \"select\"),\n            (\"Problem-Solving & Algorithms\", \"Do you solve coding challenges?\", \"select\"),\n\n            # Section 3: Software Development Practices\n            (\"Software Development Practices\", \"Familiarity with Git:\", \"select\"),\n            (\"Software Development Practices\", \"Worked with CI/CD pipelines?\", \"select\"),\n            (\"Software Development Practices\", \"How do you test code?\", \"select\"),\n\n            # Section 4: Project & Collaboration Experience\n            (\"Project & Collaboration Experience\", \"Open-source contributions?\", \"select\"),\n            (\"Project & Collaboration Experience\", \"Largest project you've worked on:\", \"long_text\"),\n            (\"Project & Collaboration Experience\", \"Experience with Agile/Scrum?\", \"select\"),\n\n            # Section 5: System Design & Deployment\n            (\"System Design & Deployment\", \"Designed a system architecture?\", \"select\"),\n            (\"System Design & Deployment\", \"Familiarity with concepts:\", \"select\"),\n            (\"System Design & Deployment\", \"Deployment experience?\", \"select\"),\n            (\"System Design & Deployment\", \"Platforms/tools used:\", \"checkbox_multiple\"),\n\n            # Section 6: Learning & Interests\n            (\"Learning & Interests\", \"Favorite development areas:\", \"checkbox_multiple\"),\n            (\"Learning & Interests\", \"How often do you learn new tech?\", \"select\"),\n        ]\n\n        for section, text, qtype in questions:\n            Question.objects.get_or_create(\n                questionnaire=qnr,\n                text=text.strip(),\n                section=section.strip(),\n                defaults={'type': qtype}\n            )\n\n        self.stdout.write(self.style.SUCCESS(\"All questions loaded.\"))\n```\n\n> Customize `type` field values as needed to match your model (e.g. `\"select\"`, `\"short_text\"`, `\"checkbox_multiple\"`).\n\n---\n\n## ✅ 2. URL Entry\n\nIn `surveys/urls.py`:\n\n```python\npath('progexp/', views.questionnaire_view, {'code': 'progexp'}, name='programmer_experience'),\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ 3. Template\n\nCreate: `templates/surveys/questionnaire_progexp.html`\n\nYou can copy your base `questionnaire.html` and customize:\n\n```django\n{% extends \"_base.html\" %}\n{% block content %}\n<h1>{{ questionnaire.title }}</h1>\n<form method=\"post\">\n  {% csrf_token %}\n  {{ form.as_p }}\n  <button type=\"submit\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Submit</button>\n</form>\n{% endblock %}\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ 4. Tests\n\nIn `surveys/tests.py`:\n\n```python\ndef test_progexp_questionnaire_view_renders(self):\n    response = self.client.get('/surveys/progexp/')\n    self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n    self.assertContains(response, \"Programmer Experience Questionnaire\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ 5. Run It!\n\n```bash\npython manage.py makemigrations\npython manage.py migrate\npython manage.py load_progexp_questions\n```\n\nThen visit:\n\n```\nhttp://localhost:8000/surveys/progexp/\n```\n\n---\n\nWant me to:\n- Extend the form logic to support checkbox inputs?\n- Handle conditional fields (e.g., “Other: ___”)?\n- Export this as a zip for import into your project?\n\nLet me know!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "yes to all the above"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "That traceback confirms the issue: your `Question` model **doesn’t have a field named `type`**, but the script tries to use one.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Fix: Use the Correct Field\n\nDjango is telling us:\n```\nFieldError: Invalid field name(s) for model Question: 'type'\n```\n\nWe need to:\n1. **Find out what your model actually calls this field** — maybe it’s `question_type`, `input_type`, `format`, or it’s entirely missing and needs to be added.\n2. If it’s missing, we can add it via a migration.\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Step 1: Check the `Question` model\n\nPlease confirm what your current `Question` model looks like. If you're not sure, here’s a safe guess based on your earlier app structure:\n\n```python\nclass Question(models.Model):\n    questionnaire = models.ForeignKey(Questionnaire, on_delete=models.CASCADE)\n    text = models.TextField()\n    section = models.CharField(max_length=200)\n    # Is there a field for type/input? If not, we'll add:\n    # input_type = models.CharField(max_length=30, choices=..., default='text')\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🛠 Step 2: Add `input_type` Field (if missing)\n\nIf the `type` field doesn’t exist and you need to store the input type, add this:\n\n```python\nclass Question(models.Model):\n    ...\n    input_type = models.CharField(\n        max_length=30,\n        choices=[\n            ('short_text', 'Short Text'),\n            ('long_text', 'Long Text'),\n            ('select', 'Select'),\n            ('checkbox_multiple', 'Checkboxes'),\n            ('number', 'Number'),\n        ],\n        default='short_text'\n    )\n```\n\nThen run:\n\n```bash\npython manage.py makemigrations\npython manage.py migrate\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔁 Step 3: Update the Script\n\nChange this line in your command:\n\n```python\ndefaults={'type': qtype}\n```\n\nto:\n\n```python\ndefaults={'input_type': qtype}\n```\n\n(assuming you renamed the model field to `