{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "woohoo! Marvelous!"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great question! Here's how to make the questionnaire accessible through a URL:\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Step-by-Step: Setting Up the URL to Take the Test\n\nAssuming you're using a Django app named `surveys`, and your `Questionnaire` model is set up as shown, follow these steps:\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 1. **Create a View to Serve the Questionnaire**\n\nIn `surveys/views.py`:\n\n```python\nfrom django.shortcuts import render, get_object_or_404\nfrom .models import Questionnaire, Question, AGE_CHOICES\n\ndef take_questionnaire(request, code):\n    questionnaire = get_object_or_404(Questionnaire, code=code)\n    questions = Question.objects.filter(questionnaire=questionnaire)\n    return render(request, 'surveys/take_questionnaire.html', {\n        'questionnaire': questionnaire,\n        'questions': questions,\n        'age_choices': AGE_CHOICES,\n    })\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 2. **Add the URL Route**\n\nIn `surveys/urls.py` (create if it doesn't exist):\n\n```python\nfrom django.urls import path\nfrom . import views\n\nurlpatterns = [\n    path('<slug:code>/', views.take_questionnaire, name='take_questionnaire'),\n]\n```\n\nThen **include this in your project’s `urls.py`:**\n\n```python\nfrom django.urls import path, include\n\nurlpatterns = [\n    path('surveys/', include('surveys.urls')),\n    path('admin/', admin.site.urls),\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 3. **Create the Template**\n\nIn `surveys/templates/surveys/take_questionnaire.html`, you can start with something simple (or use your `index.html` logic):\n\n```html\n<h1>{{ questionnaire.title }}</h1>\n<p>{{ questionnaire.description }}</p>\n\n<form method=\"post\">\n  {% csrf_token %}\n  <label for=\"age\">Select your age group:</label>\n  <select name=\"age\" required>\n    <option value=\"\">-- Select --</option>\n    {% for value, label in age_choices %}\n      <option value=\"{{ value }}\">{{ label }}</option>\n    {% endfor %}\n  </select>\n\n  <h2>Questions</h2>\n  {% for q in questions %}\n    <p>{{ forloop.counter }}. {{ q.text }}</p>\n    <select name=\"q{{ forloop.counter }}\" required>\n      <option value=\"\">--</option>\n      {% for i in \"12345\" %}\n        <option value=\"{{ i }}\">{{ i }}</option>\n      {% endfor %}\n    </select>\n  {% endfor %}\n\n  <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n</form>\n```\n\n(For now this just renders — we can wire up saving responses next.)\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 4. **Visit the URL**\n\nRun your server:\n\n```bash\npython manage.py runserver\n```\n\nThen open:\n\n```\nhttp://localhost:8000/surveys/feyman/\n```\n\n(Replace `feyman` with your `questionnaire.code` value if different.)\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to wire in the **response submission and result display** next?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
