{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "we have questionnaire not take_questionnaire"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "To view results in your Django project, here are **three options**, depending on how you'd like to access the data:\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Option 1: Use the Django Admin (recommended for quick checks)\n\n### 1. Make sure `Response` is registered in `admin.py`\n\nIn `surveys/admin.py`, add:\n\n```python\nfrom django.contrib import admin\nfrom .models import Questionnaire, Question, Response\n\nadmin.site.register(Questionnaire)\nadmin.site.register(Question)\nadmin.site.register(Response)\n```\n\n### 2. Create a superuser (if you haven't already)\n\n```bash\npython manage.py createsuperuser\n```\n\nFollow prompts for username, email, and password.\n\n### 3. Run your server and visit:\n\n```\nhttp://localhost:8000/admin/\n```\n\nLog in with your superuser credentials.  \nClick **Responses** to view submitted results — you’ll see:\n\n- UUID (with `-1`, `-2`, etc. if duplicates)\n- Age group\n- Total score\n- JSON of section scores\n- Timestamp\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Option 2: Add a simple results page (for dev or public stats)\n\nCreate a new view in `surveys/views.py`:\n\n```python\nfrom django.contrib.admin.views.decorators import staff_member_required\nfrom django.http import JsonResponse\nfrom .models import Response\n\n@staff_member_required\ndef response_list(request):\n    responses = Response.objects.all().order_by('-submitted_at')\n    data = [\n        {\n            \"uuid\": r.uuid,\n            \"age\": r.age,\n            \"score\": r.total_score,\n            \"sections\": r.scores,\n            \"time\": r.submitted_at.isoformat()\n        }\n        for r in responses\n    ]\n    return JsonResponse(data, safe=False)\n```\n\nThen add to `surveys/urls.py`:\n\n```python\npath('results/', views.response_list, name='response_list'),\n```\n\nVisit:\n\n```\nhttp://localhost:8000/surveys/results/\n```\n\nIt’ll show a JSON dump of results (requires login as staff).\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Option 3: Query results via Django shell\n\n```bash\npython manage.py shell\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```python\nfrom surveys.models import Response\nfor r in Response.objects.all():\n    print(r.uuid, r.age, r.total_score, r.scores)\n```\n\n---\n\nLet me know if you'd like:\n- A paginated web dashboard for responses\n- CSV export\n- Graphs (bar charts, averages, etc.) per section or age group\n\nWe can add any of those in minutes."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
