{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "python manage.py findtemplates\nUnknown command: 'findtemplates'. Did you mean findstatic?\nType 'manage.py help' for usage."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Thanks for sharing your `settings.py`. The issue is clear now:\n\n---\n\n### 🔴 Problem:\n\nYour `TEMPLATES` config has:\n\n```python\n'DIRS': [],\n```\n\nThis means Django is **not looking in your project-level `templates/` directory** — only in app-level directories like:\n\n```\naccounts/templates/registration/login.html\n```\n\nSo if your `login.html` is NOT at that exact location, Django won’t find it.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Fix 1 (Project-level templates)\n\nIf you have `templates/registration/login.html` at the top level of your project, do this:\n\n**Update `settings.py`**:\n\n```python\n'DIRS': [BASE_DIR / 'templates'],\n```\n\nSo this section becomes:\n\n```python\nTEMPLATES = [\n    {\n        'BACKEND': 'django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates',\n        'DIRS': [BASE_DIR / 'templates'],\n        'APP_DIRS': True,\n        'OPTIONS': {\n            'context_processors': [\n                'django.template.context_processors.debug',\n                'django.template.context_processors.request',\n                'django.contrib.auth.context_processors.auth',\n                'django.contrib.messages.context_processors.messages',\n            ],\n        },\n    },\n]\n```\n\nThen create this file if it doesn't exist:\n\n```\nshore/templates/registration/login.html\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Fix 2 (App-level templates)\n\nIf you want to keep things inside the `accounts` app, make sure your file is here:\n\n```\naccounts/templates/registration/login.html\n```\n\nAnd ensure the `accounts` app is correctly structured like:\n\n```\naccounts/\n├── templates/\n│   └── registration/\n│       └── login.html\n├── apps.py\n├── models.py\n...\n```\n\n---\n\nOnce either fix is done, restart the dev server:\n\n```bash\npython manage.py runserver\n```\n\nAnd visit:\n\n```\nhttp://localhost:8000/accounts/login/\n```\n\nLet me know which structure you prefer or if you want me to generate a login template for you."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
