ields = [..., 'contents', 'modules']\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ How to Fix It\n\nSince you're actually nesting **modules (with their contents)**, you should rename the field like this:\n\n```python\nclass CourseWithContentsSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):\n    modules = ModuleWithContentsSerializer(many=True)  # ✅ correct field name\n    class Meta:\n        model = Course\n        fields = ['id', 'subject', 'title', 'slug', 'overview', 'created', 'owner', 'modules']\n```\n\nThen remove any mention of `'contents'` from `fields`.\n\n---\n\n### 🔁 Update Summary\n\nUpdate your `CourseWithContentsSerializer` to this:\n\n```python\nclass CourseWithContentsSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):\n    modules = ModuleWithContentsSerializer(many=True)\n\n    class Meta:\n        model = Course\n        fields = [\n            'id',\n            'subject',\n            'title',\n            'slug',\n            'overview',\n            'created',\n            'owner',\n            'modules',\n        ]\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ After That\n\nYour endpoint:\n\n```\nGET /api/courses/<pk>/contents/\n```\n\nShould return the course with all its modules and nested content.\n\nLet me know if you want a sample response structure for testing."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
