{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "installed django-embed-video and got:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The error:\n\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pkg_resources'\n```\n\n…occurs because the `django-embed-video` package tries to import `pkg_resources`, which is part of the `setuptools` package — and `setuptools` is **missing** from your environment.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Fix: Install `setuptools`\n\nRun this in your virtual environment:\n\n```bash\npip install setuptools\n```\n\nThen restart your Django server:\n\n```bash\npython manage.py runserver\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🧠 Why It Happens\n\nThe `embed_video` package uses `pkg_resources.get_distribution()` to fetch version info, which is provided by `setuptools`. Some lightweight Python environments (especially with Python 3.12+) may not include it by default.\n\n---\n\nLet me know if you also want help setting up the `EmbedVideoField` in your models or rendering videos in templates."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
