IGNATURE')\n    if sig_header is None:\n        return HttpResponseBadRequest(\"Missing Stripe signature header.\")\n\n    try:\n        event = stripe.Webhook.construct_event(\n            payload, sig_header, endpoint_secret='whsec_...')\n    except ValueError:\n        return HttpResponseBadRequest(\"Invalid payload\")\n    except stripe.error.SignatureVerificationError:\n        return HttpResponseBadRequest(\"Invalid signature\")\n\n    # Handle event\n    return HttpResponse(status=200)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Don’t Visit `/payment/webhook/` in Browser**\n\nStripe’s webhook view should be triggered **only by Stripe** sending POST requests with a valid signature.\n\nIf you're testing manually, use `curl` or Stripe CLI:\n\n```bash\nstripe listen --forward-to localhost:8000/payment/webhook/\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Optional: Add Logging**\n\nTo debug incoming requests:\n\n```python\nimport logging\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\nlogger.info(f\"Webhook received method={request.method}, headers={request.headers}\")\n```\n\n---\n\nLet me know if you want a full working example with test keys and event handling!"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
