s is harmless unless you’re clustering workers. You can ignore this for local dev.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Celery worker status:\n```\ncelery@mona ready.\n```\nThe worker is alive and ready to receive tasks.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ What Now?\n\nIf you want to verify it's working:\n\n1. Open a Python shell or Django shell:\n```bash\npython manage.py shell\n```\n\n2. Call your Celery task:\n```python\nfrom orders.tasks import order_created\norder_created.delay(order_id=123)\n```\n\nYou should see output in the worker console indicating the task is received and executed.\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Bonus: Simplified `celery.py` settings for Windows\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import absolute_import, unicode_literals\nimport os\nfrom celery import Celery\n\nos.environ.setdefault('DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE', 'myshop.settings')\n\napp = Celery('myshop')\napp.config_from_object('django.conf:settings', namespace='CELERY')\napp.autodiscover_tasks()\n\napp.conf.broker_connection_retry_on_startup = True\n```\n\n---\n\nLet me know if you want to:\n- Confirm task routing is working\n- Auto-start Celery with Django dev server\n- Use Redis for better local stability on Windows"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
