{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "regenerate the backgrounder to stdout"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Certainly! Here's the corrected **Media Backgrounder** for **Todd J. McCaffrey**, output directly below:\n\n---\n\n# **Media Backgrounder: Todd J. McCaffrey**\n\n## **Overview**\n\n**Todd J. McCaffrey** is a New York Times bestselling author, software engineer, and former U.S. Army NCO known for continuing *The Dragonriders of Pern* series created by his mother, the legendary Anne McCaffrey. With over **78 published books** across science fiction, fantasy, and thriller genres—under names including Todd McCaffrey, T.J. McCaffrey, Talla Hill, and T.C. Storm—Todd blends a deep technological background with a passion for world-building and storytelling.\n\nHe holds an **MFA in Fine Arts** from **Claremont Graduate University**, a **Bachelor of Science in Mechanical Engineering** from **Trinity College Dublin**, and has completed coursework at **Pierce College** and **Norco College**. Todd is also a **licensed pilot**, 3D artist, and veteran software engineer with 16 years of industry experience.\n\n---\n\n## **Notable Achievements**\n\n- Co-authored and expanded **The Dragonriders of Pern** legacy with seven official novels.\n- Published works spanning **science fiction, fantasy, steampunk, techno-thrillers, and urban fantasy**.\n- Recognized with **multiple literary awards**, including placement on the *New York Times* Bestseller List.\n- Honored guest and speaker at **DragonCon, WorldCon, Comic-Con International**, and other global conventions.\n\n---\n\n## **Recent Works**\n\n- **Raw Space** – Original space opera exploring isolation and connection.\n- **The Steam Crown** – A steampunk epic of invention and intrigue.\n- **L.A. Witch** series – Urban fantasy set in modern Los Angeles (as *Talla Hill*).\n- **Winter Wyvern** – A coming-of-age fantasy adventure for young adults.\n\n---\n\n## **Professional Background**\n\nBefore dedicating himself to writing, Todd worked for over 16 years in software engineering and project management, holding roles at **PLATINUM technology**, **Locus Computing Corporation**, and **Symas Corporation**. He contributed to high-level defense, enterprise, and educational systems, often leading multi-disciplinary development teams.\n\nHis technical expertise includes **Java, Python, C++, and C#**, along with tools like **Unity 3D**, **SolidWorks**, **Adobe Creative Suite**, and **Pro Tools**.\n\n---\n\n## **Media Highlights**\n\n- Featured in **Locus Magazine**, *Publishers Weekly*, *SFX*, and other genre press.\n- Interview subject for science fiction documentaries and podcasts.\n- Frequent guest and speaker on panels discussing:\n  - *Writing in Shared Universes*\n  - *Integrating Science into Storytelling*\n  - *The McCaffrey Legacy: Worldbuilding Across Generations*\n\n---\n\n## **Contact**\n\n**Email**: todd@toddwriter.com  \n**Website**: [http://toddmccaffrey.com](http://toddmccaffrey.com)  \n**Phone**: (818) 324-5127  \n**Location**: Las Vegas, NV (Available for travel and virtual appearances)\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to package this for a press kit or format it for a one-sheet or website section?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
