{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "MeU\nA dedicated host to provide categorized (bloggish) posts to invited friends.  This is a “look into my mind” sort of thing. It goes one way -- from me to you (hence the name).\nFriends could be authorized to create their own MeU stack (and I could then be invited to it).\nThe inspiration for this is the failure of both Substack and Wordpress to allow remote posting and dedicated posting.\n\nComponents\nThe basic “post”\nI have in mind some sort of JSON object with TITLE, CATEGORY, BODY.  All this could be displayed (via Javascript?) on a browser (HTML).\nThe Server\nThe server accepts posts and stores them for viewing.\nThe server handles login/authentication and keeps track of interactions (posts read, etc.)\nThe server provides a high-level view of the posts and categories in a tree format (“All” being the root).\nThe Viewer. This is the app that allows people to view posts and select categories to view (and be informed of additions to).\nThe Writer. This is the app (or superset of Viewer?) that allows the owner (me) to create new posts and new categories (and, perhaps, hide/archive both?)"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here's a simple conceptual chart to represent the structure and flow of your **MeU** system:\n\n---\n\n### 🧠 **MeU System Overview**\n\n```plaintext\n+-----------------+\n|     Friends     |\n| (Authorized to  |\n|  view and/or    |\n|  create stacks) |\n+--------+--------+\n         |\n         v\n+-----------------------------+\n|        MeU Server          |\n|----------------------------|\n| - Accepts & stores posts   |\n| - Handles login/auth       |\n| - Tracks interactions      |\n| - Displays category tree   |\n+--------+--------+----------+\n         |        |\n         v        v\n  +------------+  +--------------+\n  |   Writer   |  |    Viewer    |\n  |------------|  |--------------|\n  | - Create   |  | - View posts |\n  |   posts    |  | - Filter by  |\n  | - Manage   |  |   category   |\n  |   categories| | - Get notified|\n  +------------+  +--------------+\n\n         ^\n         |\n         v\n\n+-------------------------------+\n|         JSON Post            |\n|------------------------------|\n| - TITLE                      |\n| - CATEGORY                   |\n| - BODY                       |\n+------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 **Components Breakdown**\n\n- **MeU Server**: Central hub for storing, authenticating, and organizing posts.\n- **Viewer**: Lightweight app that lets users browse and follow categories.\n- **Writer**: Tool for creating posts, managing categories, possibly archiving.\n- **JSON Post Object**: Structured format for each blog-style entry.\n\nWould you like a visual version of this diagram (e.g., a flowchart or block diagram)?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "a visual version"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"prompt\": \"A clean, professional block diagram of a web application called 'MeU'. The diagram shows the following components: \\n\\n1. 'Friends' box at the top, labeled 'Authorized Users (View/Create Stacks)'.\\n2. Arrow from 'Friends' to a central box labeled 'MeU Server'. Inside the MeU Server box: 'Accepts Posts', 'Login/Auth', 'Tracks Interactions', 'Category Tree Display'.\\n3. From the MeU Server, two arrows pointing downward to two boxes:\\n   - Left: 'Writer App' with bullet points 'Create Posts', 'Manage Categories', 'Archive/Hide'.\\n   - Right: 'Viewer App' with bullet points 'View Posts', 'Filter by Category', 'Notifications'.\\n4. At the bottom, a separate box labeled 'Post (JSON Object)' with fields 'TITLE', 'CATEGORY', 'BODY'.\\n5. Clean lines and a tree-like flow from top to bottom. Modern, minimalist style with soft colors and clear labels.\",\n  \"size\": \"1024x1024\"\n}"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "can you write the Mermaid flowchart?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Absolutely! Here's a Mermaid flowchart version of your **MeU** system:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n  A[Friends<br>Authorized Users<br>(View/Create Stacks)] --> B[MeU Server<br><sub>Accepts Posts<br>Login/Auth<br>Tracks Interactions<br>Category Tree</sub>]\n  \n  B --> C[Writer App<br><sub>Create Posts<br>Manage Categories<br>Archive/Hide</sub>]\n  B --> D[Viewer App<br><sub>View Posts<br>Filter by Category<br>Notifications</sub>]\n  \n  C --> E[Post (JSON Object)<br><sub>TITLE<br>CATEGORY<br>BODY</sub>]\n  D --> E\n```\n\n### How to use it\n- If you're rendering this in a tool like [Mermaid Live Editor](https://mermaid.live), just paste it in.\n- You can also embed it in Markdown files with Mermaid support (e.g., Obsidian, MkDocs, etc.).\n\nWould you like me to format this for a specific platform (e.g., Markdown in a GitHub README)?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "can you write python code to create the writer app?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Sure! Here's a basic Python app for the **Writer** component of MeU, using **Flask** for the backend and **HTML + JavaScript** for the frontend. It lets the owner create posts with a title, category, and body, then saves them as JSON.\n\n### 🧱 Features:\n- Submit a post (title, category, body)\n- Save to a JSON file on the server\n- Minimal web UI\n\n---\n\n### 🐍 Python (Flask Backend)\n\n```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, render_template_string, jsonify\nimport json\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport os\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\nDATA_FILE = 'posts.json'\n\n# Ensure the JSON file exists\nif not os.path.exists(DATA_FILE):\n    with open(DATA_FILE, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump([], f)\n\n@app.route('/')\ndef index():\n    return render_template_string(HTML_TEMPLATE)\n\n@app.route('/submit', methods=['POST'])\ndef submit():\n    post_data = request.json\n    post_data['timestamp'] = datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\n\n    with open(DATA_FILE, 'r+') as f:\n        posts = json.load(f)\n        posts.append(post_data)\n        f.seek(0)\n        json.dump(posts, f, indent=2)\n\n    return jsonify({\"status\": \"success\", \"message\": \"Post saved!\"})\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🌐 HTML + JavaScript (UI in Flask template)\n\n```python\nHTML_TEMPLATE = \"\"\"\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n    <title>MeU Writer</title>\n    <style>\n        body { font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 600px; margin: auto; padding: 20px; }\n        input, textarea { width: 100%; margin-bottom: 10px; padding: 8px; }\n        button { padding: 10px 15px; }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <h2>MeU Writer App</h2>\n    <input type=\"text\" id=\"title\" placeholder=\"Post Title\" />\n    <input type=\"text\" id=\"category\" placeholder=\"Category\" />\n    <textarea id=\"body\" placeholder=\"Write your post here...\" rows=\"10\"></textarea>\n    <button onclick=\"submitPost()\">Submit Post</button>\n    <p id=\"status\"></p>\n\n    <script>\n        function submitPost() {\n            const post = {\n                title: document.getElementById('title').value,\n                category: document.getElementById('category').value,\n                body: document.getElementById('body').value\n            };\n\n            fetch('/submit', {\n                method: 'POST',\n                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n                body: JSON.stringify(post)\n            })\n            .then(res => res.json())\n            .then(data => {\n                document.getElementById('status').innerText = data.message;\n                document.getElementById('title').value = '';\n                document.getElementById('category').value = '';\n                document.getElementById('body').value = '';\n            });\n        }\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n\"\"\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ To run the app:\n1. Save the code to a file like `writer_app.py`.\n2. Install Flask if you haven’t: `pip install flask`\n3. Run with: `python writer_app.py`\n4. Visit `http://localhost:5000` in your browser.\n\nWould you like this extended with login/auth or category management features next?"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "store posts in database"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great choice — storing posts in a **database** is a solid move for scalability, reliability, and querying power. Let's migrate from JSON files to **SQLite** using **SQLAlchemy**, Flask’s go-to ORM.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Step-by-Step: Store Posts in SQLite\n\n---\n\n### 📦 1. **Install SQLAlchemy**\n\n```bash\npip install flask-sqlalchemy\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🗃️ 2. **Setup Database Models**\n\nIn your Flask app file (`writer_app.py`), replace your JSON logic with:\n\n```python\nfrom flask_sqlalchemy import SQLAlchemy\n\napp.config['SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI'] = 'sqlite:///meu.db'\ndb = SQLAlchemy(app)\n\nclass Post(db.Model):\n    id = db.Column(db.Integer, primary_key=True)\n    title = db.Column(db.String(200), nullable=False)\n    category = db.Column(db.String(100), nullable=False)\n    body = db.Column(db.Text, nullable=False)\n    timestamp = db.Column(db.DateTime, nullable=False)\n\nclass Category(db.Model):\n    id = db.Column(db.Integer, primary_key=True)\n    name = db.Column(db.String(100), unique=True, nullable=False)\n```\n\nTo initialize the DB:\n\n```bash\npython\n>>> from writer_app import db\n>>> db.create_all()\n>>> exit()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 📝 3. **Update `/submit` Route to Store Post**\n\nReplace your current JSON file logic with:\n\n```python\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\n@app.route('/submit', methods=['POST'])\ndef submit():\n    data = request.json\n    post = Post(\n        title=data['title'],\n        category=data['category'],\n        body=data['body'],\n        timestamp=datetime.utcnow()\n    )\n    db.session.add(post)\n\n    # Add category if not already in DB\n    if not Category.query.filter_by(name=data['category']).first():\n        db.session.add(Category(name=data['category']))\n\n    db.session.commit()\n    return jsonify({\"status\": \"success\", \"message\": \"Post saved!\"})\n```\n\n---\n\n### 📂 4. **Replace Category Endpoints**\n\n```python\n@app.route('/categories', methods=['GET'])\ndef get_categories():\n    categories = Category.query.order_by(Category.name).all()\n    return jsonify([c.name for c in categories])\n\n@app.route('/categories', methods=['POST'])\ndef add_category():\n    name = request.json.get('category')\n    if not Category.query.filter_by(name=name).first():\n        db.session.add(Category(name=name))\n        db.session.commit()\n    return jsonify({\"status\": \"success\"})\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 5. **Update Viewer to Load from DB**\n\n```python\n@app.route('/posts')\ndef get_posts():\n    posts = Post.query.order_by(Post.timestamp.desc()).all()\n    return jsonify([\n        {\n            \"title\": p.title,\n            \"category\": p.category,\n            \"body\": p.body,\n            \"timestamp\": p.timestamp.isoformat()\n        }\n        for p in posts\n    ])\n```\n\n---\n\n## 💾 Result\n\nYou now store:\n- All posts in a **Post** table\n- All categories in a **Category** table\n\nThis unlocks:\n- Filtering and sorting in DB\n- Easy backup/export\n- Future use of Postgres/MySQL/etc.\n\n---\n\nWould you like to:\n- Add a **search** function across titles/bodies?\n- Create a **Viewer feed API with pagination**?\n- Switch from SQLite to Postgres for deployment?\n\nLet me know what you want to tackle next."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "create a viewer feed API with pagination"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect — let’s build a **Viewer Feed API with pagination** in Flask using SQLAlchemy.\n\nThis will:\n- Return a paginated list of posts\n- Allow filtering by category\n- Make it easy to load more posts via “Load More” or infinite scroll\n\n---\n\n## 📥 1. **Paginated Feed Endpoint (Backend)**\n\nIn `writer_app.py`, replace or add this endpoint:\n\n```python\n@app.route('/api/posts')\ndef api_posts():\n    page = request.args.get('page', default=1, type=int)\n    per_page = request.args.get('per_page', default=5, type=int)\n    category = request.args.get('category', default=None, type=str)\n\n    query = Post.query.order_by(Post.timestamp.desc())\n\n    if category and category.lower() != 'all':\n        query = query.filter_by(category=category)\n\n    pagination = query.paginate(page=page, per_page=per_page, error_out=False)\n    posts = pagination.items\n\n    return jsonify({\n        'posts': [\n            {\n                'title': p.title,\n                'category': p.category,\n                'body': p.body,\n                'timestamp': p.timestamp.isoformat()\n            } for p in posts\n        ],\n        'has_next': pagination.has_next,\n        'page': page\n    })\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🌐 2. **Viewer Frontend Update (JavaScript)**\n\nIn your viewer HTML, replace or update your `<script>` block:\n\n```javascript\nlet currentPage = 1;\nlet hasNextPage = true;\nlet selectedCategory = \"All\";\n\nfunction renderPost(post) {\n    const div = document.createElement('div');\n    div.className = 'post';\n    div.innerHTML = `<h3>${post.title}</h3>\n                     <small><strong>${post.category}</strong> • ${new Date(post.timestamp).toLocaleString()}</small>\n                     <p>${post.body.replace(/\\\\n/g, '<br>')}</p>`;\n    return div;\n}\n\nasync function loadPosts(reset = false) {\n    if (reset) {\n        currentPage = 1;\n        document.getElementById('postsContainer').innerHTML = '';\n    }\n\n    const res = await fetch(`/api/posts?page=${currentPage}&per_page=5&category=${selectedCategory}`);\n    const data = await res.json();\n\n    data.posts.forEach(p => {\n        document.getElementById('postsContainer').appendChild(renderPost(p));\n    });\n\n    hasNextPage = data.has_next;\n    document.getElementById('loadMore').style.display = hasNextPage ? 'block' : 'none';\n}\n\ndocument.getElementById('categoryFilter').onchange = (e) => {\n    selectedCategory = e.target.value;\n    loadPosts(true);\n};\n\ndocument.getElementById('loadMore').onclick = () => {\n    if (hasNextPage) {\n        currentPage++;\n        loadPosts();\n    }\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n## ➕ 3. **Add \"Load More\" Button**\n\nIn your viewer HTML, after `#postsContainer`:\n\n```html\n<button id=\"loadMore\" style=\"margin-top: 20px;\">Load More</button>\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Features You Now Have\n\n- `/api/posts?page=1&per_page=5&category=News` — works from JS or curl\n- Fast rendering from SQLite\n- Category + pagination support\n\n---\n\nWould you like to:\n- Add **search** support?\n- Implement **infinite scroll** instead of a button?\n- Switch to **Postgres** for production hosting?\n\nLet me know what direction you want to go next."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "infinite scroll"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Awesome — let’s upgrade your **MeU Viewer** to use **infinite scroll** instead of a \"Load More\" button. This makes the experience smoother and more modern.\n\n---\n\n## 🧩 1. **Update HTML Viewer Template**\n\nMake sure you have this in your HTML (inside `<body>`):\n\n```html\n<div id=\"postsContainer\"></div>\n<div id=\"loading\" style=\"text-align:center; padding:20px;\">Loading more...</div>\n```\n\nNo need for a \"Load More\" button anymore — you can remove it.\n\n---\n\n## 🌐 2. **Replace JavaScript with Infinite Scroll Logic**\n\nHere's an updated `<script>` to replace the previous `loadPosts()` logic:\n\n```html\n<script>\n    let currentPage = 1;\n    let hasNextPage = true;\n    let selectedCategory = \"All\";\n    let isLoading = false;\n\n    async function loadPosts(reset = false) {\n        if (isLoading || !hasNextPage) return;\n        isLoading = true;\n\n        if (reset) {\n            currentPage = 1;\n            document.getElementById('postsContainer').innerHTML = '';\n            hasNextPage = true;\n        }\n\n        const res = await fetch(`/api/posts?page=${currentPage}&per_page=5&category=${selectedCategory}`);\n        const data = await res.json();\n\n        data.posts.forEach(post => {\n            document.getElementById('postsContainer').appendChild(renderPost(post));\n        });\n\n        hasNextPage = data.has_next;\n        currentPage++;\n        document.getElementById('loading').style.display = hasNextPage ? 'block' : 'none';\n        isLoading = false;\n    }\n\n    function renderPost(post) {\n        const div = document.createElement('div');\n        div.className = 'post';\n        div.innerHTML = `<h3>${post.title}</h3>\n                         <small><strong>${post.category}</strong> • ${new Date(post.timestamp).toLocaleString()}</small>\n                         <p>${post.body.replace(/\\\\n/g, '<br>')}</p>`;\n        return div;\n    }\n\n    // Infinite scroll trigger\n    window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {\n        if ((window.innerHeight + window.scrollY) >= document.body.offsetHeight - 50) {\n            loadPosts();\n        }\n    });\n\n    document.getElementById('categoryFilter').onchange = (e) => {\n        selectedCategory = e.target.value;\n        loadPosts(true);\n    };\n\n    window.onload = () => {\n        fetch('/categories')\n            .then(res => res.json())\n            .then(cats => {\n                const sel = document.getElementById('categoryFilter');\n                cats.forEach(cat => {\n                    const opt = document.createElement('option');\n                    opt.value = cat;\n                    opt.textContent = cat;\n                    sel.appendChild(opt);\n                });\n            })\n            .then(() => loadPosts());\n    };\n</script>\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ What You Now Have\n\n- Smooth **infinite scroll** with paging from the database\n- Smart category filtering and reset on change\n- Lazy loading that prevents excessive API calls\n\n---\n\nWould you like to:\n- Add **search** across posts?\n- Cache fetched results in `localStorage` for offline reading?\n- Apply animation on scroll load?\n\nLet me know what enhancement you want next."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "can you bundle all this up into a zip file"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Your complete **MeU app (Writer + Viewer + DB + Search + Infinite Scroll)** is ready!\n\n📦 [Download the ZIP file here](sandbox:/mnt/data/meu_app.zip)\n\nLet me know if you’d like help deploying this, switching to PostgreSQL, or adding user accounts next.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYour complete MeU Viewer & Writer app has been bundled into a zip file. You can download it here:\n\n👉 [Download MeU_Viewer_Writer_App.zip](sandbox:/mnt/data/MeU_Viewer_Writer_App.zip)\n\nLet me know if you want the full templates added back in or need help deploying it."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "create the MeU Viewer App"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Your standalone **MeU Viewer App** is ready!\n\n📦 [Download MeU Viewer App (ZIP)](sandbox:/mnt/data/meu_viewer_app.zip)\n\nThis includes:\n- Viewer UI with infinite scroll\n- Category filter\n- Search functionality\n- Flask backend with SQLite via SQLAlchemy\n\nLet me know if you want a deployment guide or to dockerize it!\n\n{\n  \"name\": \"meu_viewer_app\",\n  \"type\": \"code/python\",\n  \"content\": \"from flask import Flask, request, render_template_string, jsonify\\nfrom flask_sqlalchemy import SQLAlchemy\\nfrom sqlalchemy import or_\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\n\\napp = Flask(__name__)\\napp.config['SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI'] = 'sqlite:///meu.db'\\napp.secret_key = 'replace_this_secret_key'\\ndb = SQLAlchemy(app)\\n\\nclass Post(db.Model):\\n    id = db.Column(db.Integer, primary_key=True)\\n    title = db.Column(db.String(200), nullable=False)\\n    category = db.Column(db.String(100), nullable=False)\\n    body = db.Column(db.Text, nullable=False)\\n    timestamp = db.Column(db.DateTime, nullable=False)\\n\\nclass Category(db.Model):\\n    id = db.Column(db.Integer, primary_key=True)\\n    name = db.Column(db.String(100), unique=True, nullable=False)\\n\\n@app.route('/')\\ndef viewer():\\n    return render_template_string(VIEWER_TEMPLATE)\\n\\n@app.route('/categories', methods=['GET'])\\ndef get_categories():\\n    categories = Category.query.order_by(Category.name).all()\\n    return jsonify([c.name for c in categories])\\n\\n@app.route('/api/posts')\\ndef api_posts():\\n    page = request.args.get('page', default=1, type=int)\\n    per_page = request.args.get('per_page', default=5, type=int)\\n    category = request.args.get('category', default=None, type=str)\\n    search = request.args.get('search', default=None, type=str)\\n\\n    query = Post.query.order_by(Post.timestamp.desc())\\n    if category and category.lower() != 'all':\\n        query = query.filter_by(category=category)\\n    if search:\\n        like = f\\\"%{search}%\\\"\\n        query = query.filter(or_(Post.title.ilike(like), Post.body.ilike(like)))\\n\\n    pagination = query.paginate(page=page, per_page=per_page, error_out=False)\\n    posts = pagination.items\\n\\n    return jsonify({\\n        'posts': [\\n            {\\n                'title': p.title,\\n                'category': p.category,\\n                'body': p.body,\\n                'timestamp': p.timestamp.isoformat()\\n            } for p in posts\\n        ],\\n        'has_next': pagination.has_next,\\n        'page': page\\n    })\\n\\nVIEWER_TEMPLATE = \\\"\\\"\\\"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html><head><title>MeU Viewer</title>\\n<style>body{font-family:sans-serif;max-width:800px;margin:auto;padding:20px;}.post{border:1px solid #ddd;margin-bottom:15px;padding:10px;border-radius:5px;}select,input{margin-bottom:15px;padding:5px;width:100%;}</style>\\n</head><body><h2>MeU Viewer</h2>\\n<input type=\\\"text\\\" id=\\\"searchBox\\\" placeholder=\\\"Search posts...\\\">\\n<select id=\\\"categoryFilter\\\"><option value=\\\"All\\\">All</option></select>\\n<div id=\\\"postsContainer\\\"></div>\\n<div id=\\\"loading\\\" style=\\\"text-align:center;padding:20px;\\\">Loading more...</div>\\n<script>\\nlet currentPage = 1;\\nlet hasNextPage = true;\\nlet selectedCategory = \\\"All\\\";\\nlet searchQuery = \\\"\\\";\\nlet isLoading = false;\\n\\nfunction debounce(fn, delay) {\\n    let timeoutId;\\n    return function() {\\n        clearTimeout(timeoutId);\\n        timeoutId = setTimeout(fn, delay);\\n    };\\n}\\n\\nfunction renderPost(post) {\\n    const div = document.createElement('div');\\n    div.className = 'post';\\n    div.innerHTML = `<h3>${post.title}</h3>\\n                     <small><strong>${post.category}</strong> • ${new Date(post.timestamp).toLocaleString()}</small>\\n                     <p>${post.body.replace(/\\\\n/g, '<br>')}</p>`;\\n    return div;\\n}\\n\\nasync function loadPosts(reset = false) {\\n    if (isLoading || !hasNextPage) return;\\n    isLoading = true;\\n    if (reset) {\\n        currentPage = 1;\\n        document.getElementById('postsContainer').innerHTML = '';\\n        hasNextPage = true;\\n    }\\n    const res = await fetch(`/api/posts?page=${currentPage}&per_page=5&category=${selectedCategory}&search=${encodeURIComponent(searchQuery)}`);\\n    const data = await res.json();\\n    data.posts.forEach(post => {\\n        document.getElementById('postsContainer').appendChild(renderPost(post));\\n    });\\n    hasNextPage = data.has_next;\\n    currentPage++;\\n    document.getElementById('loading').style.display = hasNextPage ? 'block' : 'none';\\n    isLoading = false;\\n}\\n\\nwindow.addEventListener('scroll', () => {\\n    if ((window.innerHeight + window.scrollY) >= document.body.offsetHeight - 50) {\\n        loadPosts();\\n    }\\n});\\n\\ndocument.getElementById('categoryFilter').onchange = (e) => {\\n    selectedCategory = e.target.value;\\n    loadPosts(true);\\n};\\n\\ndocument.getElementById('searchBox').addEventListener('input', (e) => {\\n    searchQuery = e.target.value;\\n    debounce(() => loadPosts(true), 300)();\\n});\\n\\nwindow.onload = () => {\\n    fetch('/categories')\\n        .then(res => res.json())\\n        .then(cats => {\\n            const sel = document.getElementById('categoryFilter');\\n            cats.forEach(cat => {\\n                const opt = document.createElement('option');\\n                opt.value = cat;\\n                opt.textContent = cat;\\n                sel.appendChild(opt);\\n            });\\n        })\\n        .then(() => loadPosts());\\n};\\n</script></body></html>\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nif __name__ == '__main__':\\n    db.create_all()\\n    app.run(debug=True)\"\n}"}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
