{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "please ensure that all ASINs are current and reproduce the list"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "To ensure all ASINs are accurate and up-to-date, I recommend directly using Amazon’s advanced search with keywords and filters. You can search for titles similar to *\"Ghost Shot\"* by Talla Hill and verify ASINs listed on individual book pages.\n\nYou can search Amazon with terms like \"supernatural mystery,\" \"paranormal romance,\" or authors such as Erin Sterling, Leigh Bardugo, or Tracy Wolff to cross-reference titles like *The Ex Hex*, *Legendborn*, or *Ninth House*. This will ensure accuracy in obtaining ASINs."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "use amazon's advanced search with keywords and filters to ensure that your ASINs are up to date"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Amazon's advanced search is only accessible directly through their platform. To validate ASINs, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Go to Amazon's website**: Visit [amazon.com](https://www.amazon.com).\n2. **Use the search bar**: Enter book titles or keywords like \"paranormal romance,\" \"supernatural mystery,\" or \"similar to Ghost Shot.\"\n3. **Filter by genre or category**: On the left sidebar, select relevant filters like Books > Fiction > Paranormal Romance.\n4. **Locate ASINs**: Once on a book's product page, scroll down to the \"Product details\" section where the ASIN is listed, or find it in the product URL.\n\nThis manual method will ensure the ASINs are accurate and up-to-date. Alternatively, I can help guide you through any specific book search."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
{"system": "", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "I am creating a targeted list for AMS (amazon) ads of books I want my ad to appear (on their product page) for my book, Raw Space (ASIN: B09G6HNPS4). What other books on Amazon.com can I also add (title, series name, author)"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "To curate a list of books for AMS (Amazon) ads that can target the product pages relevant to your book *Raw Space* (ASIN: B09G6HNPS4), consider these strategies:  \n\n### **Recommended Similar Titles for AMS Targeting:**\n1. **Science Fiction Adventure / Space Opera Titles:**\n   - *Leviathan Wakes* (The Expanse) by James S.A. Corey  \n   - *Dune* by Frank Herbert  \n   - *Ender’s Game* by Orson Scott Card  \n   - *The Long Way to a Small, Angry Planet* by Becky Chambers  \n   - *Red Mars* by Kim Stanley Robinson  \n\n2. **Galactic Empire / Military Sci-Fi Books:**\n   - *Old Man's War* by John Scalzi  \n   - *The Lost Fleet* series by Jack Campbell  \n   - *Honor Among Enemies* (Honor Harrington) by David Weber  \n   - *Children of Time* by Adrian Tchaikovsky  \n   - *To Sleep in a Sea of Stars* by Christopher Paolini  \n\n3. **Books Mixing Mystery and Sci-Fi:**\n   - *Altered Carbon* by Richard K. Morgan  \n   - *The Dispossessed* by Ursula K. Le Guin  \n   - *A Memory Called Empire* by Arkady Martine  \n\n### **How to Identify ASINs for Targeting:**\n1. Visit the product pages of the suggested books on [Amazon](https://www.amazon.com).\n2. Scroll to the \"Product details\" section to find the ASINs or check the URLs for the ASIN embedded there.\n3. Search for related series and check the “Customers who bought this item also bought” section to find additional ideas.\n\nThese books fit well within the genres of space opera, galactic exploration, and science fiction adventure, making them ideal for AMS ad targeting alongside *Raw Space*."}], "tags": ["chatgpt", "v1"]}
